or receipt verified. Search nonlocation not lost/destroyed; reused aid not new source review or independent corroboration.\n\n**Independence:**\n\nCatalogue and finding aid may derive from the same archival inventory. Same date/topic not a document identity join. No new historical witness or source independence claim.\n\n**Missing records:**\n\n[unpublished research reference]\n\n**Smallest discriminating step:**\n\nActual item/withdrawal identifiers, available review/release crossreferences, original May29/June26 papers and July22 answer/enclosure dispatch/receipt.\n\n**Evidence grade:**\n\nDirect metadata observation/held text pins only, not underlying report truth, execution, payment purpose or historical test completion.\n\n**Original acceptance changed:**\n\n```json\nfalse\n```\n\n**Disclosure status:**\n\nLocal/unpublished; sending/approval TODOs unchanged.\n\n**Citations:** [Supplied sources and provenance limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a86abe794e7f959e1fde).\n\n<a id=\"nr157\"></a>\n### NR157 — Workplan question/scope crosswalk rejects count-only abandonment while preserving specific oversight/program gaps\n\n**Claim type:**\n\nHeld source-content comparison/manual semantic mappings and hypothetical scope examples, not new source acquisition\n\n**Assessment links:**\n\n```json\n[\n  \"AUD003\",\n  \"AUD004\",\n  \"AUD013\",\n  \"AUD016\"\n]\n```\n\n**Source pins:**\n\n[unpublished research reference]\n\n**Exact locators:**\n\n[unpublished research reference]\n\n**Supporting evidence:**\n\nAll11broader questions mapped:2close/1reframed/2related/6noexplicitcompactcounterpart; separate8entrysheet andtwoSaudi4questionvariants. Political/economicinfluence questions remain explicit; assistance/foreknowledge distinct. Sixhypothetical record types expose date/admin/masked scope differences.\n\n**Contrary evidence and limits:**\n\nActualcompact oversight/program/opposition gaps andeditorcomment retained; no all-retained or executed-scope finding. Extraquestion sheets/req