** `steel-nysa-flatbed-photo-2026-11-03` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1cf7e1355bd872c2fc02).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 11d35c231f66ce7c18cd44b00125cac10b7d21470bccba30a4738af6c25a518f -->\n# Archival photograph: steel prepared for transport to the State Museum\n\n**November 3, 2026.** A specific New York State Archives photograph and its catalog record provide a new input to the steel-preservation search. The archive dates it **June 2002**, attributes the image to **Mark Schaming**, and captions the load as **North Tower steel ready to move to the New York State Museum**. The preserved, actually viewed image shows a large folded metal assembly resting on a flatbed trailer. Shipment, receipt, original floor and accession identity remain unverified.\n\nThis is partial operational-record progress within **STL01–STL03, AUD011/AUD016 and B188/H005**. It does not complete the steel provenance chain or any of the original eighteen acquisition/testing criteria. The FAA correction/disposition originals, Beverly Hills certification and approved attachments, and the other tracks' outstanding native inputs remain TODOs.\n\n## The acquired record and its source references\n\n| Field | Value read from the archival record | Exact saved browser-DOM locator |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [Item page](https://digitalcollections.archives.nysed.gov/Detail/objects/45414) title | WTC steel (North Tower) on flatbed ready to move to NYSM | `north-flatbed-page-dom.txt`, line 39; caption line 54 |\n| Archival image identifier | **NYSA_22533-13_14_2** | Line 56 |\n| Date Original | **June 2002** | Lines 57–58 |\n| Photographer | **Schaming, Mark** | Line 60 |\n| Source location | **Series 22533-13, Album p.79, top; negative sheet 14, #2** | Line 62 |\n| [Collection record](https://digitalcollections.archives.nysed.gov/Detail/collections/6049) | World Trade Center collection and exhibit files; **series 22533** | `series22533-page-dom.txt`, lines 39–49 |\n\nThe collection description attributes its Fresh Kills photographs to a New York State Museum curator and describes debris sorting, structural elements and possible collection additions. Its page displays **170 related objects** at line 51. That is a catalog-interface count, not a count of steel specimens, independent witnesses, retained physical pieces or photographs inspected in this review. The collection's database ID **6049**, item database ID **45414**, archival series **22533** and full image identifier occupy different identifier systems.\n\nThe album and negative references are unusually useful retrieval coordinates. The underlying album page, negative sheet, original captioning/identification worksheet and camera original were **not acquired**. Their contents and relationship to later accession records remain to be checked. The catalog date and tower attribution are institutional assertions; they were not independently authenticated from a negative, original field notes or identifiable building marks.\n\n## What was actually visible\n\nThe acquired display rendition is a **700×457 JPEG**. It shows a folded structural-looking metal assembly on a flatbed. No reliable specimen number, accession label, original member marking or floor identification was read. No scale measurement, alloy identification, temperature estimate or damage-mechanism analysis was performed. Apparent shape alone does not establish tower/floor provenance, when deformation occurred or which later exhibit contains the piece.\n\nThe caption establishes that the archive describes the scene as preparation for museum transport. It does not itself establish departure, completed delivery, title transfer, museum accession or present availability. A dispatch/receipt/loan/intake crosswalk would test those later events. A museum destination in a caption also does not establish that the object was a NIST scientific sample or was available for the specific tests previously discussed.\n\nThe strongest objection to treating this as a recovered custody chain is the missing item-level join: a photograph with an attributed destination is not a signed transfer or receipt. Conversely, the image is pertinent contrary evidence to a blanket claim that no structural material was retained for potential preservation. It does not answer whether the scientific candidates were adequately preserved or representative.\n\n## Preserve the earlier descriptions without joining them\n\n| Source | Preserved fields | Relationship to the archived load |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [Museum phase-two release](https://nysm.nysed.gov/about/press/phase-2-world-trade-center-exhibition-opens-feb-1-nys-museum), previously captured | **North / floors 71-74 / Recovery / 20-foot / 10-ton** | Unknown; no accession or marking crosswalk. |\n| [Museum exhibition page](https://nysm.nysed.gov/exhibitions/ongoing/world-trade-center-rescue-recovery-response), previously captured | **South / floors 7–9 / Rescue** | Unknown; different described exhibition section. |\n| [Photographer caption](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wallyg/55558340145/), preserved in the preceding review | **North / floors 104–107 / original 36-foot, 20-ton assembly** | Unverified third-party description; its photographed labels remained unreadable. |\n| State Archives item **NYSA_22533-13_14_2**, acquired here | **North / June 2002 / ready to move to NYSM** | No floor or accession supplied by the read fields; actual arrival unverified. |\n\nNo preferred account was selected. Different objects/displays, a loan or replacement, a changed attribution and descriptive/caption errors remain untested possibilities. Neither common object identity nor equivalent dimension/mass scope has been established. This is not a demonstrated same-specimen contradiction. The records also do not join this load to **I-0137, W14A/W14B, C12a/b, FEMA Sample 1, a NIST coupon or WTC 7**.\n\n## Preservation, access and actual reading scope\n\nThe collection and item page were actually read and preserved as browser-DOM snapshots. The exact display-image URL was observed in the public page, retrieved without credentials, preserved and visually inspected. A display-image hash identifies that downloaded rendition, not an original negative, original camera file, physical object or compressed network transmission.\n\n| Preserved representation | Acquisition/preservation UTC | Bytes | SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Collection page browser DOM | 2026-11-03T18:19:59.484591+00:00, saved-file timestamp | 12,530 | `f6d7b5f871cf349288be04f7fce91aad1ff07ba3c61cb1626fbd87f61ec6d9db` |\n| Item page browser DOM | 2026-11-03T18:21:23.674576+00:00, saved-file timestamp | 3,763 | `aa61e405a39ca8c9cf696e148d9cc82338cf8afb36ae55ab0909fd0e88383494` |\n| Displayed image entity | 2026-11-03T18:23:20.834059+00:00, request start | 38,262 | `8d195adc4128f467b1a111a950407450897b860f17f83def19191dc848ea2fb3` |\n\nOnly one specific photograph was examined. Partial collection-list metadata was read; the full set of 170 catalog entries and their image contents were not examined or classified. The offered original-download URL returned HTML rather than an image. Its response status/size/hash were recorded, but that failed response body was not saved; no original-image acquisition is claimed. The separately displayed JPEG was accessible and preserved. A collection-export request returned 403, the linked finding aid could not be obtained through the reader, and later index navigation reached a human-verification challenge. Those routes were stopped without bypass or repetition. These access observations do not establish deletion, concealment or altered historical records.\n\nThree indexed queries and one public-interface identifier search were performed. The latter exceeded a literal reading of the unit's initial three-query cap by one; that deviation is recorded, not presented as a passing limit. Subsequent navigation followed observed series-list and item links without more keyword queries or guessed record identifiers. The unrelated object numbered 22533 returned by the item search was not opened or adopted as the archival series. No outreach, fee, request, login, physical acquisition or experiment occurred.\n\nThe raw snapshots and photograph remain separate on the verified Intel store. The public derivative contains original notes, links and integrity/locator metadata, with no raw photograph, page reproduction, private case material, correspondence, personal/contact data or credentials. Earlier records remain unchanged. This acquisition does not authenticate the archive's full original-record chain or exhaust its holdings.\n\n## Next discriminating records\n\n**NYSM-07 — archival source chain:** Album p.79, top; negative sheet 14, #2; original caption/field-identification notes and accession metadata for **NYSA_22533-13_14_2**. Compare markings and physical details, preserving uncertain matches and contrary results.\n\n**NYSM-08 — transfer and museum join:** Dispatch/loading/transport documents, actual receipt, intake/accession record, condition photographs, installation/loan history and any later label/attribution versions. Establish separately whether the photographed load reached the museum and whether it corresponds to any earlier described column.\n\nThe linked [series finding aid](http://iarchives.nysed.gov/xtf/view?docId=ead/findingaids/22533.xml), remaining image review and any higher-quality source rendition remain TODOs. The State Museum visual inventory, earlier accession/attribution targets, NYHS-RG20 folders **220/8 and 218/24**, Beverly Hills certification/attachments and all original work-plan dependencies are carried forward without closure.\n\nThe [preceding published review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/9a89314d28d911789ff815d9f34fcdb787b690ff/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-exhibition-records-and-label-2026-11-03/README.md) and its native combined version are preserved. An exact additions-only [text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f16f1c08ef11397fb94e), [source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f791b1391ceab0c888e9), [observations](CITATIONS.md#nov04-57b0e4f033686679d87c), [provenance leads](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ff7cdcee7ded6d994aaa), [locators](CITATIONS.md#nov04-923b7c8188a72f534ac2), [reading scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-cd2e7459618e7f2e27ff), [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-bbdd582e50d8c02d284a), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5ac009ba5c1a25aa03fd), [verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3e25994d1842383d4ae7) and [bundle hashes](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9aea36ee097ae468144d) accompany this separately named review. Publication verification is not historical, physical or scientific validation.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 11d35c231f66ce7c18cd44b00125cac10b7d21470bccba30a4738af6c25a518f -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-6c41b20bd1137595\"></a>\n### New York State Museum: steel descriptions and an inventory lead\n\n**Source unit:** `steel-nysm-provenance-lead-2026-11-03` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-27e696fe23f1a7ce34b2).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 6c41b20bd11375952742bec5e4d0d4a029d239f210039541797f15cd16928e89 -->\n# New York State Museum: steel descriptions and an inventory lead\n\n**November 3, 2026.** Three newly read museum-authored pages identify a separate route to retained WTC building material and its documentation. A museum release carrying a **January 1, 2003** date field describes a column attributed to **North Tower floors 71–74**, while the exhibition page retrieved in this study describes one attributed to **South Tower floors 7–9**. Their exhibition contexts differ. The same-object relationship is unknown; these statements do not yet establish misidentification or a changed label.\n\nThe most actionable record lead is the 2003-dated release’s reference to a **visual inventory of the museum’s WTC collection**. The native inventory/export, object accession records and marking/transfer files could test the floor/tower attributions and the relationship between these descriptions. None was acquired here.\n\nExisting scope: **STL01–STL03, AUD011/AUD016, B188/H005 and SPT01–SPT08**. This unit does not reopen the deferred Beverly Hills certification/attachments, duplicate telephone or technical investigations, or complete the original steel-custody criteria.\n\n## What the museum sources actually say\n\n| Source and exact captured-text location | Recorded field or statement | Source role and limit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [2003-dated phase-two release](https://nysm.nysed.gov/about/press/phase-2-world-trade-center-exhibition-opens-feb-1-nys-museum), captured text line 18 | **north tower; floors 71-74; 20-foot high; 10-ton** steel column. | This paragraph describes **Recovery**, within the announcement of phase two. Museum attribution and reported dimensions/mass were not independently measured. The unit underlying “ton” is unspecified; no conversion was made. |\n| Same release, captured text lines 34–35 | **Release Date: Wednesday, January 1, 2003**. | The date is a field on the live page captured in 2026. No original 2003 publication, posting history or native release file was authenticated. |\n| [Exhibition page](https://nysm.nysed.gov/exhibitions/ongoing/world-trade-center-rescue-recovery-response), **Rescue**, captured text lines 17–19 | **South Tower; floors 7–9** steel column. | This description appears under **Rescue**. It supplies no accession number in the read paragraph. Current physical presence, original recovery attribution and a same-object connection to the 2003 description were not verified. |\n| 2003-dated release, captured text line 20 | A museum computer presentation is described as including a visual inventory of the museum’s WTC collection. | This identifies a particular underlying inventory/data product to seek. The native dataset, images, item keys, coverage and version history remain unacquired. |\n| [Collection page](https://nysm.nysed.gov/research-collections/history/political-history/collections/911), captured text line 7 | The institution describes a WTC collection encompassing building materials and other objects. | Collection-level description; it does not identify either column, its accession, source markings or a NIST/FEMA specimen. Its comparative collection-size claim was not tested or adopted. |\n\nThe release also mentions an FBI recovery video alongside the inventory. That juxtaposition does **not** establish that the FBI authored the museum inventory, held custody of every listed item or provided the source for each attribution. The inventory and video have separate described roles. We did not acquire or play either.\n\n## Preserve the different accounts and their context\n\nRetain **North / 71-74 / Recovery / 2003-dated release** and **South / 7–9 / Rescue / exhibition page retrieved November 3, 2026** side by side. Both floor and tower fields were directly read in the captured page bodies. No preferred field was selected and no earlier source was edited.\n\nThe strongest objection to a mislabeling interpretation is the different exhibition context: **Recovery** and **Rescue** may describe separate objects or displays. Multiple columns, a replacement/loan, a changed attribution or a descriptive error are untested possibilities. The number and identities of distinct physical pieces cannot be inferred from these descriptions alone. The sources were not joined by accession number, marking, transfer event or authenticated object photograph.\n\nThese are **unjoined descriptive differences**, not an established contradiction about a single specimen. An accession/loan/exhibit-installation crosswalk and contemporaneous marking/identification records would distinguish the possibilities. A guide explicitly identifying both objects, if obtained, would also matter; its contents have not been adopted from a search snippet or a browser wrapper.\n\nMuseum descriptions of retained structural material weaken a blanket premise that no potentially relevant steel was preserved anywhere. They do not establish present availability for sampling, an intact custody chain, representative scientific sampling, a particular heating/damage mechanism or adequate preservation of the scientific candidates. No link to **W14A/W14B, C12a/b, FEMA Sample 1, I-0137**, a NIST retained coupon or WTC 7 was found in the read passages. No material composition, fracture or temperature analysis was performed.\n\n## Next records to seek\n\n1. **NYSM-01 — object identity and attribution:** the museum registrar/History collections’ accession and catalog records corresponding separately to the North 71–74 and South 7–9 descriptions. Obtain original markings/photos, identification worksheets, donor/source information and building/floor attribution basis. Treat a curator’s description separately from its underlying documentation.\n2. **NYSM-02 — inventory:** the visual-inventory application/data export referenced in the 2003-dated release, including its original item keys, captions, source-image associations, revision history, coverage and later catalog migration. Do not infer that every object was in the same database or transferred by the same agency.\n3. **NYSM-03 — physical and exhibition chain:** recovery/intake/donor/transfer/transport/condition records, loan and installation/removal records, and dated label versions. Test whether the descriptions concern separate pieces, changed displays or altered attributions; retain contrary results.\n4. **NYSM-04 — linked educational guide:** the actual complete guide at the [linked public URL](https://nysm.nysed.gov/sites/default/files/2024-10/wtc.guide_.pdf), with edition/page mapping before adopting its contents. It remains unacquired/unread as a PDF. A URL path containing “2024-10” does not authenticate its authorship or publication date.\n\nThese are public-record retrieval targets, not sent requests. No contact, fee, FOIL/FOIA submission, loan request, account login, specimen acquisition or test occurred. The institution is a new holder route; no assertion about its response to a request is possible.\n\n## Preservation and actual reading scope\n\nAll three declared article bodies were read in the normal HTTPS browser without a security-warning override, credentials or altered TLS protection. The web reader had returned gateway errors and the ordinary downloader failed its local certificate-chain check; neither yielded the requested source body. Those outcomes remain preserved separately. They are not evidence of historical suppression, deletion or source falsity.\n\nThe acquired representations are **browser-rendered article DOM captures and derived visible text**, with exact URL, capture UTC, byte count and SHA-256 for each. A DOM hash is not a native 2003 file hash, HTTP response-body hash or compressed wire-byte capture. Two representations of one article are not independent corroboration. Captured-text line references below refer to the saved derivative text, not original historical pagination.\n\n| Article | Capture UTC | DOM SHA-256 | Visible-text SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Phase-two release | 2026-11-03T17:28:05.739Z | `8f405b477fcc92f9eee414eacccddaba4c466f095505279216c8cf7c06a041b2` | `34548e695dc7c1d988964954863fc789a500b9e035469e7434a8c585f9bb330b` |\n| Exhibition | 2026-11-03T17:28:43.665Z | `3c5320eb644870d9e2f46a51650018a558b0666969c0104679405c8025a31736` | `98eb4ff1a9ed39f57a62e28fada7f86c15fcd2e180f946519c744a1adef932e1` |\n| Collection | 2026-11-03T17:29:36.608Z | `a4756cedb1ff8465c64fbfa0ff8863d1c4be0edc62bcf08dec692c776a02d700` | `f8e70ee00fde609aa6ad1716edd68378fca305efd8f3e9115ec4c7b1ce4c06cd` |\n\nOnly textual descriptions are used. Artifact/gallery images, videos, audio, native accession records and the actual guide were not examined. Four focused indexed queries and three article reads were completed; displayed search results did not provide an accession join. This is not an exhaustive museum-database search or a finding that records do not exist. The guide capture returned a browser wrapper rather than PDF bytes; no PDF/source-content finding is based on it. Local access/tool receipts remain separate from historical evidence.\n\nThe native captures stay preserved on the verified Intel store. The public derivative contains original research notes and source/hash locators, excluding raw DOM/text/images, contacts, personal exhibits, private case/correspondence/strategy, credentials and coordination. Earlier steel records and the immediately preceding combined review remain unchanged.\n\n[Source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-646e8576ea09f980f7cc), [observations](CITATIONS.md#nov04-50a3cea5c9d42f5740cc), [provenance leads](CITATIONS.md#nov04-78a23cf541949c3be291), [reading scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e8868640adc88a6dd810), [open TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-68d820b32e5ad045ef55), [locators](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8fd5362cbf97bb001222), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-223487688ea01d5c070b), [verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7ae9c72d35746756543f), [bundle hashes](CITATIONS.md#nov04-43053961770fc6962a73) and the additive [text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-05141117e69c2a3e4f8f) distinguish what was read, inferred, missing and preserved. All original eighteen criteria across the five tracks remain open/partial. Publication verification does not complete original-record acquisition or scientific validation.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 6c41b20bd11375952742bec5e4d0d4a029d239f210039541797f15cd16928e89 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-49ad307d9813f4aa\"></a>\n### SAVE markings in collected-steel footage: identifier and retention-record leads\n\n**Source unit:** `steel-save-marking-followup-2026-11-03` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c4fe2470d013873c7bb8).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 49ad307d9813f4aa294a170f96249ae4f81a3975950141ce0b0d0138e2fb2cba -->\n# SAVE markings in collected-steel footage: identifier and retention-record leads\n\nNovember 3, 2026. A bounded follow-up to SV03 supplies a **provisional visual reading of “M2” beside “SAVE”**, another visible “SAVE” on an end plate, and measuring-tape activity. A second marking remains partly unreadable. These are leads to identification and handling records, not proof of specimen identity, retention, loss or wrongdoing. Missing originals remain TODOs.\n\n## Source and unchanged earlier reading\n\nThe source is the already preserved public **[WTC Tape 3.mov](CITATIONS.md#nov04-805d2455556506e07870)**, reached through [NIST’s image/video navigation](https://www.nist.gov/world-trade-center-investigation/photos-videos-and-simulations) and its [linked collection](https://googledrive.nist.gov/folders/1mO5PPh1ZyZafGUtWrzqhiaDwzTqyEPG-). The October 27 acquisition and November 3 full-file hash check identify **468,978,020 bytes**, SHA-256 **`a74ade3e8cbdf0df5976b67c60ee0a211937440e90d4a29bc211cdfc13057dcd`**. The movie was not downloaded again. The public route and file hash do not authenticate an original camera tape, filming date or physical custody. [Source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0c5184ba34eadb9c98ce).\n\nThe [October 27 report](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/75347e9c38e09b5c2037ee9490e6c2c5acf0f799/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-candidate-originals-2026-10-27/README.md#sv03--a-directly-visible-preservation-related-marking), native report lines 27–31, recorded “SAVE” in zero-based input frame **3597**, reported presentation time **240.04004 seconds**, but did not confidently join the preceding identifier to an inventory entry. It expressly left an M/N alias unselected. That report, its native frames and its uncertainty remain unchanged. The new reading comes from additional angles in the same source; it is not an independent witness or an adjudication of the old prefix uncertainty.\n\n## What was actually read\n\nAll times below are the decoder’s **presentation timestamps**, not a camera clock, filming date or historical elapsed time. All locators refer to the hash above. [Exact frame metadata](CITATIONS.md#nov04-794ffa261bb2a7182c3a) and [observation locators](CITATIONS.md#nov04-954f4a681cf4b7cfd651) permit independent retrieval.\n\n| Observation | Native zero-based frame / presentation seconds | Accepted observation and unresolved portion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SAVE-O01 | **3630 / 242.242242**; supporting view 3660 / 244.244244 | A marking beside SAVE looks more like **M2** in this angle. This remains a provisional transcription. No source-written hyphen, full catalog designation or inventory match is accepted. The earlier M/N uncertainty remains in the record. |\n| SAVE-O02 | **4050 / 270.27027** and **4080 / 272.272272** | **SAVE** is readable on a near end plate. The sampling does not establish whether the two SAVE writings concern one object, separate objects, portions, or one repeated instruction. |\n| SAVE-O03 | 4050, 4080, **4170 / 278.278278**, **4230 / 282.282282** | A separate visible long member carries an **MS1/MSI-like token and an N-prefixed string**. The suffix remains unaccepted after the short adjacent-frame extension. No N11, N14, N17 or other complete identifier is assigned. |\n| SAVE-O04 | **3660 / 244.244244**, **3990 / 266.266266**, **4080 / 272.272272** | A measuring tape is held across or along visible material. No numerical dimension, calibrated endpoint, result, responsible person or date is identified. |\n\nThe M2 candidate was written down **before** the attempted inventory consultation. An inventory label must not be used to supply unreadable characters. Adjacency in a view does not establish that markings on different visible surfaces belong to the same physical specimen. [Observations](CITATIONS.md#nov04-49a43d2fdebf8bd1092b) · [unjoined provenance leads](CITATIONS.md#nov04-bfab50476139a5f12f27).\n\n## Meaning and competing interpretations\n\nThe useful lead is a possible route from a visible marking to an intake, marking, measurement or retention record. A SAVE marking could be a handling or preservation direction; its author, date, scope and effect are untested. It does not show whether the whole member or a portion was retained, sampled, transferred or later disposed of. An identifier-shaped marking might also be a field notation rather than a final catalog number. Those possibilities remain separate from the observed lettering.\n\nThe strongest objection to any claimed retention failure is that **we have neither an authenticated instruction nor the linked disposition record**. Conversely, a visible SAVE marking or measurement activity cannot prove successful long-term retention, representative sampling or scientific adequacy. The two writings and repeated frames are not counted as independent corroboration or as a count of unique specimens. No link to W14A/W14B, C12, FEMA Sample 1, I0137, WTC 7 or Column 79 has been demonstrated. Nothing here measures material composition, temperature, fracture mechanism, thermite or historical cause.\n\n## Reading and verification scope\n\nThe initial selection used `select='between(n,3150,4050)*not(mod(n-3150,30))+eq(n,3597)',showinfo`: **32 native PNGs**. A concrete partly clipped marking then justified a prospectively recorded extension using `select='between(n,4050,4230)*not(mod(n-4050,30))',showinfo`: **7 PNGs**, including duplicate control frame 4050. Both FFmpeg 7.1.1 runs completed with exit status 0, with overwrite disabled and audio excluded.\n\nThe **39 files represent 38 distinct input indices**, not 39 independent events. Four initial indices had been extracted previously; 34 indices are newly selected relative to that earlier 16-frame set. Only **11 unique full native frames** were individually viewed: 3480, 3570, 3630, 3660, 3900, 3990, 4020, 4050, 4080, 4170 and 4230. Three labeled contact sheets were viewed for navigation; their thumbnails are not a full-detail reading of every selected image. The initial eight-view limit and the later three-view extension were respected.\n\nThe two earlier controls, frames 3597 and 3600, match the new decoded pixels; duplicate 4050 also matches. All 39 PNG hashes/dimensions and three overview hashes were checked. These are reproducible derivation checks, not historical authentication. The original file hash was checked before processing; size and modification time were unchanged after both read-only runs. No continuous visual census, new full-video count, audio review, independent or blinded transcription, AI enhancement, camera-clock test, specimen test or custody authentication was performed. [Reading scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2c3bcf1e77b83287df22) · [verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ec2baef76a4d30984d66).\n\n## Missing inventory and next discriminating records\n\nThe previously recorded NCSTAR 1-3B PDF path was absent from the verified operational media store. That is a specific storage-path limitation; the share was available. One ordinary credential-free request to the [official PDF URL](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/NCSTAR/ncstar1-3b.pdf) on November 3 returned **403 / text/plain, 17 bytes**. Its response entity was retained and hashed. It is not a PDF or evidence of a changed report, deleted record or deliberate obstruction. The attempt stopped; no alternate-client or alternate-host retry was made. No inventory page or row was read or adopted in this unit. [Acquisition limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0c5184ba34eadb9c98ce).\n\nNew TODOs are: **SAVE-01**, original tape/camera and slate/marking crosswalk; **SAVE-02**, actual intake/alias/geometry and inventory records for the candidate markings; **SAVE-03**, original SAVE instruction and subsequent cutting, sampling, transfer, receipt and disposition records; **SAVE-04**, original measurement sheets and any higher-quality source needed to test the unreadable suffix. Each requires a real record, not a presumed match. [Acceptance criteria and carried-forward TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-61e07f3797a3ec255d66).\n\nThe earlier Beverly Hills certification/attachments, museum accession and transfer chains, WTC 7-attribution questions and all **18 original-input criteria** remain open or partial. The broader acquisition/testing goal remains **blocked on original inputs**; this available reading is a separate partial research result. No new original-input acceptance criterion is closed.\n\n## Preservation and publication boundary\n\nThe movie, earlier frames, reports and conflicting or uncertain readings remain preserved. The [immediately preceding public review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/c282a14153df29812b7f365e1ae441329666b4b4/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-nysa-flatbed-photo-2026-11-03/README.md) remains unchanged; [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-269a8ae163cb0dfacc65) records only the appended current text against its immediately preceding preserved combined version. [Checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1a3716f088b07a07a127).\n\nThe public copy contains original research notes, source links, hashes, locators and limits. Raw video, audio, frames, contact sheets, PDF/error bodies, personal information, private correspondence, litigation strategy and credentials are excluded. There was no outreach, request submission, fee, physical test, private-repository push, deletion or history rewrite. Publication verification is recorded separately after the push; it does not authenticate the historical claims.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 49ad307d9813f4aa294a170f96249ae4f81a3975950141ce0b0d0138e2fb2cba -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-b7b15309f29a0e90\"></a>\n### A second collected-steel movie: readable marking and unequal frame counters\n\n**Source unit:** `steel-tape2-3-source-2026-11-03` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-187ab65f75c848d561ec).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY b7b15309f29a0e90e33807dd79fb2ad45e1296377ab1a75fff2b68bd29981d93 -->\n# A second collected-steel movie: readable marking and unequal frame counters\n\nNovember 3, 2026. The previously unexamined public **WTC Tape 2-3.mov** supplies two useful leads: a visible **N10-C3B** marking and a reproducible difference between a reported frame count and the counts emitted by the selected demux/decode pass. The earlier Tape 3 records and uncertainties remain unchanged. These observations identify records and reproduction questions; they do not establish a building origin, later custody, missing camera footage or deliberate editing.\n\n## Source acquired and preserved\n\n[NIST’s archive entry](https://www.nist.gov/world-trade-center-investigation/photos-videos-and-simulations) led to its [Collected Steel repository](https://googledrive.nist.gov/folders/1mO5PPh1ZyZafGUtWrzqhiaDwzTqyEPG-) and [Video folder](CITATIONS.md#nov04-44eed2826dd2b1a294a3). The preserved seven-item listing identifies [WTC Tape 2-3.mov](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9b5fa90dda92ce3bdf10), ID **1UzY8uR-jH_pmgTzRPok5zgrvB7xfZ4iw**. Current metadata retained the same name and size. We selected it as the next-smallest unexamined file, not because its name proved a chronological sequence or independent source.\n\nThe complete anonymous download is **815,698,448 bytes**, SHA-256 **`4beeea4b0e66c5fcaf68f5336ea4b76518f89c6d1cfbba6833915e359f8a4bcb`**, MD5 **`be6770700b7f33e3dd5f07400a809f87`**. Saved bytes were read back and matched the download hash. Retrieval began **2026-11-03T21:34:12.967803+00:00** and finished **2026-11-03T21:36:14.477082+00:00**. This identifies the current public archive entity; it does not authenticate an original camera tape, original filming date or specimen custody. [Source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-237b32351be318f15e19).\n\nThe Drive tool rejected the file at its 256 MiB transfer limit. An ordinary anonymous download through the actual public large-file warning form succeeded. A local check first overlooked the submit button’s label stored in an input value; that failed attempt was retained and the saved form used without a second initial-page request. There was no sign-in or access-denial bypass. These are acquisition/tool events, not historical evidence of withholding.\n\n## T23-C01 — Reported count versus read packets and frames\n\n| Measurement of this same video stream | Observed value | Scope |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FFprobe metadata field `nb_frames` | **11,607** | Reported field; no independent native sample-table interpretation performed. |\n| `nb_read_packets` with `-count_packets` | **11,606** | Packets emitted by this selected FFprobe demux path. |\n| `nb_read_frames` with `-count_frames` | **11,606** | Frames emitted by this selected decoder pass. |\n| Planned uniformly spaced native images | **12** | Selection used the reported count to propose zero-based endpoint 11606. |\n| Images actually emitted by that selection | **11** | Last requested index 11606 did not produce an image in that run. |\n\nThe separate count command completed with **exit 0 and empty warning output**, using FFprobe **7.1.1**. Its installed command help was checked for the counting options. The image-producing FFmpeg child completed with exit 0, but the Python checker then failed its expected-12 versus actual-11 assertion. **That original sample-acceptance check remains failed.** The actual eleven images were retained; no substitute endpoint, changed expected value or invented twelfth image was used. [Exact values and commands](CITATIONS.md#nov04-dfec936cb5f93957fce0) · [frame manifest](CITATIONS.md#nov04-80b7f403d3555714ef39).\n\nThe counting pass, source hash and failed endpoint test make the difference reproducible for this entity and software configuration. They do not identify its cause. Container/table accounting, edit-list treatment, empty or omitted samples, and demux/decoder behavior are untested possibilities. No native tables or alternate edit/decoder policies were tested here, and no preferred counter or explanation is selected. A difference between these layers is not, by itself, proof of corruption, a lost original frame, a cut, fabrication or an elapsed gap in the filmed events. The original camera/tape, export history, native sample/edit tables and an independent reproduction are needed to distinguish those possibilities.\n\nThe [earlier Tape 3 study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/75347e9c38e09b5c2037ee9490e6c2c5acf0f799/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-candidate-originals-2026-10-27/README.md) reported **6,399 stored/reported and decoded entries** for that different file. That earlier result remains unchanged and was not recounted. It neither authenticates Tape 2-3 nor makes the two files independent corroboration.\n\n## T23-O01–O03 — Field markings and collection context\n\nAll indices are zero-based decoder-input indices; times are reported presentation locators, not a filming date or historical clock.\n\n| Observation | Actual full-frame locator | Reading and limitation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| T23-O01 | **8440 / 563.229897 seconds**, frame-09 | Upper line **N10-C3B** is readable on visible structural material. The lower line remains **B-1/8-1 uncertain**. A diagonal line and cross-shaped mark are visible. No inventory, construction-origin or custody join accepted. |\n| T23-O02 | **2110 / 140.807474 seconds**, frame-03 | An **M4-like prefix** and an incompletely accepted suffix; lower **S-1/5-1-like** line. Full identifier remains unaccepted. The original partial transcription is retained in OBSERVATIONS.json. |\n| T23-O03 | Frames 01,04,07,08,10,11; exact indices/PTS in manifest | Structural members/plates on pavement and racks outdoors, with visible open surfaces, deformation and white markings. No active cutting, measuring, transport, preservation instruction or later disposition established from these sampled stills. |\n\nThe readings were recorded before the limited held-text check. A subsequent exact search for N10/C3B in the two held NCSTAR 1-3B page-text derivatives, physical pages 87 and 94, returned no match. That two-page searchable-layer result is not a complete inventory search or proof the identifier is absent. The earlier failed PDF route was not retried. No source label or desired match was used to complete an unreadable character. [Observations](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3b138c76d7d38d2c576b).\n\nThe new readable string is a specific target for marking photographs, intake/alias records, retained-piece/coupon crosswalks and source filming logs. It is not an authenticated final catalog number or WTC 7 attribution. Nearby surfaces and labels are not assumed to belong to one specimen. Sparse sampled views do not establish or exclude overlap with Tape 3; file counts and repeated views are not independent witness or specimen counts. The strongest objection to a lost-evidence inference is the absent specimen/instruction/transfer/disposition join. A visible stored member also cannot establish adequate preservation or representative scientific sampling.\n\n## Actual reading, method and limits\n\nMetadata describes a **640×480 Cinepak (`cvid`), RGB24** video, reported rate **2997/200** fps, video duration **774.506507 seconds**, and format duration **774.506667 seconds**. These are separate reported quantities, retained without correction. The format creation tag reads **2010-06-11T17:49:08Z**, the video tag **2010-06-11T17:49:09Z**, and Drive metadata creation/modification **2019-11-26T06:38:59.078Z**. These object fields do not authenticate filming or measure audio/video synchronization. Audio metadata is retained separately; audio content was not listened to or transcribed. [Metadata](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c0c015e51d04e3783b16).\n\nBefore content reading, twelve indices were frozen by `floor(k*(11607-1)/11)` for k=0…11: **0,1055,2110,3165,4220,5275,6330,7385,8440,9495,10550,11606**. Only the first eleven produced PNGs. All eleven actual raster hashes and native dimensions were verified. **Eight** were individually viewed: frames **01,03,04,07,08,09,10,11**. One labeled, reduced navigation overview was viewed; its final unused slot says no output and is not a source blank image. Its thumbnails are not full-detail readings of frames02/05/06. No additional interval or full-frame view was used. [Reading scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b78839da175c70408c74).\n\nThe one full count pass was prospectively added after the concrete endpoint mismatch; it was not an unchanged count rerun. FFmpeg and FFprobe share a library family, so their agreement is not independent decoder validation. No continuous scene census, voice/person identification, AI enhancement, interpolated frame, calibrated physical dimension, camera-clock authentication, material test, building attribution, historical-cause or intent inference was performed. Source size and modification time remained unchanged through extraction and counting; hashes prove entity identity, not historical conclusions. [Verification and failed checks](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9cfa7ff80602efd52139).\n\n## TODOs and preservation\n\n**T23-01:** native sample/duration/edit tables, applicable export/software configuration and independent count reproduction. **T23-02:** original camera/tape and export/source lineage. **T23-03:** actual N10-C3B and uncertain-marking photographs/intake/alias/geometry/coupon/transfer/disposition records. **T23-04:** a source-supported scene/cross-file overlap map if needed. Each remains unperformed; no missing original is silently supplied by the current download. [Acceptance and carried-forward records](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8b5088e9d75f4d3f4f98).\n\nAll earlier FAA, telephone, recorder, materials and steel original-input requirements remain open or partial. The [preceding SAVE review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/71b47a3713297a336e56109e9cea805a8547fa3e/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-save-marking-followup-2026-11-03/README.md), its M/N/M2 readings and all underlying source bytes remain unchanged. The new [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-acf1c62529b9a298ec5f) appends this report to the immediately preceding preserved combined version, with no removed historical text. [Request checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3008b15048f8013ad0f0).\n\nOnly minimized original notes, links, hashes, metadata, locators and limitations are published. The movie, audio, frame images, contact sheet, raw warning/documents, personal/contact fields, private case material, correspondence, litigation strategy, credentials and coordination records are excluded. There was no outreach, new request, fee, filing, physical test, private push, deletion, source overwrite or history rewrite. Acquisition, measurement, historical authentication and publication remain separate states.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY b7b15309f29a0e90e33807dd79fb2ad45e1296377ab1a75fff2b68bd29981d93 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-fb46aa22712dbc1c\"></a>\n### AA77 carrier printouts: event stages, zero fields and the limits of call counts\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-aa77-event-census-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-aa5baa42594bfa5cb926).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY fb46aa22712dbc1c08af01528c5e599c444b86a0c862f13bd24f5bf5807fbd21 -->\n# AA77 carrier printouts: event stages, zero fields and the limits of call counts\n\nNovember2,2026, America/New_York. TEL01/TEL03/TEL04; AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. **New comparison of an already-held reproduced record span; no new download, native carrier database, authenticated conversation or complete release.**\n\nThe available Flight77 section contains **23 source-annotated records with eight different printed Start Time labels**. Of these,18print zero in the Duration field and5print positive numbers. In **four accepted CSC-identifier groups**, a routed-to-operator record has zero while a later disconnect record with the same printed identifier has a positive Duration. One group includes handoff-started/completed records as well. This makes it unsafe to count each zero record as a separate failed conversation, or each printed record as a separate call. It does **not** establish the real number of conversations, their callers, their recipients or what happened in the disputed named zero-duration entry.\n\n## Source, actual reading and new-versus-reused work\n\nThe [public Request14 reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/13499791/T7-B13-Flight-11-Calls-Fdr-Response-From-DOJ-to-Doc-Req-14-Calls-From-AA-11-and-77-and-UA-175-and-93-ATT-Wireless-UA-And-GTE-Airphone-Call-Record) supplied28hosted JPEG entities on October27,2026. This unit reads **reader11–24**, Bates **M-WFA-00000632–645**, fax labels034–047, as reproduced images. All14preserved entity lengths and SHA-256 values match their acquisition pins. [Every image's exact URL/access date/hash](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8a1eb996a9b2bc683a28).\n\nThe [earlier enclosure review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ad7be60185f5d3a49f0e0b7564f4da3610afaf92/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-carrier-enclosures-2026-10-27/README.md) had read selected fields and all page-accounting labels. Its C05 already documented158-versus146anchor arithmetic. The [earlier selected-event comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/cd950cd141582ab562ad74e17be6231077a2cc4c/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-event-joins-2026-10-27/README.md) tested fiveblocks on15/16/20/21 and exact CSC/GS pairs for two groups. Those are reused findings, not new discoveries here. The new work is the **whole available Flight77 span's record/continuation accounting, accepted CSC-only grouping, broader phase patterns and explicit annotation map**. The completed UA93/UA175 table work and court-label analysis are not repeated as new evidence.\n\nAll14whole page images were inspected, plus local nearest-neighbor key/field detail sheets. Enlargement adds no source detail; no OCR or new automated transcription was run. The upper fragment on11 precedes the Flight77 heading and is **excluded**, not silently assigned to that flight. Several records continue across pages; the final fragment on24 continues record23, not an extra event. Source circled1–23labels are useful locators, **not authenticated native unique record IDs**. Their author and insertion date remain unknown. [23record operational readings](CITATIONS.md#nov04-59499de32ad524a351a6) · [Computed results](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c272361f807e0925b080) · [Method and reading limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3c0e8858702dbf8b64a3).\n\n## 1. Quantities in the held span\n\n| Quantity | Result | Meaning and limit |\n|---|---:|---|\n|Source-annotated record headers under the Flight77 heading |23 |Not23people, calls or conversations; page continuations excluded from extra counting. |\n|Distinct printed Start Time strings |8 |Not independent clock calibration or eight authenticated calls. Source order includes07:14:57 before07:12:18. |\n|Accepted complete CSC readings / distinct CSC values |22records /7values |One first-record repeated-digit/length reading remains unaccepted. No claim of eight accepted full identifier groups. |\n|Full GS strings independently accepted for this census |0 |GS fields were inspected but uncertain separators/final glyphs were not filled; no new full CSC+GS equality claim. Earlier selected pair tests remain separate. |\n|Zero / positive Duration fields |18 /5 |Field values, not failure/success findings about conversations. |\n|Event-type codes represented |6 |Menu selection25:9; routing29:4; air disconnect4:7; ground disconnect3:1; handoff started1:1; handoff completed2:1. |\n\nRaw CSC values, GS reading details, contact/card/phone fields and images are excluded from publication. Public K01–K07 labels are **our derived aliases**, not carrier IDs or caller identities. The first unaccepted CSC record is retained separately; it is not matched to another row using its clock. Equal printed identifiers strengthen a printout association but do not prove installed identifier allocation/reuse rules, actual physical call identity, a unique end-to-end leg or a complete export.\n\n## 2. Four groups contain zero routing records and positive disconnect records\n\n|Our alias / printed start |Source-annotated records and reader pages |Printed event-code sequence |Duration fields in that source order |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|K03 /07:15:34 |4–7; reader13–15, Bates634–636 |menu25,menu25,routed29,air disconnect4 |0,0,0,102 |\n|K05 /07:20:15 |10–15; reader16–19, Bates637–640 |menu25,menu25,routed29,handoff1,handoff2,air disconnect4 |0,0,0,0,0,274 |\n|K06 /07:25:48 |16–19; reader19–22, Bates640–643 |menu25,menu25,routed29,air disconnect4 |0,0,0,159 |\n|K07 /07:30:56 |20–23; reader22–24, Bates643–645 |menu25,menu25,routed29,air disconnect4 |0,0,0,260 |\n\nThe code groups these records by **individually entered accepted CSC strings**, not by desired start/time matches, circled labels or a group key copied into all rows. Full GS-string equality is not asserted. The K06 selected zero/159pair was already documented; the other three full phase groups and the broader accounting extend that observation. These are related stages in the **same reproduced source**, not four independent witnesses or corroborations of a historical conversation.\n\nFor K05, the [handoff-started record13 on reader18](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/18-f7e10d4c8d.jpg) prints07:24:01 and its [completed continuation14 on reader19](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/19-1f570a8a28.jpg) prints07:24:06. Both have zero Duration; the later disconnect record15 prints274. Those labels do not establish aircraft position, a measured five-second transfer, the effective radio configuration or what any person heard. They are a concrete target for the actual event/schema/clock and station-mapping records. No timing cause or preferred account is selected.\n\nThe07:18:58group K04 remains different: its two held records8–9, [reader15–16](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/15-d3c94df2c0.jpg), print zero. The early connected-to-office narrative and later court/briefing unconnected label remain alongside it. **Positive fields in other groups do not resolve K04**, identify Barbara Olson or prove which operator/office event the early unnamed narrative describes. The first two source-annotated records are also zero and are not transformed into conversations from their start-to-event spans.\n\n## 3. The printout itself contains scoped explanatory annotations\n\n[Reader13, Bates634, record4](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/13-ec2683a0f2.jpg) marks the1969billing-start and answer-supervision fields with **“Time is not tracked because OSPS bills”**. [Reader14, Bates635, record6](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/14-92e4203dc6.jpg) marks the routed-event duration **“Duration is not tracked by AWS”**. The record4annotation also describes an operator-selection path; that remains the annotator's description, not an inspected operator ticket or proof of an actual completed transfer.\n\nThese are source-image annotations. They are more specific than a generic possible explanation, but **the annotator, insertion date, installed version and governing authority are unverified**. A fax header naming AT&T Wireless does not authenticate who added every note. Do not promote the annotations into a universal carrier data dictionary, or apply GTE ACIS definitions to this different AT&T/Claircom evidence.\n\nAll18zero rows in this span also show the printed1969billing/answer dates. Those literal values remain; we do not replace them with0, an epoch conversion, a true call time or a demonstrated explanation for their presence. The annotations specifically address selected fields/records; they do not establish that every zero, including the07:18:58disconnect, is merely an untracked value.\n\n## 4. Broader arithmetic controls, without reannouncing old discrepancies\n\nThe positive Duration values are158,102,274,159and260. In all five, the number equals the difference between the supplied printed event and billing-start clocks. In four it also equals the answer-supervision-to-event difference. The [record3 continuation on reader13](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/13-ec2683a0f2.jpg) is the existing exception:07:13:11billing,07:13:23answer,07:15:49event, Duration158; the answer interval is146. **The12-second anchor distinction was already published as C05**, not newly discovered. The new all-positive accounting supplies controls around it; it does not establish universal duration units, conversation onset or calibrated elapsed time.\n\nThe [routed record18 on reader21](https://html.scribdassets.com/5bafzdomdce6sz3/images/21-1a330ff42d.jpg) retains the earlier **07:26:18 /07:26:28** reading uncertainty; no single event time is accepted for that row. It is not converted into a measured negative/positive timing anomaly or silently chosen to make the sequence orderly. Higher-quality source media and effective system definitions remain discriminators.\n\n## Conflicts, contrary evidence and what remains missing\n\n- **159/154seconds:**the reproduced159field remains beside the Commission final-report note57's154; the new grouping does not explain or correct either account. [Final-report notes, printed455](https://www.9-11commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.pdf#page=7).\n- **Connected/unconnected:**the September20,2001report reader43–44/internal1–2 describes an unnamed caller connected to the office; the May2004briefing and court classify the09:18:58entry as unconnected. A unique underlying event/leg join is still missing. [Early report](https://www.scribd.com/document/24392516/T7-B19-Key-302s-Fdr-Entire-Contents-FBI-302s) · [May briefing](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886083/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-General-Fdr-52004-DOJ-Briefing-on-Cell-and-Phone-Calls-From-AA-77-408).\n- **Eight/seven, direct/collect and May6:05Pacific/6:13nozone:**earlier count, recipient and time accounts remain source-specific and unresolved. Eight different start strings here do not adjudicate another report's counting conventions. Keyton's released form, Sept20reader rendering and the May-family released response are held components, not wholly missing categories.\n- **Counterevidence to simplistic interpretations:**multiple printed phase records share accepted CSC values; zero routing/handoff fields coexist with positive disconnect fields. That weakens counting every zero as a separate failed call. Conversely, a positive duration and a named display label do not independently authenticate an actual speaker/conversation. The [staff report physical94note265](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=94) expressly leaves conversation-to-unknown-record matching uncertain.\n\nRoutine event-stage reporting, transcription/compilation error, version differences, different legs or incorrect attribution are competing possibilities to test; deliberate manipulation is untested. Neither explanation nor motive is inferred from this census. The source printouts, their summaries and exhibit may share inputs and are not independent corroboration.\n\nThe full Request14delivery/release/version chain and missing Bates609–631/fax011–033remain open. No contents are inferred for that hosted gap. Native carrier/switch/operator/office records, key-allocation and field/clock rules, annotator/transformation records and source-to-exhibit/caller/recipient joins remain needed. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-55886fe0a96a634fc753) retain all five tracks and18full criteria; this unit closes none by publication or arithmetic.\n\n## Reproduction and preservation\n\n[compare_events.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d38d2f23f75ccc0aa5b8) computes counts and groupings from supplied manual readings. Native execution used the local raw-CSC transcription; the public derivative retains only aliases. Controls include an unequal-key pair, a changed key with the same start, reversed input membership and two missing keys that must not be joined. They validate comparison behavior, **not our ability to read each glyph or a historical event**. No blinded second analyst, native export or independent image decoder was used.\n\n`python3 -B verify.py` checks the bundle and safe derived-data reproduction. Optional `--capture-dir` checks original JPEG hashes; optional `--transcriptions` repeats the accepted raw-CSC comparison from locally supplied readings. An independent reviewer should transcribe the original public images first, rather than copying our groups as a second source. [Actual verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-268403673fbdc4d62fb8).\n\nOriginal images/old reports/public history remain unchanged; [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a30c0f437519ba4c0b67) is actual zero-context Git output against the immediately preceding preserved combined review. Initial source-path guesses, premature image views while a producer was still live, and mispositioned reading crops were our process errors, not historical anomalies. The same live process was awaited to terminal success; no failed output was counted as source absence. No raw images/keys/contacts/card data, signatures, private case material, outreach, new request, fee, deletion, overwrite, main merge or history rewrite is part of this public addition.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY fb46aa22712dbc1c08af01528c5e599c444b86a0c862f13bd24f5bf5807fbd21 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-ae2f2071277cb6b4\"></a>\n### An answering-system collection report supplies a concrete property-record target\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-answering-system-property-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-77c093578f2968a6cf77).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY ae2f2071277cb6b489afb0ad3fa69e6b8bd3858620515bb28fc9aa03f90b3877 -->\n# An answering-system collection report supplies a concrete property-record target\n\nNovember2,2026, America/New_York; acquisition/reading November3UTC. **TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** A newly inspected official FBI interview describes an unintelligible message possibly associated with Philip Rosenzweig. Following that exact lead located a public Commission-packet mirror containing a report of collecting a telephone with an answering system and referring to **FD-192 / bulky evidence**. This advances the property/custody inquiry. The original property form, device, audio, analysis and disposition remain unacquired.\n\n## First source: a possible caller, not an identified voice\n\n[Official FBI part02, physical35, footer000000425](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=35), final body paragraph, says an answering machine recorded an **unintelligible phone call between8:44a.m.and9:00a.m.** on September11. It records the interviewee's belief that Rosenzweig **might have attempted** to call. That is a qualified attribution, not intelligible identification, a verified completed passenger conversation or proof the call originated on an aircraft.\n\nThe same paragraph lists his cellular carrier as **either Sprint or Cellular One**. It does not establish that the reported message used that handset or either service. Do not infer a cellular transmission from possession of a cell phone, choose a carrier, or add this unconfirmed contact to an authenticated-call total. No caller voice, original recording, destination/service event, aircraft position or calibrated clock was tested.\n\nThe visible report gives **investigation09/12/2001**, **transcription09/15/2001**, **dictated09/15/2001**, **case265D-NY-280350**, **REQ.#35-13**, and footer **000000425**. These fields have different explicit roles. They are not competing dates for the September11 event. The recipient's identity is masked in this release and is not reconstructed from another version. Unrelated personal/medical/employment/travel details, contacts and agent names are excluded from this derivative.\n\n## Second source: reported collection and a reference to FD-192\n\nThe [public Packet6 reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/19131547/T7-B13-DOJ-Doc-Req-35-13-Packet-6-Fdr-Entire-Contents-FBI-Reports-730), **reader84 / printedfooter000000476**, shows a report dated **9/14/01**. Its opening says items were provided to FBI agents and a Massachusetts state trooper on **9/14/2001 at11:45AM**. Item1 describes **one white Sony telephone with a self-contained answering system** and says:\n\n> This item was placed on a FD-192 to be placed in bulky evidence.\n\nThat sentence is a specific route to pursue. It is a statement in a report about listing/routing the telephone, **not the FD-192 itself**, an inspected bulky-evidence entry, a barcode, a complete custody log or proof of present survival. No original telephone, answering-machine recording, forensic extraction, examination result or disposal record was acquired here. The hardware serial and private telephone/address fields are retained only in the preserved raw image and excluded from publication; their omission from this derivative does not mean the source lacks them.\n\nThe final body paragraph describes **approximately8:45AM** on September11 and a telephone call that was **static**, whose nature the recipient could not determine. Preserve this beside the first report's **8:44–9:00 / unintelligible / might have attempted** account. A common unmasked passenger-name reference, request label or approximate time does not authenticate a common household, message, device or call. The masked interviewee's identity is not filled from this mirror's different redactions. No controlling timestamp, service or caller is selected, and no discrepancy is resolved.\n\nThe collection report also displays **case265D-NY-280350**, **REQ.#35-13**, and footer **000000476**. Its bottom handwritten302-like control is not adopted as an exact identifier. Its separately listed personal items and biological-identification information are outside this telephone study and not republished. They do not become audio evidence by appearing on the same page.\n\n## Source relationship and authentication limits\n\nThe FBI source is an official delivered PDF entity, unchanged at **5,561,167bytes /78pages**, SHA-256 **055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51**, acquired **2026-10-31T22:04:24.920527+00:00**. This unit inspected only physical35. Official hosting authenticates the provenance of that released entity; it does not verify the historical truth of every interview statement.\n\nThe collection report is a **third-party public reader image of an apparent FBI/Commission record**, not an authenticated agency-native production. The visible cover, reader1, says **Commission Copy / Requests#35-13 / Packet#6**. That identifies the displayed packet's claimed relationship; it does not prove complete production, native delivery, an official source-to-item join, or that every record in the100-page reader was inspected. The reader's AI-enhanced title/description is not relied on as evidence.\n\nOnly reader1 and84 were downloaded through the supported browser's displayed-image function and read. Both entities are **WebP,904×1242**, despite displayed asset names ending.jpg. That is delivery-format metadata, not evidence of historical alteration. The original browser downloads and redundant Intel copies remain unchanged. The image entities identify the actual viewed bytes:\n\n| Entity | Bytes | SHA-256 | Preservation UTC |\n| --- | ---: | --- | --- |\n| Reader84 collection report |48,980|62df96a149ce5f4d6399aee8bcf1c4e5c975a01eb3222349fc68a2a9e460af8e|2026-11-03T03:00:22.998104+00:00|\n| Reader1 cover |74,054|5c3c272ca7b38d276178bddcc64047684f8812ba8f9f2ff2060c79391283b75e|2026-11-03T03:00:54.992220+00:00|\n\nThese are preservation times; the exact preceding browser-download times were not separately captured. Ephemeral asset-query credentials are excluded from provenance/public payload; no token-removal fetch, login, gated whole-document download or denied official route was used. A first local copy attempt failed because the resolved output directory had not yet been created; the directory was then created and the same downloaded bytes copied exclusively and verified. No remote re-download, original overwrite or historical anomaly is inferred from that execution error.\n\nThe ordinary-text index for held official part02 had no Sony/FD-192/bulky hit. That bounded index result is **not** a source-absence, official-omission or concealment finding. This review did not read all78pages, all eight FBI parts or all100 mirror pages. A newly located indexed NARA finding-aid reference to Team7/Box13/Packet6 is a navigation lead, not an acquired official counterpart of footer476. No claim of a complete official release crosswalk is made.\n\n## What the records can test next\n\n**RH01:** Obtain the agency-held counterpart of footer476 and any native attachments/metadata. Compare to the mirror without overwriting either. Source authenticity and full document context remain open.\n\n**RH02:** Obtain the actual **FD-192**, bulky-evidence registration, item/barcode/location fields and all receipts/transfers for the telephone described in the September14 collection report. A report's past-tense listing statement and future placement language do not certify every handling stage.\n\n**RH03:** Obtain preserved answering-system memory/audio, source/copy/extraction logs, examinations and findings, including negative or inconclusive outcomes. Determine whether any record actually joins the collection to the earlier possible message. Ordinary noise, an unrelated caller, a misunderstood connection, an aircraft call, or another contact remain untested possibilities. No voice or signal analysis was performed here.\n\n**RH04:** Obtain device settings/time checks, native carrier/operator/destination returns and source-to-recipient worksheets. Retain both time descriptions and both carrier candidates; an uncalibrated reported interval is not a flight-clock anchor. Do not identify callers from matching time strings or infer tampering from absent verification.\n\n**RH05:** Obtain retention/disposition/return records and surviving derivative-copy references. The report establishes a concrete retrieval target; it establishes neither destruction nor continued retention. These requests are TODOs, not sent communications; no new FOIA, fee, outreach or filing occurred.\n\nThe strongest limitation is the unverified link between a qualified message attribution and a telephone collection described in a separate, mirrored report. An authenticated counterpart, item-level custody/analysis or contrary source could change this assessment. A collection record alone cannot establish who called, what they said, advance knowledge or conspiracy.\n\n## Scope, revision and continuing work\n\nActual reading: **one official FBI face**, plus **two newly acquired mirror faces**. No adjacent official page was needed because physical35 ends a self-contained report. The Ong transcript candidate pages48/50 repeated completed work and were excluded. No new OCR, ASR, sound decoding, clock fitting, physical measurement, independent transcription or complete archive search was performed. The unchanged technical-owner recorder/materials results and independent audit retain their own scope; this unit does not claim their unfinished tests.\n\nAll five original work-plan tracks and all eighteen substantive criteria remain open/partial. FAA correction/delivery, signed administrative disposition, telephone original joins, recorder/materials native tests and steel preservation/attribution originals remain explicit dependencies. This is progress on a concrete telephone property-record chain, not completion of the goal.\n\n[SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0799143605bf320ebd1a), [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ac24fe7595f3558d12d6), [READING-SCOPE.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-173d3a0c2385674891fe), [OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1502b4c5961d1f0cd5a3), [LOCATORS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3cdd3c169e2feb424309), [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d932a867d58cc433900c) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d2cea0cfed6fe793625b) separate source representations, inference limits, actual preservation checks and missing originals. [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e9ec303ebf257b8565c9) preserves the exact additive text comparison against the immediately preceding combined review. Raw source images/PDF, private fields, message content, correspondence and local coordination are excluded from the public derivative. Remote Git verification is separate from source reading, and publication does not authenticate historical claims.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY ae2f2071277cb6b489afb0ad3fa69e6b8bd3858620515bb28fc9aa03f90b3877 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-9ca9357fc59c4fd7\"></a>\n### Britton telephone evidence: underlying interview, reference dates and search coverage\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-britton-source-chain-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-13e00290f13a7842a30d).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 9ca9357fc59c4fd77aa39bb00a521c74db26ebef344561eeefd34c53df7430bb -->\n# Britton telephone evidence: underlying interview, reference dates and search coverage\n\nReview: October 31, 2026 local / November 1, 2026 UTC. This is a documentary source comparison, not a call/device experiment or a finding of fabrication or concealment.\n\nThe held official FBI release contains a two-page recipient interview that we had not previously read in this work. It qualifies the cellphone claim as the recipient's assumption, gives an approximate alternative call time, and supplies a specific report locator. A separate staff working sheet cites that locator but still calls for phone-record confirmation. The Commission staff-report citation gives a different interview date. These records now narrow the required carrier, source-version and citation checks; those checks are not complete.\n\n## Sources and actual reading scope\n\n1. **Official FBI part 02 PDF, physical pages 9–10**, release footers **000000226–000000227**, REQ. #35-13, file **265A-NY-280350-302**; first-page handwritten locator **302 25306**. [Official PDF, page9](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=9). The previously acquired 78-page PDF is 5,561,167 bytes, SHA-256 **055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51**. Newly rendered and visually read both selected pages in full. The released PDF is held; original interview notes/audio, native authoring and carrier events are not thereby authenticated.\n2. **Official PG1602 control record, part 06 viewer pages 10–12**, footers **000000251–000000253**, case **265A-PG-69744 (PENDING)**, REQ. #35-13. [Official viewer](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-06-of-08/view). Read those three pages, preserving six unchanged browser views. The source PDF was not downloaded in this unit; the earlier stopped 403 route was not retried. A historical PENDING label is not a current case-status determination.\n3. **Commission staff report, physical page 99, note 371.** [Official NARA PDF](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=99). Previously held 121-page PDF, 6,760,035 bytes, SHA-256 **9671b7afe9a45928dcbe053e567b7f830876bc31e32a1d221b39fa59493d5bbb**. Newly rendered page 99 and read the citation in the page image. The source is the official archived staff report, not merely an extracted-date assertion.\n4. **Staff working-sheet reproduction, selected blocks on viewer pages 1–2 of 8**: TO: File; FM: John Raidt; RE:Phone calls from aircraft hijacked on 9/11 as per Concordance. [Public reproduction](https://www.scribd.com/document/13499803/T7-B13-Flights-Phone-Calls-Fdr-Search-of-FBI-302-Files-for-175-77-and-93). Read the header/query discussion and Britton entry 3, including fields B/D/F/G/H; preserve three selected viewports. No native memo/PDF/query database or authenticated archival delivery was acquired. AI-enhanced title/description, suggested documents and uploader labels are not agency evidence. No claim that every page or entry was read.\n\n[SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b836497165710d6e543f) provides exact fields, dates, source URLs, acquisition/capture times, byte/hash and scope records. Images and source PDFs remain preserved locally, outside the public payload. Screenshot/render hashes identify those derivatives, not historical call data.\n\n## 1. What the underlying interview actually qualifies\n\nThe official part 02 report's first page records an interview on **09/17/2001**, with **Date of transcription 09/20/2001**; its continuation repeats **09/17/2001**. The interview subject remains masked here. No identity from a less-redacted mirror is used to fill that mask or identify a masked PG1602 actor.\n\nThe call paragraph begins **“At approximately 9:30am or 9:45am on 09/11/01”** (the **or**, two values and approximate qualification are retained). It reports a hijacking conversation, a number supplied for a callback, screaming and the line going dead. The next paragraph says the attempted callback got a message that the number was not in service. It then expressly says the recipient **assumed** Britton had borrowed a cellphone, given the number she supplied. This is an inference reported in an interview, not direct observation of the onboard equipment or an independently verified service classification.\n\nThe report also limits what the recipient said was conveyed: no identifying details about the hijackers, their number or armament, who was flying, the intended destination, or other passengers' activities. The continuation says Britton did not explain how she knew about the two World Trade Center impacts. Those are limits on this account, not proof the events did not occur. A callback failure is not proof that the original conversation was impossible; original routing, dialed-number and service records are needed. No personal/contact/profile data from the continuation is reproduced publicly.\n\n## 2. Comparison without silently converting assumptions into measurements\n\n| Source and exact field | Preserved wording/value | Limit or unresolved join |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Official part 02 p. 9, callback paragraph | Recipient **assumed** a borrowed cellphone from the supplied number | No native carrier/device verification; subject masked |\n| Working sheet p. 2, entry 3B | **Borrowed Cell Phone**; contact digits excluded from this public derivative | Summarized category; entryG cites record 25306, not a carrier row |\n| Working sheet p. 2, entry 3H | **CONFIRM TIME AND DURATION OF CALL WITH CELL PHONE RECORD.** | Explicitly an outstanding task in the sheet; no later completion supplied by that instruction |\n| Official part 02 p. 9, call paragraph | Approximately **9:30am or 9:45am** | Two approximate alternatives; timezone/clock not established |\n| Working sheet p. 2, entry 3D | **Time: Between 9:30-9:45** | Different time formulation; no conversion of alternatives into a verified interval |\n| Working sheet p. 2, entry 3F | **No tape mentioned in 302** | Not a finding that no recording existed anywhere |\n| PG1602 pp. 10–11, Event narrative | Relayed **cellular telephone** description and **“the plane will crash in 20” / “SECONDS.”** | Report of a relay, not an independently timed 20-second interval; actors remain masked |\n| Official part 02 p. 9, crash wording | Turning and going to crash; line went dead | This selected two-page report does not supply the PG1602 narrative's 20-second measurement or independently authenticate a crash time |\n\nThe working sheet's explicit **265A-NY-280350-302-25306** reference and the official scan's **302 25306** annotation provide a qualified record-reference association. They are not a native byte/version match or permission to reconstruct masked identities. The sheet is a derivative account of its cited report, not a second independent witness or carrier confirmation. We have not proved which document PG1602's reply referenced.\n\n## 3. Dates and the prior-interview claim remain separate\n\n**PG1602 p. 10** is a communication dated **09/22/2001**, Pittsburgh to Pittsburgh. The information-received field says **09/20/2001, 11:18 PM**, source label **SOMERSET CRASH DP** (unexpanded). Its continuation on **p. 11** reports contact and a reply that the person had been interviewed by FBI New York. Some wording near the end of the first line is obscured by markings; the legible phrase **“INTERVIEWED BY FBI NEW YORK”** is retained without inventing missing text. The form's **Event Date 09/11/2001; Time 12:00 PM** is an administrative field whose relation to the reported call is unverified.\n\n**PG1602 p. 12** records assignment on **09/21/2001 at 1:23 AM** and conditions setting an interview lead on a determination that the person **“HAS NOT ALREADY BEEN INTERVIEWED.”** The prior-interview reply, “Lead Required?: YES” and conditional assignment are all preserved. Neither the presence of an assignment nor a reply about an interview establishes the actual interview's record ID, performance, clearance or later closure. No missing return is treated as proof of inaction.\n\n**Staff-report p. 99, note 371** cites: **“FBI report of investigation, recipient of call from Marion Britton, Sept. 14, 2001.”** The held official candidate instead has an interview date of **September 17** and transcription date of **September 20**. Both candidate dates and the **September 14 citation** remain. Note371 lacks the specific 25306 identifier in the printed citation. Thus we cannot yet establish that it cites this very report, that the citation is erroneous, or that the dates were changed. A different interview, a citation mistake or a version difference are untested possibilities. Obtain the actual cited September 14 record or a source crosswalk before adjudicating them.\n\n## 4. A specific search-coverage question, not a reproduced defect\n\nThe working sheet says its data came from a set of FBI 302 files derived from searches using **phone call AND flight AND 175/77/93**, **phone AND call AND flight AND 175/77/93**, **cell phone AND flight AND 175/77/93**, and **cell AND call AND flight AND 175/77/93**, with the flight numbers checked independently. Its claim of a “complete set” is scoped to those searches; it does not establish complete FBI holdings, a full carrier database or a complete independent call census.\n\nThe writer adds: **“For some odd reason inputting 11 in the flight number field would search and return 175 instead of 11. Need to check with FBI on this.”** We read that statement in the reproduction; we did not rerun the query or acquire its native execution log, syntax, field definitions, database version, original/corrected results or follow-up. Treat it as a reported retrieval problem and a concrete TODO. It does not establish deliberate exclusion, actual loss of Flight 11 evidence or a live defect today. The relevant test is reconstruction from the original database/query records, preserving both successful and contrary results.\n\n## Assessment, missing records and preservation\n\nConfidence is high about the displayed qualifications and dates in the held official PDFs. Confidence is limited about call service, exact time, native-record authenticity beyond the released PDF, whether the candidate is the note 371 source or PG1602 interview, and what happened to the reported search issue. A plausible ordinary reading is early interview inference followed by provisional staff categorization and a still-pending verification task. That interpretation is not established merely because it is plausible. These sources do not establish a manufactured call, suppression or intent.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a1f6f2e18e739c6a3a08) retains the actual September 14 source/citation crosswalk; native interview material; PG1602 contact/assignment/return/version records; carrier/operator/routing/service and clock joins; the exact 25306-to-call/exhibit mapping; and native working-sheet/query/follow-up records. No inquiry/request was sent. The held official two-page interview is now read and should not be described as wholly unacquired; its underlying notes/audio and operational joins remain missing. All 18 original FAA/telephone/recorder/materials/steel requirements remain open/partial; no native call, calibrated clock, voice, decoder or laboratory test was completed here.\n\nEarlier records and conflicting values are unchanged. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d1d5843a507a252d330d), [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-6329515b0029b6e61362) and [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-4da340b4f44199e8692d) distinguish actual reading, source/hash/diff checks, public additions and unperformed tests. The addition diff is against no prior file at this new path, not a replacement of previous reports. [EDITORIAL-REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-84fbad2b4e5834103db1) and [FINAL-REVIEW-REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7a6d02ee3662d0a837ba) preserve successive prepublication text changes; earlier candidates remain unchanged locally. Raw PDFs/screenshots, personal/contact/profile details, masked identities, private correspondence, strategy and credentials are excluded from the public payload.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 9ca9357fc59c4fd77aa39bb00a521c74db26ebef344561eeefd34c53df7430bb -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-db35489ff539b5bd\"></a>\n### First operator’s 2002 interview: screen-print lead, handoffs and conflicting labels\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-first-operator-followup-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-cfe366a595c641e54a3c).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY db35489ff539b5bd71547e4979f7beb074a470d0e9bae6c9e1477d6d5cbdd802 -->\n# First operator’s 2002 interview: screen-print lead, handoffs and conflicting labels\n\nThe interview records an Airfone operator’s account of a caller who identified himself as **Todd Beamer**. That is the report’s attribution, not an independent voice or caller identification.\n\n**The newly read interview identifies a specific original artifact:** a computer-screen print reportedly made when the call disconnected, intended for engineering to determine where the call originated on the aircraft. It also gives a file/serial pointer to the supervisor’s interview. Neither the print, transfer receipt nor engineering result is attached to these two pages.\n\nThe record also prints **flight 99**, whereas the earlier supervisor account prints **Flight 93**. It shifts between **JOHNSON** and **JACKSON** within one paragraph. These values remain preserved with their qualifications. They do not establish a different aircraft, fabricated call, deliberate alteration or concealment.\n\n## Source and actual scope\n\nThe [held public mirror, physical 23–24](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=23) is a third-party reproduction of FBI-form records. The 73-page PDF has **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 **`e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`**, and was acquired October 27, 2026. No new source download or public search was performed. The original bytes are unchanged; a hash does not independently authenticate the source as an agency master.\n\nBoth interview pages were newly read in full on November 2. They are internal **1–2**, production footers **000000370–371**, file **265A-NY-280350-302**. The investigation date is **06/05/2002**; transcription and dictation fields are **06/11/2002**. Those are distinct field roles, not an adopted date discrepancy. The account concerns September 11, 2001 and is a later recorded recollection.\n\nFor comparison, previously read [official FBI part 08, physical 4–5](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-08-of-08/at_download/file#page=4) was viewed again. Its PDF SHA-256 is **`a7d3d872daf33d41c993ade5ccf2e9aa5421ffb1f4cda6164d6bb712372dde41`**. The earlier source carries **265D-NY-280350**, distinct from the 2002 report’s **265A** labels. No case alias or serialized-copy relationship is established by adjacency or similar names. Official hosting identifies that released entity, not the truth of every assertion or full custody.\n\nFive held contact sheets were used only for navigation. They are not 60 newly read source pages. Two new and two previously read full-page faces were examined; no complete 73-page/21-page review, hidden-text recovery, new OCR, audio/ASR, native clock or carrier replication is claimed. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ebfbd49e7910ee201910) supplies access dates, representation roles and source/raster hashes. Raw scans, images, full interviews, contact/financial/profile fields and signatures are excluded from this derivative.\n\n## 1. Screen print: reported creation versus intended transfer\n\n[Physical 24, final paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=24) says a print of the computer screen containing administrative call information was made when the call disconnected. It says the information **was to be passed** to engineering to determine where the call was made on the aircraft.\n\nThat identifies an artifact and intended work. It does **not** establish that engineering received it, performed the analysis, identified a seat/handset or produced a retained result. The actual print and its fields, session identifiers, dispatch/receipt, engineering work order and analytical disposition are concrete retrieval targets. An earlier provider report separately describes notes, a typed summary and a print handed to an agent; generic print-screen wording does not show these are the same artifact.\n\nThe [earlier May 11, 2004 memorandum review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b6923d4d9c874ab71fe88112f401d5279caaeb95/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-operator-notes-mfr-2026-10-31/README.md) records uncertainty about whether the first operator made notes. A computer print is not automatically handwritten notes. The new interview neither resolves nor contradicts that uncertainty. It does not report a recovered call recording.\n\n## 2. A specific interview pointer\n\n[Physical 24, first paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=24) references the supervisor’s interview under **265A-NY-280350-OUT, serial 3255**. Preserve that string as printed. Locate the actual serial, its cover, continuations, enclosures and interview/source-version association before equating it with a previously acquired supervisor account. The pointer is not a receipt or proof the referenced material is in this compilation.\n\n## 3. Times and holds describe different reported phases\n\n| Source | Preserved account | Limitation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| First operator, physical 23, first substantive paragraph | Answered at **approximately 8:40 a.m. Central** | Later recollection; no native clock/event match. |\n| First operator, physical 24, second paragraph | **Less than ten minutes** speaking or conferring with the supervisor | Her involvement, not total session, caller speech or billed duration. |\n| Same paragraph | **Three holds:** once **less than two minutes**, twice **less than thirty seconds** | Estimated holds; no exact summed interval or event rows recovered. |\n| Supervisor, official part 08 physical 4 | Received the call at **approximately 8:45 a.m. Central** | Different participant/possible phase; source clocks and event identity unjoined. |\n\nThe supervisor handoff is described, but these reports do not supply the actual transfer timestamp or a calibrated five-minute interval. Do not adjust either time or count held time as continuous passenger speech. Native agent/session/conference/hold records, clock/field definitions and original notes are needed. Existing silence, later-callback and terminal-time disagreements remain unchanged.\n\n## 4. Flight label and surname variations\n\n[Physical 23, final paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=23) reports the caller’s number as **United flight 99**, expressly qualified as what the operator recalls. Its earlier paragraph says only that her screen indicated a **United Airlines** flight; it does not say the screen displayed 99. The [supervisor report, official physical 4](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-08-of-08/at_download/file#page=4), reports **United Airlines Flight 93**.\n\nPreserve **99 / 93** and their source roles. Caller name, airline and destination make a proposed documentary comparison useful, but they are not a native session or voice-identification join. Original notes, media, screen fields and report versions could distinguish recollection, transcription, different events or other possibilities. None is selected as the cause or the actual spoken number.\n\nThe second substantive paragraph on physical 23 repeatedly uses **JOHNSON**, but two consultation sentences use **JACKSON**. The report does not explain the variation. Both remain recorded. An editorial error, alias, different person or another cause has not been tested; no preferred surname, reconstructed identity or intentional alteration is inferred.\n\n## 5. Preserve what was heard, inferred and not recalled\n\nThe first substantive paragraph reports two people with knives and someone entering the cockpit, then explicitly attributes to the operator the conclusion that the latter was additional. That inference is not an independent direct count of three attackers. The second paragraph’s calm/quiet description is reported perception, not an acoustic measurement or test of authenticity.\n\nPhysical 24 says she did not recall clothing or ethnicity descriptions. That is a limit on recall, not proof no such words were spoken. These distinctions matter when comparing accounts; they do not independently establish or disprove the caller’s identity or any historical mechanism.\n\n## Status, limits and next records\n\nThe useful advance is a closer creation/engineering-work pointer, an exact interview serial and a bounded source comparison. [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-62302f250938af0ccc0b) contains **seven related analyst entries**, not seven independent records or corroborations. No native print, transfer, completed engineering result, original notes/audio, calibrated clock or authenticated caller/session mapping has been recovered by reading these pages.\n\nThe strongest limitation is dependence on reproduced reports and recollection: multiple forms can summarize the same event, and the June 2002 and September 2001 records do not authenticate each other. Quiet speech, naming/number differences and missing underlying artifacts do not establish a fake call or cover-up. The notes/print/engineering and source-version records could strengthen or weaken later interpretations.\n\nAll original five-track/18 requirements stay open or partial. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-886d30aa896cb023c29b) retains the missing inputs; prior actual acquisitions/tests remain performed. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-248983a7b3ae35136da6), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d953b48ec06da1120d1b) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a9cb610a6d7da597213e) separate reading, preservation and publication from historical validation. Earlier source bytes, printed conflicts and report versions remain unchanged. No new search, outreach, request, fee, filing, private-source use, source overwrite or history rewrite occurred. Publication is not main-branch adoption or substantive goal completion.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY db35489ff539b5bd71547e4979f7beb074a470d0e9bae6c9e1477d6d5cbdd802 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-0368da16ae973391\"></a>\n### HQ1492: an explicit request to obtain the reported Flight 77 message\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-hq1492-recording-request-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e03f41cfc3d74faaee3b).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 0368da16ae973391a7fd8e3fea8f04e6c198c76afe6435e9d34cd653a4a67820 -->\n# HQ1492: an explicit request to obtain the reported Flight 77 message\n\nA newly read FBI-form unit, **HQ1492**, directs the Washington Field Office to **obtain a recording** of a message attributed in the intake text to **“TODD REUBEN,”** described as a **Flight 77** passenger. This is a more specific acquisition target than the previously read **WF334** direction to contact someone about message contents.\n\n**The document records a request and assignment—not completed collection, recovered audio, confirmed cellular use, caller identity or a final result.** Its relationship to WF334 remains unverified. The two spellings, dates, control labels and differently worded instructions remain separately preserved.\n\n## Exact new source unit\n\n[Public reproduction, physical 57–59](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=57): production footers **000000753–755**. These three full-size page faces were newly read on **November 2, 2026**. The held source is a **73-page, 2,997,662-byte** third-party reproduction of FBI-form records, acquired **2026-10-27T13:40:38.310907+00:00**, SHA-256 `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`.\n\nThis is not an independently authenticated FBI master, native intake database or complete production. No new PDF was downloaded. Source images/full tip/contact/network-address/personnel/signature fields remain outside the public derivative. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-84beedb1d82f89b46a08) gives source/image hashes, exact scopes and reused records.\n\n## What the pages actually say\n\n[Physical 57, Event, footer 000000753](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=57), reports a **“CELL PHONE CALL”** from **“TODD REUBEN, PASSENGER ON FLIGHT 77”**, a **saved message**, and possible useful background noise. Those are reported allegations. There is no recording, transcript, authenticated speaker/flight or carrier determination in this unit. “Cell phone” in a tip is not an engineering finding distinguishing cellular from an installed aircraft telephone. The background-noise description is a possibility, not an acoustic result.\n\n[Physical 58, footer 000000754](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=58), marks **Lead Required? YES**. [Physical 59, Set Lead 1, footer 000000755](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=59), specifies **HQ1492**, **WFO / Washington, DC**, assignment **09/15/2001 at 6:10 PM**, and an instruction to contact a masked party **“AND OBTAIN RECORDING OF MESSAGE LEFT BY PASSENGER OF FLIGHT #77. MAY HAVE BACKGROUND NOISE.”**\n\nThis creates precise targets: the actual lead response/contact interview and disposition; any submitted or collected media, evidence inventory/receipt/barcode, copy/transcription/examination and analytical finding. The directive itself does not prove that an agent contacted anyone, a recording existed or was acquired, or any analysis succeeded. No completed result appears within these three faces; that is not proof the FBI failed to follow up or that no result exists elsewhere.\n\n## Preserve the fields and comparisons\n\n| Field / source | HQ1492, newly read | WF334, prior reading |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Reported name | **TODD REUBEN**, p57 Event | **TODD RUBEN**, p68 Event |\n| Reported flight | **77** | **#77** |\n| Information Received | **09/11/2001, 7:49 AM**, p57 | **09/11/2001, 7:49 PM**, p68 |\n| Header date | **09/16/2001**, p57 | **12/15/2001**, p68 |\n| Event Date / Time | **Both blank**, p57 | **09/11/2001 / time blank**, p69 |\n| Assignment | **09/15/2001, 6:10 PM**, p59 | **09/12/2001, 7:20 AM**, p70 |\n| Task | **Obtain recording**, p59 | Contact regarding contents of answering-machine message, p70 |\n| Typed control | **HQ1492**, p57/p59 | **WF334**, p68/p70 |\n| Handwritten bottom notation | Read as **HQ3060**, p57 | Previously read as **WF8406**, p68 |\n\nThe [earlier WF334 report](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6e9ce8fa287fa4410241bc8fba303cefd6476467/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf334-recording-lead-2026-11-02/README.md) supplies its exact source/field pins. The [court animation context](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2f78618d88ebcbd3e91811e9ba17f6457a6027ef/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf334-static-context-2026-11-02/README.md) contains the spelling **Reuben, Todd** as presentation text; independent underlying origin of the accounts is not established.\n\nThese are **different, unjoined records**. The matching minute and different AM/PM markers are preserved, but neither intake-receipt field is authenticated as the time a message was left. No AM-to-PM correction, common-clock chronology, processing-delay calculation, post-crash call conclusion or same-message assumption is made. Header, receipt, event and assignment fields retain distinct roles. A native creation/edit/import/routing history and original submission would test their relationship.\n\nSimilarly, handwritten notations do not establish aliases or replacement controls. Their writers, dates and functions remain unknown. Neither two typed controls nor four typed/handwritten appearances establish two or four calls. Similar allegations, source copies and handling stages are not independent corroboration of wrongdoing.\n\n## Intake and routing context\n\nPhysical 57 records **To:WFO**, **From:COUNTERTERRORISM**, case **265D-HQ-1348101 (PENDING)**, **Method of Contact:Written**, source label **INTERNET TAR - 618**. These labels identify source-record/routing targets, not authentication of an internet submission or caller. **PENDING** is printed source text, not a verified present case status. Masked parties and omitted network/contact identifiers are not reconstructed or republished.\n\nThe name and alleged-flight/message similarities make HQ1492 a candidate to cross-reference with WF334 and the earlier family-canvass attribution account. They do not prove identity equivalence, a distinct verified recipient, an additional real call, a specific carrier row, or a refutation of that canvass. Misidentification, duplicated or inaccurate tips, earlier/misattributed messages, inconclusive follow-up and a genuine relevant message remain untested possibilities. Original submissions, actual dispositions, message/custody and carrier/session/canvass joins are the discriminating records—including negative and inconclusive findings.\n\n## Actual work and limits\n\nTwo new exact-name official-domain queries and a bounded held-index check yielded no usable original follow-up locator. Generic/unrelated results were not opened as evidence. One index-schema assumption was wrong and was corrected in a preserved local addendum; no text miss was promoted to source-wide absence. The steel reuse check confirmed already completed routes and known photos, so those searches were not repeated or published as new.\n\nThe subsequent **16-page contact sheet** was navigation only. It exposed this record missed by the earlier narrow text/report checks. Only **three full faces**, 57–59, were newly read in detail. This is not a full 73-page census or independent transcription of every other tip. It demonstrates why a text-index miss must not be treated as proof of absent source content. Other contact-sheet material remains navigation-only, not adopted historical findings.\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e793ee8e1ddb859cbdb5) contains five related analyst entries about this one unit. [verify.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2af115e33cdb5818afb9) checks declared source/image/derivative bytes, manually entered locators, exclusions and preserved predecessor; it does not independently verify the pixel reading, tip, voice, caller, aircraft, cellular technology, clock, custody, disposition or historical cause. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3d24b76bbea6fd95abc1) states exactly what ran.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8d563dd2b3b26de75dfc) retains all five tracks and 18 requirements, the original HQ1492/source-submission/recording/disposition targets and previous WF334/serial3255/print/engineering targets. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-02ab8d888e9d68d50db1) and the actual additive [Git text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2131801a83345a14e9e5) preserve revision accountability. No original-plan criterion or whole investigation is completed by this reading or publication. Prior conflicting records and source bytes remain unchanged.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 0368da16ae973391a7fd8e3fea8f04e6c198c76afe6435e9d34cd653a4a67820 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-19e41c750f30f8e9\"></a>\n### May-family relays: the interview-request chain and preserved source differences\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-may-family-relays-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-15316a6617a3c876fd86).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 19e41c750f30f8e98f12e6a4992a2d652f9eb12bf59181eab2b8d649335e5e7e -->\n# May-family relays: the interview-request chain and preserved source differences\n\nThe newly read records locate a specific **Las Vegas family-interview and response trail**. A September 11 Dallas memorandum directs Las Vegas to interview Ron May and report information **positive or negative**. A separate **DL99** intake directs Dallas to prepare an interview request. Neither is the completed interview, a returned result or a native carrier record.\n\nBoth accounts relay information through **Jane Allen, American Airlines' Vice President for Flight Services**. **They are not independent interviews or independent confirmation of a call.** Both say approximately **6:05 Pacific time**. No 6:45 or 40-minute discrepancy survives full-page reading; the preliminary thumbnail guess was ours and is rejected, not preserved as historical evidence.\n\nThe memorandum also describes Flight 77 as having **“crashed into the World Trade Towers.”** The held official staff report describes its impact at the **Pentagon**. Both descriptions remain separately sourced and unchanged. Their difference does not establish why the memorandum used that wording, who knew what when, or that the family call was fabricated.\n\n## Exact new source units\n\n[Physical 53–54](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=53), production footers **000000741–742**, are the Dallas memorandum dated **09/11/2001** and its lead page. [Physical 60–62](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=60), footers **000000756–758**, are **DL99**, header **09/18/2001**, with event/lead continuations. All **five full faces** were newly read on **November 2, 2026**. Earlier contact-sheet views were navigation only.\n\nThe unchanged public mirror is **73 pages**, **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`, acquired **2026-10-27T13:40:38.310907+00:00**. It is a **third-party reproduction of FBI-form records**, not an authenticated FBI master/native intake database, complete production, original family interview or carrier event file. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f86f92c0c1e7f1b4a9a9) gives source/image pins and exclusions. No new PDF download, public query, OCR or audio analysis occurred.\n\n## The relay chain and actual requested work\n\n[Physical 53, Details](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=53), says Dallas received information from Allen, who said Ron May had called her. The memorandum says May **“apparently”** told Allen he had received a call from his daughter **Renee May**, a Flight 77 attendant. [Physical 60–61, Event](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=60), attributes information to Allen and describes Ron May and his wife receiving their daughter's call. Both relay six reported hijackers, movement toward the rear, attempted cockpit access and a line going dead. These remain **reported call descriptions**, not independently identified people, authenticated disconnection causes or verified carrier/device/service facts.\n\n[Physical 54, Set Lead1](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=54), directs **Las Vegas** to contact and interview Ron May and send **“information, positive or negative”** to Counterterrorism, New York, Washington Field and Dallas. Other addressees receive **“Read and clear”** instructions. Those office-specific tasks are not interchangeable: read-and-clear does not cancel the Las Vegas interview direction, prove case closure or supply a completed result.\n\n[Physical 61](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=61) marks **Lead Required? YES** and says Las Vegas covers the matter. [Physical 62, DL99 assignment/task](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=62), records **09/11/2001 at 7:30 PM** and directs **“PREPARE EC REQUESTING INTERVIEW OF RON MAY FATHER OF AA FLT 77 FLIGHT ATTENDANT RENEE MAY.”** An instruction to prepare a request is distinct from preparing/sending/receiving it, conducting the interview and returning its findings. No completed EC/receipt/interview/disposition is supplied by these five faces.\n\nExact underlying targets are the original airline/parent contacts and notes, Dallas EC/request and dispatch/receipt, Las Vegas interview/report/attachments and response—including negative or inconclusive information—and the native control/routing/disposition history. No contact, new request or fee was authorized or made here.\n\n## Preserve times without forcing a clock or call match\n\n| Source field | Printed value / wording |\n| --- | --- |\n| Memorandum header, p53 | **09/11/2001** |\n| Memorandum Details, p53 | **about 6:05 a.m., pacific time, 9/11/01** |\n| DL99 header, p60 | **09/18/2001** |\n| DL99 Information Received, p60 | **09/11/2001, 3:25 PM** |\n| DL99 Event narrative, p60 | **AROUND 6:05 PACIFIC TIME** |\n| DL99 Event Date/Time, p61 | **09/11/2001 / 6:05 AM** |\n| DL99 assignment, p62 | **09/11/2001 at 7:30 PM** |\n| Reused staff-report p31 | Attempt **9:11 A.M.**; connection **9:12 A.M.**, citing note 260 |\n\nThe approximate forwarded Pacific-time statements, unlabelled event/receipt/assignment clocks and later call entries have different source roles. No timezone is supplied here for unlabelled fields, and no silent conversion, controlling value, calibrated delay, exact event order or native-row identity is accepted. Original timing bases, carrier dictionary/clock, intake history and family interview are still needed. The later staff entry is not the underlying log.\n\nDL99 is the typed control. Its case is **265D-NY-280350-DL (PENDING)**; a bottom notation is read as **DL666**. The memorandum lists **265D-NY-280350**, **265D-WF-222811**, **265D-HQ-1348101**. A faint handwritten serial-like notation on physical 53 is not confidently transcribed; no value is adopted. Handwriting functions/aliases and PENDING's current relevance are unverified. No contact numbers, masked staff identities or private profiles are reproduced or reconstructed.\n\n## Preserve the impact-site conflict and contrary context\n\n[Memorandum physical 53, opening Details](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=53), describes the attendant aboard American Airlines Flight 77 **“just before it crashed into the World Trade Towers.”** The [official archived staff report, printed/physical34](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=34), says American Airlines Flight 77 crashed into the **Pentagon**. The memorandum's words are not replaced with the later description.\n\nThe [same staff report, p31](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=31), also describes earlier airline/FAA uncertainty about which aircraft struck the towers. That is **later reported context**, not independent proof of why this specific memorandum used its phrase. Early confusion, misreporting, copying, a different underlying account or another explanation remain untested; no one is selected. Original upstream contacts and memo drafting/transmission history would discriminate. This mismatch does not invalidate every relayed call detail or establish deliberate deception, a changed aircraft history or a concealed recording.\n\nStaff p31 also retains uncertainty about whether rearward movement meant passengers or crew. Its account of the mother and the relays' references to the father/parents are not silently collapsed into a single verified recipient/conversation. Original interviews, carrier/session records and canvass inclusion rules are needed to test which reports describe which events.\n\n## Reuse the existing interview citation honestly\n\nPreviously held [staff-report physical94, notes260–262](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=94), cites **FBI “American Airlines Airphone Usage,” September 20, 2001** for the call entries and **“FBI report of investigation, interview of Ronald and Nancy May, Sept 12, 2001”** in note261. Note262 separately cites an airline-employee interview and January 20, 2004 QFR/email response. These are **existing citations reused as locators**, not newly acquired original interviews, usage logs, emails or source authentication.\n\nThe staff PDF has **121 pages**, **6,760,035 bytes**, SHA-256 `9671b7afe9a45928dcbe053e567b7f830876bc31e32a1d221b39fa59493d5bbb`, captured **2026-10-28T00:16:15.117345+00:00** from the official National Archives URL. Previously read pages **31/34/94** were reused; they are not new reading/discovery counts. No fresh aircraft-impact or recorder test was performed, and the technical owner's work remains separate.\n\n## Verification and unresolved requirements\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2d0727b3c27ded805e29) preserves five related analyst entries, not five confirmations or a count of calls/hijackers. [verify.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-feeaa4837444fd058e6c) checks declared source/raster/body identities, manual source locators/values, exact predecessor preservation and all 18 TODOs; it does not independently transcribe pixels, authenticate a caller, family interview, aircraft, service, clock, carrier event, custody or response. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5e860a61821e8587167b) records actual modes.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8a19c22763b054f432a7) carries the specific original interview/request/response/clock/impact-wording targets and all five tracks and 18 requirements forward. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5a6c42281dccb9a3efde) and the actual additive [text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7a9b75483590f7d92584) preserve accountability. Original records, agreements, source conflicts and earlier versions remain unchanged. No original-plan criterion or whole investigation is completed by this source comparison or publication.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 19e41c750f30f8e98f12e6a4992a2d652f9eb12bf59181eab2b8d649335e5e7e -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-659e757a9dc5e1b4\"></a>\n### May interview: first page located in an already-held official release\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-may-official-counterpart-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-603d3db057cc42ad7298).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 659e757a9dc5e1b41d76346f301d71f6cd379ff8cb042e1cf79c63be2c072c00 -->\n# May interview: first page located in an already-held official release\n\nResearch date: November 2, 2026, America/New_York. Verification receipts may carry November 3 UTC. This is a telephone operational-record follow-up, not a new witness interview or a finding about conspiracy.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe first page of the June 2002 Nancy and Ronald May interview is **already held in the official FBI PDF**, physical page **73**, production footer **000000769**, printed page **1**. Its investigation field reads **06/05/2002**; its transcription field reads **06/06/2002**. It says an assistant U.S. attorney from the **Eastern District of Virginia** was present. These are statements and fields in the released report, not independent authentication of the interview, participants or dates. [Official first page](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=73)\n\nThe earlier 73-page reproduction remains unchanged: its physical page 70/footer **000000768** is followed by physical page 71/footer **000000770**, printed continuation page **2**. Locating 769 in a different entity does not insert it into that reproduction, explain the selection/redaction history, or prove that an agency removed a page. The [preceding report](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/56e7780d85b9947de12f36dfe614ac1794d3ff78/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02/README.md) described a gap in that particular held copy. It must no longer be read as though the first-page component is unlocated across all our holdings. [Mirror continuation](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=71)\n\n## New source comparison\n\n| Record / source | Physical PDF page; footer; printed page | What is actually observed | Limit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| September 12, 2001 Las Vegas response, third page; official | 72; 000000747; 3 | Four receiving-office entries: Dallas, New York, Washington Field and Counterterrorism, each instructed to **Read and Clear**. Header reference is **265D-NY-280350**. | A routing instruction, not proof of dispatch, receipt, execution, global case closure, or a recording's disposition. |\n| June 2002 May interview, first page; official | 73; 000000769; 1 | Investigation **06/05/2002**, transcription **06/06/2002**, file **265A-NY-280350**; EDVA assistant U.S. attorney reported present. | Interview and transcription are different date roles. These dates are not a contradiction merely because they differ. Keep **265A** distinct from the response's **265D**; no reason for the designations is inferred. |\n| June 2002 May continuation; official | 74; 000000770; 2 | Continuation date **06/05/2002**. Reports Nancy took notes and wrote down supplied airline telephone numbers during the call. Also reports one-minute-or-less duration and a background male voice she believed was another crew member. | Recollections in an interview report, not recovered notes, recorded audio, measured duration or independent speaker identification. |\n| Same-numbered continuation; mirror | 71; 000000770; 2 | The selected note-taking, duration and background-voice passages agree in their reported substance with official page 74. | Same-family / related-document content is not a new independent witness or a second independently authenticated call. No whole-page byte-equivalence claim. |\n| Next May continuation; official | 75; 000000771; 3 | Continuation date **06/05/2002**; reports attempted further contact without a conversation. | Identifying portions remain masked. This unit does not join the attempt to a particular phone event, the workplace report, or any recovered recording. |\n| Next official page / stop boundary | 76; 000000827 | Different record and footer, not the mirror's workplace footer 772. | Unrelated content excluded; page 77 not inspected. This is not a finding that 772 is absent from every release. |\n\nSources: [official 72](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=72), [73](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=73), [74](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=74), [75](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=75), and [mirror 71](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=71). Source byte hashes, acquisition times and reading scope are in [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c7ea8d12c0264f27c5a2). Page numbers here are one-based physical PDF pages, not production-footer numbers.\n\n### Different redactions and coverage remain separate\n\nOfficial page 74 and mirror page 71 share footer **000000770**, but they are not interchangeable page images. The official copy masks airline-employee identifying fields that are visible in the reproduction; excluded personal portions also differ in coverage/redaction. We do not fill the official masks from the mirror or reproduce those personal portions. Shared report wording and footer do not establish the complete copying, review or release history. A release/version manifest or authoritative page-accounting record is still needed to test why the forms differ.\n\n### What the notes reference does—and does not—supply\n\nBoth selected continuations report that Nancy took notes during the call and wrote down the airline numbers. **Neither selected passage says those notes were given to the FBI.** No actual note set, evidence item, receipt, transfer, preservation decision or examination result was recovered in this unit. The first-page EDVA participation statement supplies an additional office to check for existing interview-related records; it does not establish that that office received the notes, created a particular record, or retains it now. No contact or request was made.\n\n## Conflicting records and remaining joins\n\n1. **Mirror workplace report:** the preceding reading of mirror page 73/footer **000000772** prints investigation **06/10/2001**, transcription **06/28/2002**, and a **09/11/2001** narrative. These values remain unchanged and unresolved. This unit did not locate or adopt an official counterpart to that report; the June 5/6 family-interview fields are from a different record and cannot correct or authenticate it. Its reported unanswered call / no answering machine or voicemail remains a report, not a recovered message or native caller-ID log. [Prior assessment](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/56e7780d85b9947de12f36dfe614ac1794d3ff78/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02/README.md); [mirror 73](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=73).\n2. **Earlier response timing:** the previously examined Dallas relay's **6:05 a.m. Pacific** and official September 12 response's **6:13 a.m., no printed zone**, remain source-specific observations. This new first page does not independently clock the call or choose between those accounts. [Preserved holdings and limits](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/56e7780d85b9947de12f36dfe614ac1794d3ff78/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02/HOLDINGS-CHAIN.md).\n3. **Pickup / HQ1492 / WF334 / HQ366:** no new collector identity, callback result, media item, receipt, return response or completed disposition was located. The first page and routing page do not establish a common recording, alias, caller, recipient or evidence item across these controls. Earlier differing names, AM/PM entries, dates, assignments and NO flag remain in the [unchanged prior record](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/56e7780d85b9947de12f36dfe614ac1794d3ff78/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02/OBSERVATIONS.json).\n\n## A limitation in our own search method\n\nThe existing ordinary-text indexes for official September parts 01, 02 and 08 were searched for exact date/footer patterns and the already public May names. Only the May-name query returned the useful part-02 page-73 locator. The exact **769** footer and **06/05/2002** date patterns did not match those indexes, even though both are visible on page 73. An exact-text miss therefore cannot establish that a page or record is missing. This is a demonstrated limit of our navigation method, not evidence that the agency hid the image or altered the underlying record. [Search metadata](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d1830aba1d5a6d4e2b93).\n\n## Reading, preservation and verification limits\n\nThis unit inspected **five selected official page faces (72–76)** and **one reused mirror face (71)**. It did not read every body in the 78- or 73-page entities, recover hidden text, reconstruct masked identities, download another copy, repeat the completed pickup/provider searches, or inspect original notes/audio/native phone data. The already-held September response pages 70–71 and mirror workplace/continuation readings outside these six faces are reused prior assessments, not newly tested here.\n\nOriginal PDFs, earlier publications and conflicting observations remain unchanged. The new report is an additive derivative with a [revision diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-157bec17de527546c66d), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5134c5e81bd405b3e488), [method](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d338b99286fb8d50a6cd), and [open inputs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-589a70bde0d08e0a3845). Verification checks source/bundle bytes and reproduces the declared index matches; manual image readings remain explicitly manual. It does not authenticate the call or interview, identify a collector, establish misconduct, or complete the five-track original-records goal. The most useful next evidence is the actual note set and its provenance, an authoritative interview/version inventory, and any collection/receipt/return/disposition documents that explicitly join the recording controls.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 659e757a9dc5e1b41d76346f301d71f6cd379ff8cb042e1cf79c63be2c072c00 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-c5c27cdaec790f60\"></a>\n### May-family response status: a released September 12 record is already held\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-may-response-qualification-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a81e4561d3839e680ebf).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY c5c27cdaec790f6078ea486b32bf351ed1591aed8d3ec3813310b631555653fd -->\n# May-family response status: a released September 12 record is already held\n\nThis is an **additive status qualification** to [the relay/request review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6d775a5c70c1f7793dde9a2200d5c456e2779883/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-may-family-relays-2026-11-02/README.md). **We already hold an official released September 12, 2001 Las Vegas-to-Dallas communication reporting a meeting with Ronald and Nancy May and a local covered disposition.** It was acquired, read and [published in the October 31 review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/fb0d56eeaa07cfc9348306d1cedbcbea059fc5c8/investigation/broader-evidence/fbi-keyton-acis-originals-2026-10-31/README.md). It must not remain classified as a wholly missing May-family interview/response category.\n\nThe parent review correctly says its five selected relay/request faces do not themselves supply the completed result. Broader TODO wording about obtaining the family report and Las Vegas response needs this holdings qualification. **The response document is held; underlying notes/audio, exact file-version/serial joins, carrier data and independent authentication remain separate gaps.** This does not rewrite prior sources or claim a new download.\n\n## Exact held record and actual source content\n\n[Official FBI September part02, physical 70–71](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=70), production footers **000000745–746**, is dated **09/12/2001**, **To: Dallas / International Terrorism**, **From: Las Vegas / Squad 8**. It expressly references **265D-NY-280350 Serial 79** and lists the same NY/WF/HQ case families as the new relay memorandum.\n\n[Physical 70, Details](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=70), says agents met **RONALD and NANCY MAY** on **September 12, 2001**. It records Nancy's account of a call from her daughter Renee at **“6:13 a.m.”** on **September 11, 2001**, reporting six hijackers and movement toward the rear, after which Nancy was asked to contact the airline. **No timezone is printed for 6:13.** The named interviewees appear openly in this released body; masked agent names are not reconstructed or filled from another source.\n\n[Physical 71](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=71), says Ronald then contacted American Airlines with the information Nancy received, that neither had additional information to report, and **“No further investigation by Las Vegas at this time, this lead should be considered covered.”** Preserve **by Las Vegas**, **at this time** and **this lead**: this is not entire-case closure, a finding that no other office acted, or independent verification of the call's carrier/device/clock/voice.\n\nThese passages are a released **interview/response account**, not merely a request to interview. They report a completed meeting and local handling status; we have not independently established the meeting from native notes, nor identified raw audio, a signed separate closure order or all later activity. Do not invent a requirement that only an unredacted native file counts as a held record, and do not promote a released narrative to empirical carrier validation.\n\n## Preserve the clocks and the source chain\n\n| Record | Printed time / source role |\n| --- | --- |\n| Parent memorandum physical 53 | **about 6:05 a.m., pacific time**; airline-to-FBI relay |\n| DL99 physical60/61 | **AROUND 6:05 PACIFIC TIME**; event field **6:05 AM** |\n| Official response physical 70 | **6:13 a.m.**, no printed timezone; reported family interview account |\n\nAll values remain unchanged. No controlling time, unprinted timezone, clock conversion, exact elapsed difference or native-row association is accepted. A reported family account and relays based on that family account are not independent confirmations or extra calls. The response distinguishes **Nancy receiving** the call and **Ronald forwarding** information to the airline; preserve those roles rather than flattening all versions into one recipient statement. Native timing bases, original notes, carrier/session/clock and canvass records would test the joins.\n\nThe response's typed **Serial 79** is a concrete retrieval key. The earlier memorandum has matching subject/routing/case context, but its faint handwritten serial-like notation remains **unadopted/uncertain**. We do not force that glyph from the expected answer or declare a unique request-to-response/version join. Native serial/index/dispatch/receipt records would establish that mapping.\n\nThe previously held staff report's **note 261** cites a September12 Ronald/Nancy May FBI interview. This held communication is consistent with that date/participants and supplies an interview account; exact identification of the edition/file the staff used remains unverified. The underlying interview record category is partially satisfied by the official released report; raw notes/media/carrier and source-version requirements remain open. The parent report's separate WorldTradeTowers/Pentagon description conflict and agreement of its two 6:05 relay bodies are unchanged.\n\n## Source provenance, revision and acceptance\n\nThe official PDF has **78 pages**, **5,561,167 bytes**, SHA-256 `055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51`, acquired **2026-10-31T22:04:24.920527+00:00**. Prior two source rasters were reused and re-viewed; no new PDF/image download, public query, OCR, audio/ASR or technical-owner experiment occurred. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ab00cb8a06d8c5374c3e) records exact page/footer/image/earlier-publication pins and limits. Official hosting supports release provenance, not independent historical authentication of every assertion.\n\nInitial raster-generation receipts said pending when created. Later final reading/publication records supersede that initial work-status cue; pending on an old receipt is not proof the source is still unread. Our qualification corrects a holdings/status omission, not historical evidence or an old witness statement.\n\nThe earlier public relay report and source bytes remain unchanged. This uniquely named candidate adds a source-status qualification and actual predecessor [text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a78d43b619146d506bf8); it does not overwrite the old report. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ef6a97905e88965a9e7c), [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3d90cba0b9f0a13b914e), [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3680a4069f27536e05dc) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d052f1b9a74d5bca0f90) distinguish held documents, source claims and unperformed tests. Four related entries are not independent corroboration. Checks cover bytes/manual locators/preservation, not independent source transcription or call authentication.\n\nA held released interview/response component is now explicitly recognized. **No whole TEL01–TEL04 requirement or original five-track goal is completed**: native carrier/operator/office/clock/canvass/media/custody and other required originals/tests remain unresolved. The qualification is proposed on a separate non-overwriting review branch/PR against the parent relay branch, without merge or history rewrite.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY c5c27cdaec790f6078ea486b32bf351ed1591aed8d3ec3813310b631555653fd -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-27e08d91225ff52d\"></a>\n### Telephone originals: two note sheets and an operational lead-assignment trail\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-notes-lead-assignment-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9f6509ed952052c2a222).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 27e08d91225ff52daab3d6127ef2fc16c008a19475d97c184ebd1dbe8f1b9876 -->\n# Telephone originals: two note sheets and an operational lead-assignment trail\n\nOctober 31, 2026 Eastern / November 1 UTC. The [official FBI September interviews, part 06 of 08](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-06-of-08/view) supplies specific original-note and lead-completion targets. The evidence here consists of rendered agency records, not the underlying notes, carrier exports, original audio or native lead database. All eighteen original five-track requirements remain open/partial.\n\n## 1. A report says two contemporaneous note sheets were given to agents\n\n**Viewer pages 1–2**, internal pages 1–2, are an FD-302-style recipient interview with transcription date **09/11/2001**, file reference **265D-NY-280350**, and **REQ. #35-13** footers **000000598–000000599**. It describes two calls involving Peter Hanson.\n\n**Page 2, note-handoff paragraph**, says the recipient took **two sheets of notes during the two phone calls** and **provided those notes to the interviewing agents**. This is a concrete claim of an original-note handoff. The note sheets themselves, an evidence-item identifier, storage location, signed receipt and subsequent custody history were not acquired here. Do not assume a 1A location merely because other telephone records mention 1A material. These are described as the recipient's notes, distinct from an agent's interview notes and the typed FD-302.\n\nOther source distinctions matter:\n\n- Page 1 places the first call **sometime before 9:00 a.m.**, followed by a second **within a matter of minutes**. Those are recollections; no explicit zone or calibrated start/end pair is supplied in the adopted passages.\n- The recipient **believed** the caller was using a cellular telephone. The report records a supplied number but the public copy masks it. This is not verified service or a carrier-row join. The page-2 concern about a callback making the phone ring is another statement from the same account, not independent confirmation of the device.\n- Page 1 reports an immediate notification to **Easton Police Department**, including a named captain. The original police call, intake/incident log, any recording and any contemporaneous police notes are additional retrieval targets. No such notification record was obtained in this pass.\n- Page 2 explicitly leaves the abrupt ending uncertain: the recipient did not know whether the caller hung up or the phone malfunctioned. Neither explanation, nor a physical cause, is established here.\n\nThe most useful next comparison is the actual two note sheets against the typed report, original interview material, police notification records and call-specific carrier data. The sheets could preserve earlier wording or timing, but their contents must not be invented from the report. Two sheets and two calls do not establish two independent witnesses or a complete network-attempt count. The masked recipient identity remains masked; unrelated personal/profile fields are excluded.\n\n## 2. PG1581 separates a newspaper-derived claim from an interview assignment\n\n**Viewer pages 13–15**, footers **000000259–000000261**, contain a Pittsburgh-to-Pittsburgh FBI communication dated **09/22/2001**. Its case ID is **265A-PG-69744 (PENDING)**; its synopsis and embedded **Information Control Form** identify **PG1581**. The printed title is **UNITED FLIGHT 93**, followed by **PFLP**. That second label is retained literally and unexpanded: its administrative meaning is not established here, and it does not by itself identify attackers, affiliation or responsibility. “Pending” is a historical printed status, not a verified current case status.\n\n| Source field/location | Printed value or description | Limit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Page 13, communication date | **09/22/2001** | Not the date of the in-flight call or proof of dispatch/receipt. |\n| Page 13, method and information-received fields | **Written; 09/16/2001; 12:00 AM** | Native field meanings, entry history, clock precision and defaults remain unknown. |\n| Page 13, Event narrative | A **September 16 Pittsburgh Post-Gazette article** is said to describe a **13-minute conversation** involving Todd Beamer and a GTE supervisor. | An attributed newspaper statement, not an independent FBI duration measurement. The actual article was not acquired or read here. |\n| Page 14, event fields | **09/11/2001; 12:00 AM** | Retain the printed time. Do not treat it as an independently measured midnight call, silently correct it or declare it a default. |\n| Pages 13–14, priority/lead fields | **IMMEDIATE; Lead Required: YES** | Priority and an instruction are not proof of notification, interview execution or completion. |\n| Page 15, assignment | **PG1581; 09/21/2001 at 1:40 AM**, Pittsburgh | An assignment field, not a calibrated call clock or completed-interview return. |\n| Same page, instruction | **“IF NOT ALREADY DONE”**, locate/interview the masked GTE supervisor regarding the Beamer call. | The qualifier does not establish that no earlier interview had occurred. Do not infer a ten-day failure or ignored witness from the dates alone. |\n\nThese different date/time roles remain side by side. No preferred event time, correction, source default or explanation for the document/assignment ordering has been selected. The two midnight labels, assignment, priority and newspaper-derived narrative are not independent corroborations of a historical call. This form also does not resolve the various duration and holding-period descriptions preserved in earlier operator-record reviews; those require recording, phase, clock and source joins.\n\n### Exact cross-references to pursue\n\nThe page-13 Event paragraph cites **GTE Airfone Serial 348, case 265A-NY-280350**. Its continuation on page 14 separately refers to **Serial #8**, without reprinting an explicit case namespace alongside that reference. Preserve the two references rather than assigning both automatically to one file or assuming their contents agree.\n\nNext targets: the actual referenced serials and their enclosure/custody records; PG1581's native intake/assignment/edit history; its completion, clearance, deconfliction or return record; the actual newspaper article; and case/control-title records needed to understand the printed context. A bounded check of one already held 73-page public mirror's existing text index did not locate PG1581 or Serial 348. That is an index-locator result, not proof the records are missing, withheld or destroyed. No cross-reference body was recovered or validated by that check.\n\nDo not identify the masked supervisor or agent by borrowing a name from another release. Similar subject matter alone does not establish that a previously inspected interview is the completion of PG1581. The source communication, embedded form, continuation and lead page belong to one documentary chain; they are not four independent witnesses.\n\n## Preservation, reading scope and open tests\n\nThe official item advertises **516,162 PDF bytes** and exposes **15 viewer pages**. Five distinct source pages were inspected: **1, 2, 13, 14 and 15**; pages **3–12** remain unread in this pass. Eight unchanged browser screenshots were retained locally. Two separate local diagnostic enlargements repeat visible page-13 pixels only, using nearest-neighbour scaling, to read the Event references and case caption. They add no detail and are not OCR, generative enhancement, hidden-layer recovery or independent evidence. The original captured bytes remain unchanged.\n\n[SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f2625e8ef5d115c2e37e) records actual page/paragraph/footer locators, captured-view hashes, preservation times and diagnostic methods. The hashes identify browser images, **not a native FBI PDF, original note, audio master or authenticated case database**. No PDF was requested or obtained; no audio, note sheet, native carrier table or lead-return record was acquired. No waveform, device, row-level call-count, voice or independent-clock test was performed.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-240df0a5dea4e4269d90) retains the original-note, police, carrier and PG1581 dependencies with the full FAA/telephone/recorder/materials/steel plan. Raw images, contact/DOB/profile details, signatures, masked identities, private case material and correspondence are outside this public payload. No outreach, new request, fee, filing, mailbox access, experiment, source alteration, private push or history rewrite occurred. Earlier source records and published assessments remain unchanged; this is record-acquisition progress, not a completed substantive investigation or a conspiracy finding.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 27e08d91225ff52daab3d6127ef2fc16c008a19475d97c184ebd1dbe8f1b9876 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-1752be6522ace761\"></a>\n### Official telephone-release lead: recording labels and separate reporting channels\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-official-part03-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8f8564ee034e9b233848).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 1752be6522ace761f68cca9a93c331889985b2b97c7e6a241aaa9a36df8aac08 -->\n# Official telephone-release lead: recording labels and separate reporting channels\n\nResearch date: October 31, 2026, Eastern; public-source views and preservation extend into November 1 UTC. Scope: TEL01–TEL04. All original five-track acceptance requirements remain open.\n\nThe [FBI Vault September interviews, part 03 of 08](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-03-of-08/view) supplies two useful record-identification leads. Its Ong transcript header and the opening recorded conversation need separate descriptions. A separate Flight 93 report identifies a handwritten statement and an Airphone information relay. Neither is an acquired native recording, activity table or authenticated handwritten original.\n\n## 1. Preserve the transcript header beside its actual opening\n\n**Observed, viewer page 2:** an FD-302-style header prints **DL-336**, case **265D-NY-280350**, and transcription date **09/12/2001**. Its introductory paragraph describes a taped telephone conversation between Betty Ong and the American Airlines Southeast Reservation Center, identifying Winston and Vanessa and Flight 11. The paragraph states September 11, 2001 as today's date.\n\n**Observed, viewer page 3, internal page 2:** the continuation is headed Betty Ong and dated **09/11/2001**. The visible opening speaker states **12:28 p.m. Central Time**, identifies a corporate-security role, and introduces a conversation with Nydia Gonzalez about what occurred that morning. Gonzalez describes her operations-specialist role and an incoming flight-attendant call at approximately **8:20**; the visible passage does not assign that recollection a time zone.\n\n**Interpretation and limits:** the header's broad description and the opening's retrospective interview context are preserved side by side. Do not relabel the entire record, choose a controlling description, treat the 12:28 recording time as the in-flight call time, silently supply a zone to 8:20, or call this an authenticated native recording of Ong. Pages 4–10 were not read in this pass. They could contain further material relevant to the record's scope. Mapping DL-336 to the actual source recording, transcript segments and custody entries remains a TODO. The apparent difference in descriptions does not establish substitution, falsification or an error in the underlying audio.\n\nThe [previous SERO inventory review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/d5b279a04f2fe18b78548222aea75451bfa7f60a/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-sero-evidence-inventory-2026-10-31/README.md) preserves a separate September 13 memorandum's original-media inventory, roughly 8:20 call-start descriptions and reported four-minute recording limit. No byte, track, recording-session or calibrated-clock join between that inventory and DL-336 has been established. Similar names or subject matter do not make them the same recording or independent corroboration.\n\n## 2. Flight 93: a statement and a different Airphone relay\n\n**Observed, viewer page 11:** a report dated **9/11/01** bears **Reference Lead Control Number SF:62**, footer **REQ. #35-13**, and **000000156**. It describes interviewing a United employee at San Francisco International Airport. The narrative says a system aircraft-maintenance controller took a Flight 93 flight-attendant call at approximately **6:40 a.m.** The report describes **two male hijackers with knives**. It then says a handwritten statement was supplied and reproduces a statement beginning **0640 PST** at the **STARFIX Desk**. That is a typed representation of a statement, not the inspected handwritten original.\n\n**Separate reported channel, same page and continuation:** the lower page-11 paragraph describes information from Airphone that a passenger had called; it then introduces information relayed by that passenger. Viewer page 12, internal page 2, reports **three males**, **bombs and knives**, no injuries at that time, and a reported Pennsylvania location. Its header shows **265D-NY-280350** and **9/11/01**. It expressly says the interviewee had no further identifiable information on the weapons or explosives.\n\n**Preserve, do not reconcile:** retain the two-men/knives account beside the three-men/bombs-and-knives relay. These are differently attributed communications within a report; they are not established as simultaneous descriptions of one exchange. Neither headcount is selected as controlling. No weapon, explosive, location, caller identity or exact event clock has been independently verified here. The narrative's unqualified 6:40 and the reproduced statement's 0640 PST remain separate clock labels; no PST/PDT conversion or alignment to other flight records was performed. The report, its typed quotation and continuation are not three independent witnesses.\n\n**Concrete next records:** the original handwritten statement, its attachment/intake record, STARFIX/controller call records and recordings, and the underlying Airphone passenger/operator record and relay documentation. Those could test the timing, attribution, completeness and differences; they have not been acquired or tested in this pass.\n\n## Reading, preservation and access limits\n\nThe item advertises **2,119,910 bytes** and its viewer exposes **12 pages**. One request to its actually exposed PDF download link returned **HTTP 403**. No PDF binary, original response payload or PDF SHA-256 was obtained. The normal public Document/Pages viewer remained readable; no alternate binary route, header spoof, hidden asset, credential or gate workaround was used.\n\nFive distinct source-page views were inspected: cover 1; page 2; the visible upper portion of 3; page 11, including a fitted view; and page 12. The poor cover was not used to establish an evidence-custody receipt. Initial loading frames were not interpreted as blank or missing original pages. Page 11's fitted view exposed its lower relay paragraph and prevented treating its two accounts as necessarily one event. Small or cropped fields outside the adopted observations remain unverified.\n\nFour unaltered browser screenshots were retained locally with hashes in [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-712c9806c9a98fcdc6ea). **Their hashes identify captured viewer images, not a native FBI PDF or audio recording.** Raw screenshots, telephone/contact details, redacted identities, signatures and private case material are excluded from this public payload. Source-page paragraphs provide the locators; no artificial line numbers are attributed to scanned pages.\n\nThe finding is a traceable record-and-recording identification lead. It does not establish a conspiracy, foreknowledge, fabricated calls, explosives or a complete production. The original activity reports, carrier records, native recordings, clock definitions and custody joins remain [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b32f2fad556b0d84ec95). No agency contact, new request, fee, experiment, private push or source alteration occurred. Prior source records and published assessments remain unchanged.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 1752be6522ace761f68cca9a93c331889985b2b97c7e6a241aaa9a36df8aac08 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-7bb21f69292085bd\"></a>\n### Silent-input control failed; court speech was not transcribed\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-offline-reading-control-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-14c8d9b88406b154490e).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 7bb21f69292085bdf685f6b2eca09f48e0f8880faefbef3fbe2a2ffe11a8d3ba -->\n# Silent-input control failed; court speech was not transcribed\n\n**This is a test of our reading method, not a finding about 9/11.** The installed recognizer produced **“You” from ten seconds of all-zero audio samples**. That failed the predeclared control, so the planned court-audio passes were stopped. No words from the court audio were newly transcribed or authenticated.\n\n## What was actually tested\n\nOn November2,2026, a WAV containing160000mono samples at16000Hz/16bits was generated directly from320000zero bytes. A separate file inspection of that saved WAV confirmed every sample byte was zero, the header fields and the10second duration. WAV SHA-256: `ee7bea4232762775f8fce9b3e27e4d3948c8ac6a45a87ca769f703d6eed0b448`.\n\nOne local **whisper.cpp1.9.2 /base.en** pass used CPUonly, English,4threads/1processor, temperature0 and no temperature fallback. No initial prompt, desired words, grammar, VAD or translation was supplied. The OS process profile denied network; the permission probe returnedEPERM. Existing installed tools/weights were reused, with no download or source upload. [CONTROL-RESULT.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-671bc6e31936ad99bdb4) pins the exact engine/model/input/output hashes, command template, timing, options and observed outcome.\n\nInference exited0, but its text file contained `You` followed by a newline. **Successful execution and a passed control are different outcomes.** The frozen criterion required empty stripped text. The observed nonempty output therefore failed that criterion; it was not erased, excluded, retuned or rerun to obtain a pass.\n\n## What stopped, and what remains unknown\n\nThe source court archive was checked before and after the job. The intended Ong event/stream payload extraction and both speech passes were **never reached**. The only new derived audio was the synthetic silent WAV; the only inference directory was the silent-control run. No Flash/ActionScript was executed, no actual call was played or submitted to the recognizer, and no court-word timing, voice or source identity was measured.\n\nThe [preceding printed-passage comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a8b410fc96d29f50f9c134f87acb0822eedc8961/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-playback-text-comparison-2026-11-02/README.md) preserves the **I'm number five /Our number5**, speaker-label, cockpit-question and **Somebody/nobody** differences, with their agreements and alignment limits. This failed synthetic control supplies **no new reading of any of those passages**, selects neither printed account and changes no historical conclusion.\n\nOne false word on synthetic silence does not estimate the recognizer's speech-error rate or show that every transcript it generates is wrong. Conversely, repeating a plausible word is not independent authentication. A different engine/platform/configuration could behave differently; that was not tested. We did not alter this probe's settings, switch models or run additional controls after its failure. The result is a reason to keep machine text provisional, not a cause assigned to the historical source differences.\n\n## Reproduction and scope\n\n[reproduce_control.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-540b00837ee607e36a80) provides the control-only command with exclusive output creation, pinned engine/model checks, an explicit network-denial probe and no source-media input. Supply the matching existing engine and model paths; no automatic downloads or installation. The original full pipeline executed the documented call. This standalone wrapper was syntax-checked and compared to its options, **not rerun** after the frozen stop condition. Its WAV generator was separately checked in memory against the actual input bytes.\n\nThe observed engine binary SHA-256 is `40bca494d49af736058eb3f33cbcebaa020eacf6d0087b623f334946e1ab2128`; model SHA-256 `a03779c86df3323075f5e796cb2ce5029f00ec8869eee3fdfb897afe36c6d002`/147964211bytes. These identify the tested assets; they do not promise identical output on other installations. Public files include selected synthetic results and authored reproducibility material, excluding raw logs, machine transcript files, court audio, model weights and private case data.\n\nThe native session/CD/tape/copy/custody/segment records and independent source listening needed to test the printed differences remain missing. Existing FAA correction/disposition, telephone native/release/operator/recipient, recorder configuration/paired-output/clocks, materials specimen/calibration and steel preservation/attribution/review-delivery requirements remain open under their original criteria. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-478f2b4025caa77cddea) retains all18IDs. Neither this control nor publication completes those requirements.\n\n[CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9a039cd00d3011a676a1), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1429cd381a2b6820638b) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a377c2363af1f3482d85) separate the failed method control from successful preservation checks. The diff adds this methods note after a preserved copy of the preceding report; that report, its sources, all conflicting words and public history remain unchanged. No independent historical audit or main-branch adoption is claimed.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 7bb21f69292085bdf685f6b2eca09f48e0f8880faefbef3fbe2a2ffe11a8d3ba -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-a0c82e0e8d10d467\"></a>\n### A later operator interview identifies original notes and qualifies the reported counts\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-operator-notes-mfr-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9584efe7599de5da6b61).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY a0c82e0e8d10d467602650c077ae7530ed993fe0736d8e00c0003524ad40c501 -->\n# A later operator interview identifies original notes and qualifies the reported counts\n\nOctober 31, 2026, America/New_York; capture November 1 UTC. **TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** A newly inspected three-page public reproduction of a May 11, 2004 Commission interview memorandum identifies a concrete missing-record target: Jefferson's brief Post-it notes, reportedly held by the FBI. It also supplies an explicit qualification about reported passenger counts and another silent-line estimate. These are statements in a later interview record, not authenticated original notes or independently measured call events.\n\n## Source, provenance and reading scope\n\nThe [public reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886438/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-Todd-Beamer-Fdr-5-11-04-MFR-Lisa-Jefferson-416) labels the upload as a call transcript, but its actual body is headed **MEMORANDUM FOR THE RECORD**, dated **May 11, 2004**, prepared by **John Raidt**, Team **7**, and describes a briefing by Lisa Jefferson. The uploader is **9/11 Document Archive**, a third-party mirror. Neither the platform's AI-enhanced title/description nor its catalogue ranking establishes document type, truth or agency custodianship. The reproduced historical Commission Sensitive / Unclassified markings are retained as provenance; no classification or release-authority conclusion is inferred from them.\n\nAll three displayed pages were read in the normally accessible reader text and visible images. Five adopted viewport captures cover the three pages; a sixth captured page 3 while loading and is retained only as a diagnostic. The subsequent loaded page 3 is readable. A transient blank frame is not a blank original, deletion or missing-page finding. No login, free trial, download gate, hidden API or guessed asset route was used.\n\nThe browser DOM/text capture is **54,260 UTF-8 bytes**, SHA-256 **90ecfacf04cb7fdf9cd2a1fc339262efe43ff94aaeb32c3e1358fb1f6183264a**. That fingerprints a captured reader representation, including its fragmentation and interface material; it is not a native PDF or agency-master hash. Raw source text/images and incidental personal/interface details remain outside this public payload. [Source fingerprints](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8797a70f97e7f0ccbf8d), [exact printed-page/paragraph and captured-line pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-21cbbde05d74a6d7f587), [scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a62dff73105eda3baa3d).\n\n## Original notes: a specified form and reported holder\n\n**S1 printed page 3, Additional clarifications, second paragraph** says Jefferson made only a few basic notes on a small Post-it pad and that the FBI held them. The same passage reports her view that they would add little information. Preserve both parts; this is neither a recovered note nor an independent appraisal of its evidentiary value. The interview occurred in 2004 and does not prove present retention, completeness, original acquisition date or a particular evidence barcode. P02.\n\nThe already held [official FBI interview report, physical page 45](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=45), says notes, a typed event summary and a screen print were handed to the interviewing agent. That separately specifies attachment and receipt targets. It does not, without an item/copy/custody join, identify those notes as the same physical Post-it material described in 2004. A typed synopsis, a screen print, original notes and later recorded recollection remain distinct artifacts. No redacted identity is reconstructed. P03.\n\n**S1 page 3, first clarification** records uncertainty about whether the first operator, Johnson, took notes. Preserve that uncertainty. It does not establish either that she made none or that no such record survived. Obtain the individual originals, not a collective assumption about both operators. P04.\n\n## Counts: the memorandum adds a provenance qualification\n\n**S1 page 2, third paragraph** reports **10 in front / 27 in back / 5 flight attendants**, through an account attributed to the flight attendant. Its parenthetical note says the description reflects the flight manifest rather than contemporaneous distribution within the cabin. That is the memorandum's qualification; the actual manifest, initial notes and interviewer drafting basis are not attached or independently checked here. It cannot be treated as a verified explanation of every earlier count. P05.\n\nKeep the [earlier transcript reproduction](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886478/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-Todd-Beamer-Fdr-9-15-01-FBI-302-Transcript-UAL-SAC-Nick-Leonard-Re-Jefferson-Beamer-Call-419) beside it: viewer **5 / Bates M-NKA-00012173** reports **27 front / 10 back**, while viewer **10 / Bates M-NKA-00012178** reports **10 front / 27 back**. Neither allocation is selected, repaired or converted into measured seating positions. The shared total **37** is only arithmetic on reported numbers, not an authenticated manifest or independent headcount. P06.\n\n## Timing and information paths remain unjoined\n\n**S1 page 3, opening paragraph** reports a **15-minute** silent/open-line interval, followed by news of a crash and termination. The [earlier official operator account, physical pages 4–5](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-08-of-08/at_download/file#page=4) reports **20 minutes** of silent-open time and a separate **approximately 5-minute** later-contact estimate. The September follow-up reproduction, viewer **19–20 / Bates 12187–12188**, reports **about 10 more minutes** holding and news **about 10 minutes later**. These are separate estimates and phase descriptions. No sum, controlling endpoint, clock conversion or identification with billed duration is imposed. P07.\n\n**S1 page 1, notification/handoff paragraphs** describes the **Airplane Operations Surveillance Center (AOSC)** notifying authorities and an FBI connection remaining with AOSC while the operators spoke with the caller. This specifies a relay/bridge record target. It does not demonstrate an FBI recording, prove direct monitoring of every word or authenticate a particular communications leg. Preserve the prior reported lack of local recording capability alongside this reported relay path; different paths have not been joined or tested. P08.\n\n**S1 page 3, third clarification** distinguishes earlier events being recounted to the operator from events occurring during the call. The final clarification is explicitly tentative about another operator listening to a different passenger's call. Neither passage authenticates a clock, carrier assignment or recording of that separate call. They caution against treating all reported detail as simultaneously and independently overheard. P09.\n\n## Next originals and limits\n\nThe immediate targets are the individual original Post-it/other operator notes, attachment inventories and transfer receipts; original September 14 letter/synopsis and enclosures; interview notes/recording and draft/version records behind the 2004 memorandum; the actual manifest and source of its parenthetical qualification; and AOSC/FBI relay, bridge, watch-log and any recording/disposition records. Native carrier/operator identifiers, field definitions, clock rules, actual media and complete production/exhibit joins remain open. No new contact or request was sent.\n\nThe strongest limitation is source dependence: a 2004 staff memorandum recording one operator's recollection, a 2001 interview summary and a later transcript reproduction are different records, not necessarily independent measurements. Memory, source copying, wording, transcription, scope or other causes could matter; none is selected as a resolution. These observations do not establish fabricated calls, concealment, foreknowledge or attack participation. They identify records that can test those interpretations in either direction.\n\nThe separate September 14 letter was **not** recovered in this search. The new substantive advance is the actually inspected interview record's specified note form/holder, count qualification and phase/relay claims. Earlier originals, conflicting values, public history and shared registers remain unchanged. All original five tracks and 18 requirements remain open or partial; publication is not empirical completion or independent audit acceptance.\n\n[Comparison and discriminating records](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a4bad4f52acd24c7c4f7), [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-06cb9997232f9f0f9550), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e01859965e3c38b69386), [verification limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a0eb58e62c28fc578be9) and [additive text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-fc1adcc9f68bd57088a0) accompany these redundant public research notes. No raw privacy-marked source, full speech, contact/financial/access/signature data, private correspondence, litigation strategy or credentials are published. Prior [recording-index review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6e75761061f0bfa9148eb98a213aa4a24f1ad123/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-recording-index-2026-10-31/README.md) remains unchanged.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY a0c82e0e8d10d467602650c077ae7530ed993fe0736d8e00c0003524ad40c501 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-55f1fc90da422986\"></a>\n### FBI-hosted counterpart preserves the Flight 99 reading and engineering-record lead\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-operator-official-counterpart-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-821a2470b0276034cc59).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 55f1fc90da422986685fcaedfcb4c1214136ad2774f74b7cdb8a51d93b0297a1 -->\n# FBI-hosted counterpart preserves the Flight 99 reading and engineering-record lead\n\nThe already-held FBI release supplies a counterpart for the previously examined mirror: **physical 18–19 of part 02** visibly retain the **flight 99** recollection, screen-print/engineering passage and **serial 3255** citation. This strengthens the provenance of those selected passages. It is a second copy of a related report, **not independent corroboration that a call, print transfer or engineering analysis occurred**.\n\nThe referenced interview itself remains unacquired. The exact serial lookup returned this same held PDF, not the separate cited record. No original print, engineering receipt/result, recording or native session was recovered.\n\n## Sources and actual scope\n\nThe [FBI-hosted release](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=18) was acquired **October 31, 2026, 22:04:24 UTC**. It contains **78 pages**, **5,561,167 bytes**, SHA-256 **`055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51`**. This unit newly read complete page faces **18–19**, internal **1–2**, production footers **000000370–371**. It did not download the source again or establish its current HTTP availability.\n\nThe [earlier mirror, physical 23–24](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=23), has SHA-256 **`e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`**. Its previously inspected fields are retained in the [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6d9d2c9684c29602cf5bb570cbf38c46e09fd50d/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-first-operator-followup-2026-11-02/README.md). Shared case/date/footer and selected wording support a documentary-counterpart comparison; they do not authenticate a complete release/assembly chain or make the entities byte-identical.\n\nOnly nonpersonal independently visible fields are compared. Masked official names and contacts were **not filled from the more-visible mirror**. No whole-file read, new OCR, hidden-content extraction, audio/ASR, voice identification, native clock or carrier replication occurred. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5fb44ccd9a709f3e30f9) distinguishes new readings from reused context and source-entity hashes from historical authentication.\n\n## What the official page visibly supports\n\n| Field or passage | Official part 02 | Earlier mirror | Limit |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Case/date/footer | **265A-NY-280350-302**; investigation **06/05/2002**; transcription/dictation **06/11/2002**; footers **370–371** | Same selected labels | Documentary association, not original authorship/custody. |\n| Initial call receipt | **Approximately 8:40 a.m. Central**, physical 18, first substantive paragraph | Same reported estimate | Not calibrated call start or independent clock evidence. |\n| Recalled flight number | **United flight 99**, physical 18, final substantive paragraph | **United flight 99** | The recall qualification remains. Neither page says the screen displayed 99. |\n| Referenced interview | **265A-NY-280350-OUT, serial 3255**, physical 19, first paragraph | Same pointer | The citing document is not the cited serial. |\n| Administrative screen print | Reportedly made when the call disconnected; information **was to be passed** to engineering, physical 19, final paragraph | Same reported creation/intended action | Actual print, dispatch/receipt, analysis and result still missing. |\n\nThe **99** reading is visible in the agency-hosted page as well as the mirror; it is not merely a value introduced by our new summary or an adopted OCR line. The earlier [supervisor account, part 08 physical 4](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-08-of-08/at_download/file#page=4), reports **United Airlines Flight 93**. Both values remain with their source roles. Repetition in copies of a report does not independently establish what was spoken, which aircraft or native session was involved, or why the values differ.\n\nThe screen-print passage remains evidence of what the report says was made and intended. It is not the original print or completed engineering work. The visible serial reference provides a precise retrieval target but does not identify the held supervisor copy as serial 3255. One exact public query for the case/serial returned the same held part 02 entity; it supplied no separate original and was not followed by a redundant download.\n\n## What cannot be transferred across copies\n\nThe official personnel fields are masked, including positions involved in the earlier mirror’s surname-variation observation. **That observation remains mirror-specific.** This review neither independently confirms those names at the masked positions nor assigns an identity to an official blank. Source redaction differences are preserved without reconstructing what was withheld or asserting that a particular omission was improper.\n\nThe official first page also visibly carries an unclassified-information stamp dated **01-26-2007**. The interview/document fields say **June 2002**, while the collection filename contains **2001-09**. Preserve these distinct field/object roles. The stamp is not substituted for an interview, original creation or public-release date; the filename does not establish when every included document was created. No classification-law finding, later alteration, deletion or selected explanation follows from these labels.\n\n## Remaining records and evidentiary weight\n\nThe useful change is a stronger source-location/provenance anchor for selected nonpersonal wording, coupled with a clearer limit: it does not authenticate every unmasked field in the mirror or supply the cited interview. Multiple copies can share the same underlying statement and mistakes. They are not independent witnesses or measurements.\n\nNext discriminators remain the actual **serial 3255** with cover/continuations/enclosures and source-version association; the administrative print with field/session definitions; engineering dispatch/receipt/work order/result/disposition; original notes/media, caller/session and clock/custody joins. Existing **99/93**, timing/hold and mirror-only surname observations stay preserved and unresolved. No fabrication, deliberate alteration, concealment or historical cause is established.\n\nAll five tracks and 18 original criteria remain open or partial; prior actual analyses remain performed. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ea55fb172ab5df448a45) retains them. [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d788794976ef816535e2) contains four related source/provenance entries, not four independent confirmations. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-79cdd01e5c54b3a0a10d), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a0e5580b9c4425937eb0) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d5ec93e3507434a80264) distinguish source reading, preservation and publication from unperformed native tests. Raw PDFs/images/full interviews, contacts, signatures, masked identities and private material are excluded. Publication is not main-branch adoption or substantive goal completion.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 55f1fc90da422986685fcaedfcb4c1214136ad2774f74b7cdb8a51d93b0297a1 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-e9a3b30e010cabc2\"></a>\n### PG1012: a reported telephone story and an instruction to disregard it\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-pg1012-disregard-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-296aaf859d4775d9115b).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY e9a3b30e010cabc2de9c5e1f5cc11604d61fbca06c65c61c5b1dd3b948416698 -->\n# PG1012: a reported telephone story and an instruction to disregard it\n\nReview date: October 31, 2026, America/New_York; source captures November 1, 2026, 03:22–03:23 UTC.\n\nThe useful new record is an FBI information-control form that preserves both a relayed story about a Flight 93 passenger and a later instruction to disregard it. It also identifies a fax/control number and says an EC was drafted. These are concrete retrieval targets. The released form alone establishes neither the story's truth nor whether the instruction was justified. It is not evidence, by itself, of deliberate suppression.\n\n## Exact source and reading scope\n\n[Official FBI Vault, Interviews September 2001, part 06 of 08](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-06-of-08/view): viewer pages **7–9 of 15**, printed release footers **000000245–000000247**, request label **REQ. #35-13**, control **PG1012**. Page 7's communication is dated **09/20/2001**, Pittsburgh to Pittsburgh, case **265A-PG-69744 (PENDING)**, precedence **IMMEDIATE**. “PENDING” is the historical printed label, not a current case-status determination. Read all three selected pages; no claim to read the whole 15-page item in this unit.\n\nFive original browser screenshots were preserved unchanged and hashed, with two separate visible-pixel enlargement diagnostics for reading. Capture hashes, exact capture times and page/field locators appear in [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-12727a60cfc18873d0ea). These are hashes of screenshots, not of the FBI PDF, original email, fax or native database. A separate ordinary request for the part06 root PDF endpoint returned HTTP 403; no PDF body or PDF hash was acquired, and that route was stopped. Successful viewer access and a failed direct request are both preserved without inferring removal or motive.\n\n## The two accounts, preserved side by side\n\n**Page 7, Event paragraph, footer 000000245:** the masked source “PROVIDED AN E-MAIL,” described as received from a radio-club member. The paragraph says the email related information from a person on United 93. Its exact relevant wording includes:\n\n> PASSENGERS EVENTUALLY (?) HAD THE HIJACKERS. PASSENGER'S NAME - JEROME GLICK. HIS WIFE TELEPHONED CALL TO 911.\n\nThe question mark and wording are retained, not repaired into a clearer story. The paragraph then says **“FAXED COPY OF CONTROL NUMBER HQ1409 RECEIVED FROM SIOC.”** This is an account of an email and fax, not either underlying item, a direct passenger interview, a verified 911 call or a carrier record. The source and preparer remain masked. Their identities are not inferred from other releases.\n\n**Page 8, opening continuation, footer 000000246:** after a masked field, the record says:\n\n> FAXED TO PITTSBURGH 9/16 AT 3:45 A.M. INSTRUCTED TO DISREGARD AS WIFE OF JEROME GLICK IS IN SAN FRANCISCO. EC DRAFTED.\n\nThe location assertion and instruction are preserved as the record's claims. This review did not establish who issued the instruction, what particular part of the tip was to be disregarded, how the location was checked, or what the drafted EC said. It also did not establish whether “EC DRAFTED” identifies the displayed September 20 communication itself or a separate record. No separate missing memo is presumed to exist merely from that phrase.\n\n**Pages 8–9, review and lead fields:** “Lead Required?: YES” remains on page 8. Page 9 records assignment of **PG1012** on **09/15/2001 at 7:55 PM**, with the instruction **“CONDUCT VICTIM FAMILY INTERVIEW OF”** followed by a masked field. This is an assignment entry, not proof an interview occurred or failed to occur. The coexistence of the interview instruction and disregard note is retained; their operative scope, edit order and later disposition have not been recovered.\n\n## Dates are different administrative fields\n\n| Printed field and locator | Exact value | What remains unknown |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Information Received, p.7 | 09/13/2001; 10:40 AM | Source clock, timezone, receipt mechanism and underlying email/fax timestamps |\n| Event Date/Time, p.8 | 09/13/2001; 10:40 AM | Whether this marks intake or another event; it is not independently established as a September 11 telephone-call time |\n| Assigned To, p.9 | 09/15/2001 at 7:55 PM | Native assignment/history and performance/return |\n| Fax narrative, p.8 | 9/16 at 3:45 A.M. | Actual fax header, transmission/receipt, timezone and relation to the instruction |\n| Communication header, p.7 | 09/20/2001 | Creation/edit/version/approval sequence and relation to “EC DRAFTED” |\n\nThe values have not been combined into a calibrated timeline. Their order is not itself a contradiction: receipt, assignment, forwarding and preparation can be different events. Conversely, an ordinary administrative explanation is not established merely because it is possible. Native records are needed to test the relationships.\n\nThere is also a representation difference: the rendered title's second line reads **PFLP**, while the previously returned web-reader text gives **PELP**. Both are logged as representations in SOURCE-PINS.json. Neither is expanded into an affiliation claim. Native byte equivalence and the cause of the rendering/extraction difference were not tested; no record alteration is inferred.\n\n## Significance, strongest objection and next discriminating records\n\nThis source narrows a question about how a particular tip was screened and corrected. A plausible competing interpretation is ordinary triage of a garbled, multiply relayed email. The form's own disregard note is contrary evidence against treating the initial story as an established independent confirmation. It does not independently prove the reason for disregarding it, and a city name alone does not identify which assertion was considered mistaken. Missing underlying records do not establish concealment, destruction or that the tip was true.\n\nThe best next records are **the original email and relay headers/attachments; SIOC control HQ1409 and the fax with transmission/receipt; the instruction's source and supporting check; the EC or a documented link identifying the September 20 wrapper as that EC; and PG1012's actual interview/return and disposition history**. Any claimed 911 call also needs its own independently matched log/audio/custody/clock record. The masked interview subject is not silently equated with a named person in the narrative. All remain open in [OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-052801c8eeeae4926664); no outreach or new request was sent.\n\nTwo exact public searches, recorded in SOURCE-PINS.json, returned this same official record plus an unrelated keyword collision. They did not supply the underlying email, fax or EC. A locator check of the already held 73-page mirror's text index found no exact hits for PG1012, HQ1409, EC DRAFTED or Jerome Glick. This is a limited index result, not proof those materials are absent from every release or archive.\n\nThe three pages, their five screenshots, two reading crops and returned text are dependent representations of one control-form record, not independent witnesses or multiple corroborations. No original notes/audio/carrier rows/911 record/native lead database were acquired; no call, voice, waveform, decoder, laboratory or calibrated-clock test was performed. All 18 requirements across the existing FAA, telephone, recorder, materials and steel work plan remain open or partial. This bounded source review does not complete that work.\n\n## Preservation and revision accountability\n\nEarlier reports and conflicting accounts are unchanged. This is an additive study, not a replacement for the prior telephone reviews or a new reconstruction of masked identities. The previously covered office-witness paragraph was not republished as a new discovery. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-92774f6ad6c4c651cc58) tracks the user's requirements; [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-797487c6dc9098b47a74) records actual checks and unperformed work; [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-73dd17f9d2773362d355) is the exact addition diff for the five substantive files against no preceding file at this new path. Screenshot/legibility verification is separate from that text diff. Raw images, source PDFs, personal/contact fields, signatures, correspondence, strategy and credentials are outside the public payload.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY e9a3b30e010cabc2de9c5e1f5cc11604d61fbca06c65c61c5b1dd3b948416698 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-848b3c42adf6bff4\"></a>\n### Tape-pickup and HQ1492 follow-up: collection outcomes still open, further May records located\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9c3e721866a37f6d826d).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 848b3c42adf6bff4e669dfcb8aaac80f6eac9c871c70ff330d66348b730090f1 -->\n# Tape-pickup and HQ1492 follow-up: collection outcomes still open, further May records located\n\nNovember2,2026, America/New_York. TEL01–04; AUD016-A1/TC05-B105/TC06-B110. **No collector-identification callback, evidence receipt, actual tape or completed HQ1492collection/disposition was located in this bounded review.** That is not evidence those records never existed, that the FBI failed to act, or that anything was suppressed. The requested pickup, HQ1492, WF334 and HQ366chains remain unjoined.\n\nThe new useful source findings are a later May-family account identifying contemporaneous handwritten notes; a separate report of an **unanswered workplace call with no answering machine/voicemail on the reported telephone**; and a source-specific **first-page/production-footer gap** that limits the held later interview. The workplace report prints **investigation06/10/2001** and **transcription06/28/2002** while describing09/11/2001. Those strings remain unresolved; no year is corrected and no pre-event knowledge inferred.\n\n## Sources and actual scope\n\nThe [held public mirror](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf) has73pages/2,997,662bytes, SHA-256 `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`, acquired2026-10-27T13:40:38.310907UTC. It is a third-party reproduction, not an authenticated native FBI master or complete production. Its bytes remain unchanged.\n\nThis unit inspected18whole mirror faces: **1–3,51–52,54–59,67–73**. Most are reused context checks; the substantive tail71–73was newly assessed for this question. It also inspected footer-only clips from **all73pages**, plus the already-held official FBI response at **part02physical70–71**. The two official faces are reused, not newly acquired witnesses or an independent authentication of calls. No whole73page body review, new OCR, listening, waveform/voice identification, private-record use or redaction recovery occurred. [Exact entities, access dates and image hashes](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b021f850d4fbe212a107) · [Scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-896f3c889fb725b71280) · [Findings/locators](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1f2962020059e389a0e5).\n\nThe [official part02PDF](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file) has78pages/5,561,167bytes, SHA-256 `055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51`, acquired2026-10-31T22:04:24.920527UTC. Official hosting identifies the released representation, not native notes, all source facts or a complete evidence chain.\n\n## 1. What is and is not a collection outcome\n\n| Chain | Exact held evidence | What remains unproved |\n|---|---|---|\n|Reported pickup |[Mirror52/footer000000740](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=52), paragraph2, reports a female FBI agent picked up a tape early in the day; her card was at an office and an identification message had been left. |Collector identity/callback result, actual pickup date/time, original/copy/item identity, receipt, transfer/examination and disposition. This is a reported pickup, not a signed collection certification. |\n|HQ1492 |[Mirror57–59/footers753–755](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=57), written/intake/request unit, directs WFO to obtain the reported recording; assignment09/15/2001at6:10PM. |An instruction/assignment is not completed contact, collection or authentication. No returned media/item/response is supplied by those faces. |\n|WF334 |[Mirror68–70/766–768](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=68) directs contact regarding message contents, assignment09/12/2001at7:20AM. |No unique HQ1492/pickup/media join. Contact wording does not itself document a recovered tape. |\n|HQ366 |[Mirror55–56/743–744](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=55) records a saved pre-incident-message allegation and LeadRequiredNO. |No reasoned disposition, actual collection/test result or link to the pickup page. NO does not prove no work elsewhere or suppression. |\n|May-family response |[Official part02physical70–71/745–746](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=70) reports a September12meeting and local covered lead, referencing265D-NY-280350Serial79. |It is a held response, but it does not identify these media controls, a tape/item/collector or their disposition. A common broad case number/flight label does not supply a unique response-to-request join. |\n\nThe pickup's **BA264** and handwritten **IN3221** remain unexpanded leads, not authenticated flight/office/alias identifiers. The source's calm/pre-hijacking belief remains a recipient's interpretation, not a measured call time. No masked person or agent identity is reconstructed.\n\nHQ1492prints **TODD REUBEN**, receipt09/11/2001at7:49AM, header09/16/2001 and handwrittenHQ3060. WF334prints **TODD RUBEN**, receipt7:49PM, header12/15/2001 and handwrittenWF8406. Preserve these roles/values, the different task wording and written-versus-telephone/radio intake descriptions. Neither receipt is authenticated as a message timestamp. Typed/handwritten controls are not established aliases or additional calls. [Prior HQ1492findings](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2f363700f6b7010a7927a4794ba9972f09385dbe/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-hq1492-recording-request-2026-11-02/README.md) · [Prior pickup findings](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/96de8d9745391a966e3967195cda70ff77a764f9/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-preincident-2026-11-02/README.md).\n\n## 2. An official held response lies within a gap in the mirror's numbering\n\nThe mirror goes from **physical56/footer744 to57/footer753**. The already-held official May response carries **745–746**, numerically inside that range. Both sources also display the request tag35-13. This is a concrete cross-source locator—not proof that the PDFs are identical releases, that every missing number is recovered, or that the mirror can be silently completed from another file. We preserve both entities and their source relationships.\n\nThe official response reports a completed family meeting and limits its covered/no-further-investigation wording to **LasVegas, at that time, this lead**. It does not refer toHQ1492,BA264,WF334, a recording inventory/item or a collector in the two inspected faces. No source cross-reference demonstrates that it resolves those requested chains. Conversely, it must not be described as an unacquired family response. [Earlier held-response qualification](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/e451c84f5494eef39539807b9b984bdb2bcd8eec/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-may-response-qualification-2026-11-02/README.md).\n\nIts6:13a.m.with no stated timezone remains beside the Dallas relay's6:05a.m.Pacific; no conversion or preferred time is adopted. The later May continuation's reference to waking at6AM is **not another measured call timestamp**.\n\n## 3. Later May continuations identify contemporaneous notes\n\n[Mirror71/footer000000770, internal2](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=71), has a continuation header naming NancyMay/RonaldMay and date**06/05/2002**; [72/footer771, internal3](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=72) has the same header/date. These are later report continuations, not the already-held September12,2001EC.\n\nThe internal2account says Nancy took notes during the reported call and wrote down airline telephone numbers. **The actual note set is a new specific retrieval target.** The passage does not say those notes were handed to the FBI, entered in a1Aenvelope, copied, retained or destroyed. No item/receipt/custody number is supplied. Do not merge this note set with Woodward's signed notes, Jefferson's Post-its, a tape or the reported pickup card.\n\nThat continuation also records a recollection of a call lasting one minute or less and a background male voice believed to be another crew member. These are later attributed recollections, not independently timed or heard speech. The numbers themselves, family biography and unrelated personal details are excluded here. The duration recollection must not be substituted for a billed-duration field or joined to a particular carrier row without evidence. Original notes, interview media, carrier/session/recipient records and applicable timing definitions could strengthen, qualify or contradict it.\n\nThe earlier EC's report that Ronald contacted the airline and this later account of Nancy placing calls before Ronald spoke remain in their own source roles. They may describe different portions of a contact chain; no contradiction, common-event reconstruction or preferred account is imposed.\n\n## 4. A separate workplace-call report supplies contrary and unresolved evidence\n\n[Mirror73/footer000000772](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=73) reports an attempted contact by ReneeMay to a redacted workplace recipient. It says the recipient's caller-IDdisplay indicated a call, no one answered, and the reported telephone had **neither an answering machine nor voicemail**. The source gives no call time. This is a report of an **unanswered attempt**, not a recovered saved message, authenticated caller-IDlog or additional conversation. The masked recipient is not identified from other records.\n\nThe record is relevant contrary evidence to assuming every apparent additional recipient implies another recorded/in-flight conversation. It does not establish that no other device/copy/answering service existed, resolve any tape request, or refute/validate the family-canvass conclusion about connected unknown calls. Caller-ID/native phone records, the actual canvass's inclusion rules and original contact records remain necessary. Adjacency or a common flight label does not join it toHQ1492/WF334/HQ366/the pickup.\n\nThe form visibly prints **Dateoftranscription06/28/2002** and **Investigationon06/10/2001**, while its body refers to09/11/2001. Preserve all three fields. A clerical date entry, a reproduction problem or a misunderstood field/version are untested possibilities. **Do not silently replace2001with2002 or conclude that an interview occurred before the attacks.** An original dated interview record/notes, native creation/transcription history and another authenticated release would discriminate.\n\n## 5. The held tail is incomplete as an interview context\n\nPhysical70has footer768;71has770and internal2;72has771and internal3;73has772and a separate first-page form. Our footer-only census accepted70visible production labels on physical4–73. The first3faces are handwritten research notes without those footer labels, checked separately after their clips were blank. **No page bearing769was located in this held copy.** The first page of the later May FD302—candidate footer769—remains a specific missing context target; adjacency does not itself authenticate its production number or content. [Full footer map](CITATIONS.md#nov04-52f046fddeb6f4a9c8bc).\n\nThis is a limitation of the particular public reproduction, not evidence of FBI deletion, withholding, unlawful disposal or deliberate omission. A native/released counterpart, original item index and complete version/page accounting could test whether the compiler selected pages, a page was omitted, a first page exists elsewhere or another relationship applies.\n\nThe initial expectation that the last three footers would be769–771was **our planning error**. Direct checks confirm the prior pickup/HQ1492/WF334locators; no uniform off-by-one correction is warranted. Those prior reports and source bytes remain unchanged. Our tentative citation concern is not a new historical discrepancy.\n\n## Actual searches, remaining work and verification\n\nThree existing official-source ordinary-text indexes (49/78/21rows) were searched for the exact public controlsHQ1492,HQ3060,BA264,IN3221, allowing embedded spaces. They yielded no matching locator. Two new official-domain queries—HQ1492withrecording andBA264withtape/FBI—returned empty search results; no new source was opened/downloaded. [Exact scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b4b78bc28131127b1f54). These narrow misses do not show nonexistence, no follow-up, destruction, withholding or archive-wide exhaustion. No extra broader query, person/contact search or repeated failed route was attempted.\n\nThe immediate targets remain collector/card/callback/contact records; exact lead responses and final/negative/inconclusive disposition; any original/copy media with evidence inventory/FD340/1Aandtransfer/examination records; original written/web intake and routing/history crosswalks; and the missing May firstpage/note set/native contact records. No particular envelope/item/alias relationship is backfilled. [Action/holdings crosswalk](CITATIONS.md#nov04-16bbbedbeec5921d5b00) · [Open TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7e14401447d40c662960).\n\nAll five work tracks/eighteenfullcriteria remain open or partial. Existing technical-owner work is not duplicated and no independent audit acceptance is claimed. [Verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5eabe1cbe7c1ac9c2462) checks source-byte integrity and supplied locator/field accounting, **not historical call, collector, custody, date accuracy or a completed disposition**. Original sources, conflicting values and prior findings remain preserved with an actual additive [Git text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8c1de22477886dfb7074) and [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-dc8ba768cbc45207c167). Raw PDFs/images/notes/audio, personal contacts/biography, agent/personnel identifiers, network/payment details, redacted identities, lawsuit material and private correspondence are outside this public derivative.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 848b3c42adf6bff4e669dfcb8aaac80f6eac9c871c70ff330d66348b730090f1 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-ebfc4dae28e69589\"></a>\n### A reported FBI tape pickup and a separate pre-incident message intake\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-pickup-preincident-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1b14060bfa46eb8a0edd).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY ebfc4dae28e69589c845398e645539ab2b6fcad951e1f20b4911c6d3e55255af -->\n# A reported FBI tape pickup and a separate pre-incident message intake\n\nOriginal-record plan **TEL01–TEL04** remains open. A newly read narrative says a **tape had been picked up by a female FBI agent** and that a message had been left to identify the agent. This supplies a concrete collector/receipt/custody target beyond the [earlier access offer](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/189851483980fff2946921fbaa0d189d70e8ddae/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf1899-voicemail-access-2026-11-02/README.md) and [recording request](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2f363700f6b7010a7927a4794ba9972f09385dbe/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-hq1492-recording-request-2026-11-02/README.md). **It is a report of pickup, not the tape, a signed receipt or verified acquisition outcome.** None of these records has been joined to the same message or caller.\n\nA separately read intake, **HQ366**, describes a message **“JUST BEFORE THE INCIDENT”**, says there was **“NO INDICATION OF IMPENDING DANGER IN MESSAGE,”** and marks **“Lead Required? NO.”** Its relationship to the pickup narrative is unverified. Preserve both accounts without treating the NO flag as suppression or the pickup report as completed authentication.\n\n## Exact sources and actual reading\n\n[Physical 52, production footer 000000740](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=52), is the new pickup narrative. [Physical 55–56, footers 000000743–744](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=55), are the HQ366 intake/continuation. Three new full-size faces were read on **November 2, 2026**. [Physical 51, footer 000000739](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=51), was reused solely to check the boundary against a previously reviewed office interview; it is not a new witness reading.\n\nThe unchanged public mirror has **73 pages**, **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`, acquired **2026-10-27T13:40:38.310907+00:00**. This is a **third-party public reproduction**, not an independently authenticated FBI/native master, complete production or original media chain. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b30829c838072c9b03f8) records exact scopes and image hashes. Raw/full records, personal messages and contact/personnel identifiers remain outside the derivative.\n\n## What the pickup narrative says\n\n[Physical 52, second paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=52), reports that a tape **“was picked up by a female FBI Agent”** at an office **“early in the day.”** It says the agent's card was at the office and **“A message has been left to find the identity of the Agent.”** The collector is not identified in the visible narrative. No masked party or agent identity is reconstructed.\n\nThis is a source's report within a narrative, not a firsthand collection certification or evidence-inventory record. The actual pickup date/time, location/recipient association, agent, original/copy status, tape/device format, evidence identifier, transfers and final result remain unverified. The card, callback/identification record, original contact report, collector's notes and evidence receipt are specific retrieval targets; no contact or new request was made here.\n\nThe first paragraph says the contact was in reference to **BA264** on **September 11, 2001**. The page header gives **265D-NY-280350**; a bottom handwritten notation is read as **IN3221**. Those strings remain unexpanded: BA264 is not identified here as an aircraft flight, and IN3221 is not assigned an office or alias function. The contact-date wording and relative pickup phrase do not authenticate an exact pickup chronology.\n\n## A pre-hijacking belief is not a measured call time\n\n[Physical 52, third/fourth paragraphs](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=52), reports a greeting message attributed to someone said to be on **Flight 77**. The recipient believed it was left **before the plane was hijacked because the caller was “calm.”** Possible faint background noise or other useful sounds are described as the reason for contacting the FBI.\n\nPreserve that account and its basis. Calmness alone does not establish hijacking status or time. No audio was acquired/listened to, no acoustic finding was tested, and no caller/aircraft/device/carrier event or clock was authenticated. The underlying message, preserved metadata and carrier/session/clock joins would test it. A genuinely pre-hijacking greeting would have a different evidentiary role from a conversation describing a hijacking; the canvass's actual inclusion rules must be obtained before assuming either belongs to the same call population.\n\n## What HQ366 records—and what NO does not establish\n\n[Physical 55, Event](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=55), reports a Flight 77 message described as **“JUST BEFORE THE INCIDENT”**, possible useful background information, and **“SHE'LL SAVE AND AWAIT CONTACT FROM FBI.”** It also says there was no indication of impending danger in the message. Those are intake descriptions, not authenticated message content, chronology or a laboratory finding.\n\n| HQ366 field | Printed value / qualified reading |\n| --- | --- |\n| Header date, p55 | **09/12/2001** |\n| Information Received, p55 | **09/11/2001, 7:50 PM** |\n| Event Date / Time, p55 | **09/11/2001 / time blank** |\n| Typed control, p55 | **HQ366** |\n| Case, p55 | **265D-HQ-1348101 (PENDING)** |\n| Handwritten bottom notation, p55 | Read as **Ser342** |\n| Lead Required?, p56 | **NO** |\n\nThe receipt field is not a time the message was left. The handwritten notation has no verified author/date/function or alias relationship. PENDING is historical source text, not current case status.\n\n[Physical 56](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=56) marks **NO** but supplies no reasoned disposition or actual collection/testing result. It does not establish that no handling occurred elsewhere, that the narrative pickup concerned this intake, or that the FBI declined an existing request for analysis. Ordinary triage, other handling, inaccurate records and an uncompleted investigation remain untested possibilities; none is selected. Original intake-review rules, cross-references and actual contact/collection/disposition records would discriminate.\n\nThe two new units describe potentially similar messages, but masked identities and absent native cross-references prevent joining them. Neither apparent similarity nor differing work-status wording establishes a contradiction about one proven event. Do not count them, their control labels or earlier HQ1492/WF334/WF1899 forms as independent corroboration or additional confirmed calls.\n\n## Boundary correction and remaining work\n\nAn earlier navigation cue tentatively called physical 52 a continuation. It has its own printed **1**, different narrative format/header and different subject context from physical 51's previously read office FD302. **No continuation or subject linkage is adopted.** Adjacency in a released compilation is insufficient; the native packet index is still needed. Our tentative cue is preserved as a processing limitation, not a conflicting historical witness statement.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c884c870c2a278f24f9e) retains the tape/card/collector/receipt/media/custody/analysis targets, original HQ366/source/review/disposition records, and all five tracks and 18 original requirements. Original message identity, relevance, timing and final outcome remain untested; inaccuracies, misidentification, related/unrelated messages and actual successful or unsuccessful handling remain possible. No fabricated call, deliberate noncollection, concealment, motive or historical cause is established.\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8da86c1858d78d61305f) has four related analyst entries about two new source units. [verify.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ea1bc0f91de3a620ec02) checks declared source/image/derivative identities, manually entered locators, predecessor preservation and retained TODOs; it does not independently transcribe or authenticate the reported pickup, message, caller, clock or custody. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-41501909e3d5ab3fe4be) states the actual modes run. The [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-02f19dcd1278c25f824d) and actual additive [text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-6a02efba91e3cdf498a4) preserve prior versions. No original criterion or whole-goal completion follows from source reading or publication.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY ebfc4dae28e69589c845398e645539ab2b6fcad951e1f20b4911c6d3e55255af -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-4d98af31362ca56e\"></a>\n### Telephone-record lead: reported FBI cassette custody and a later playback\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-playback-custody-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a959f5790accc5eccec8).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 4d98af31362ca56e7f55f8b675894b0f7cd5a325eb12c4053ebe7304d52341ea -->\n# Telephone-record lead: reported FBI cassette custody and a later playback\n\nOctober 31, 2026 Eastern / November 1 UTC. Scope: the existing telephone-originals work, TEL01–TEL04. This is public-source research, not a finding that the original acquisition or empirical-test requirements have been completed.\n\n## A specific playback and custody record\n\nThe [official FBI Vault September interviews, part 04 of 08](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-04-of-08/view), **viewer page 18**, contains a report dated **3/27/02** describing a visit on **March 26, 2002**. Its footer bears **REQ. #35-13** and **000000348**. The body reports:\n\n- A listener used headphones and a cassette player to hear a copy of a cassette tape described as in FBI custody.\n- The listener was supplied a transcription. The report describes the recording as a **911 call made on September 11, 2001**, by a person who identified himself as a United Flight 93 passenger.\n- The listener reportedly identified the recorded voice. The report subsequently describes other people receiving opportunities to listen and/or read the transcription. It does not report a separate voice identification by every listener.\n- Its final paragraph states that the cassette containing the 911 call and its transcription remained in FBI custody.\n\n**What this supports:** a concrete existing-record retrieval target: the cassette/copy and transcription used during that visit, their evidence-item and custody records, the original emergency-call source, and the documentation of the reported voice recognition. This is documentary counterevidence to a blanket claim that there was no retained recording or no reported identification at that time. Such a blanket claim was not independently tested here.\n\n**What remains unknown:** no audio, cassette, master, transcript attachment, evidence barcode, dispatch log, duplication log or signed custody receipt was acquired in this pass. The report's statement of custody is not a complete custody chain. A listener's reported recognition is not an independent audio-authentication or forensic voice test. No native audio analysis or voice test was performed here. The record does not establish a recording's completeness, absence of edits, date of creation, exact event clock, or survival today. No join to the separately reviewed Beamer/operator, Ong/SERO, carrier table or court-exhibit records has been established.\n\nNames and identities masked in this record remain masked. No identity or family relationship is reconstructed by comparing it to other releases. The report, the playback it describes, its final custody sentence and a later reprint must not be counted as separate independent witnesses to authenticity.\n\n## A transcript counterpart: preserve the different release forms\n\n**Part 04 viewer pages 1–2** contain an Ong-labelled transcript header and opening. The header prints **DL-336** and transcription date **09/12/2001**. The introduction describes a taped conversation involving Ong and the Southeast Reservation Center; the continuation bears **09/11/2001** and its opening speaker states **12:28 p.m. Central Time**, introduces a corporate-security role and asks about the morning. The visible reply recalls an incoming call at approximately **8:20**, without a time zone assigned in that passage.\n\nThe [previously preserved part 03 observations](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/12173507b1f00e9fdd51e42448dcb2498cc9c4e5/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-official-part03-2026-10-31/README.md) locate a corresponding header/opening on **viewer pages 2–3**. Those parts also expose different redaction coverage. We preserve the records as different release representations with shared visible text; we have not established full-document or byte equivalence, complete segment mapping, source independence, a change to underlying audio, or the reason for the redaction differences. No masked name or contact field is filled from another copy.\n\n| Item-level observation | Part 03 | Part 04 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Public viewer's total | 12 pages | 18 pages |\n| Item's advertised PDF size | 2,119,910 bytes | 601,286 bytes |\n| Viewed DL-336 header/opening location | Viewer 2–3 | Viewer 1–2 |\n| Binary obtained in these two source units | No; one direct request returned 403 | No binary request made |\n\nThese are container/release and reading-scope observations. They do not show that the difference in totals is missing transcript pages, that two parts have identical contents, or that an underlying recording was altered. In particular, part 04 page 18 is the separately dated playback report described above, rather than evidence that the whole eighteen-page part is one Ong transcript. The adjacent **page 17** is a differently dated September report continuation; adjacency alone does not join its subject or narrative to the March playback.\n\nThe broad taped-conversation heading, retrospective opening and separate clock roles remain side by side. No controlling description, time-zone conversion or recording identity is selected. The original audio and transcript-segment/custody map remain TODOs; pages **3–16** of part 04 were not read in this pass.\n\n## Preservation, scope and next records\n\nFour distinct public source pages were inspected: **1, 2, 17 and 18**. Five unchanged browser screenshots were retained locally, including both a larger body view and fitted complete-page view of page 18. Page 2 was read only in its visible portion. Small/unclear footer fields beyond the expressly adopted locators remain unverified. Initial loading frames were not interpreted as blank or missing original pages. No OCR, hidden-layer recovery, direct-download retry, alternate asset, credential or gate workaround occurred.\n\n[SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8b8e8752cb21fcb95fbd) supplies the official URL, source-page/paragraph references, captured-view hashes and preservation timestamps. **These SHA-256 values identify browser images, not an FBI PDF, cassette, audio master or historical truth.** Raw images, personal/contact information, masked identities, signatures, private case material and correspondence are outside this public payload.\n\nThe [TODO list](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8c9baf7f3cdf48341676) retains the playback materials, original emergency-call recording and logs, custody/duplication/transcript records, the DL-336 source/segment map, and the outstanding carrier/operator tables. Individual missing inputs remain deferred while available public-source work continues. All eighteen original five-track requirements remain open/partial; this source-level lead closes none of them. No agency or witness contact, new request, fee, physical experiment, source alteration, private push or history rewrite occurred. Earlier source records and published assessments remain unchanged.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 4d98af31362ca56e7f55f8b675894b0f7cd5a325eb12c4053ebe7304d52341ea -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-727382fccfadc025\"></a>\n### Two Ong-labelled transcripts: fuller printed comparison, unresolved audio provenance\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-playback-text-comparison-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-eadf3ad5ebad51f27174).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 727382fccfadc02547a133926dabf8e83b4d49e6f53dcbfe66f43c1d2ae008c4 -->\n# Two Ong-labelled transcripts: fuller printed comparison, unresolved audio provenance\n\nThe released FBI packet contains additional printed differences beyond the previously recorded **passenger/purser** wording. In corresponding injury passages one account prints **“I'm number five.”** and the other **“Our number 5,”**. The repeated cockpit-access question is assigned to different printed speakers. A nearby question and a **Somebody/nobody** clause also differ. These observations concern the released **transcriptions**, not independently heard speech. Neither wording or speaker assignment is selected as correct.\n\n## Source, boundaries and actual work\n\nThe unchanged [official FBI September part04 PDF](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-04-of-08) has18pages/601286bytes, SHA-256 `854bf3408241640a4b5549fba79b7a1f8a9a2639267488b9db3132bd08ac3caf`. It was acquired November2,2026 and previously read for selected findings. This new unit compares the displayed passages end to end; it is **not a new source acquisition** or a claim that the pages were never viewed before.\n\n- **A: DL-336**, physical3–7, footers000000402–406. Page2 supplies the retrospective interview/playback context. The line preceding playback on3 and the post-**Recording concluded** interview on7 remain separate from airborne-playback content.\n- **B: DL267/CE66**, physical11–14/internal2–5, footers000000458–461. Its cover on10 reports CD-ROM-to-analog copying for transcription. The CD, tape and copy/session logs remain unacquired.\n\nAll nine comparison page images and both context pages were directly inspected. Source and reused-raster hashes matched prior pins. [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-564a76a0d9ee1dd7a1d0) gives exact source/page/footer locators; [PASSAGE-MAP.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-fe82aa5e526dee460579) covers the consecutive displayed passage groups and uncertain relations. Analyst IDs are navigation labels, not invented original line numbers. This is a passage-level review, not a certified word-perfect transcription or exhaustive punctuation census. No new listening, voice identification, waveform alignment or clock fit occurred.\n\n## Differences requiring source-media checks\n\n| ID | Printed record A | Printed record B | Qualification |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| D01 | Physical5/footer404: **I'm number five.** | Physical12/footer459: **Our number 5,** | Corresponding injury/galley/cockpit context; earlier and later number-three identification remains in both records. No actual identity or contradictory self-identification inferred from the printed difference. |\n| D02 | Physical6/footer405 places the repeated cockpit-access question under a redacted label and its reply under **ONG**. | Physical13/footer460 includes both question and reply in one **FA ONG** paragraph. | The printed attribution differs. This cannot identify the actual voices or establish an extra participant. |\n| D03 | Physical6: **Can they not see the girls get upset?** The earlier fragment on4 instead prints **(UI) Did you seen the girl who got stabbed?** | Physical13: **Would they not maintain a sterile cockpit?** | The later comparison follows the door-closed fragment/apology and precedes the guys-up-there reply. Earlier A4 alignment remains nonunique. Neither question is adopted as heard speech. |\n| D04 | Physical6: **Somebody can call the cockpit.** Earlier physical4 prints **Nobody can call the cockpit to see if we can get inside.** | Physical13: **nobody can call the cockpit,** | Preserve all three readings. They do not establish whether a cockpit call occurred or succeeded. |\n| D06 | Physical5 uses **he's coming back** and a generic unintelligible-background marker. | Physical12 uses **somebody is coming back** and includes explicit background speech before a separate talking marker. | Pronoun/coverage difference; absence from a printed span is not demonstrated absence from original audio. Names in the background line are omitted from this derivative. |\n| D07 | Physical5: **our passenger is stabbed.** | Physical12: **our purser has been stabbed.** | Previously documented in the [generation-chain review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/17aef02c7d79169234dc04c4a67f38425900ea30/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-transcript-generation-chain-2026-11-02/README.md), retained rather than counted as new independent evidence. |\n| D08 | Early physical3 prints **We can't even get a manager to the cockpit.** Later physical6 prints **We can't even get into the cockpit.** | Physical13 also prints **We can't even get into the cockpit.** | The early fragment cannot uniquely be time-matched; the later agreement is counterevidence against portraying every passage as conflicting. |\n| D09 | The later reservation query has a first-name speaker label; earlier labels are redacted. | Corresponding physical13 labels use **OP Agent** and additional explicit confirmation turns. | A label/coverage difference, not a recovered identity or verified call-leg join. |\n| D10 | Physical7: **No, we're just calling medical and we can't get**; then **Recording concluded.** | Physical14: **No. Somebody is calling Medical and we can't get**; then **End of tape**. | Both printed lines stop at **get**. No missing duration or native recording endpoint is measured here. |\n\nThe exact selected readings, page/paragraph anchors and limits are preserved in [DIFFERENCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-713bfd463942773118b8). D05 separately records the sequence/coverage issue below. Ten register entries are analyst observations, not ten calls, edits, witnesses or independent confirmations.\n\n## A sequence issue, without a claimed explanation\n\nA begins with breathing/description/cockpit/Flight12–11 material on3, followed by reservation and seat questions on4; similar topics occur again in its longer run on5–6. B begins with a number-three/cockpit/mace/hijack opening on11, then seat/name material and the longer overlapping sequence on12–14. The early A fragments therefore cannot all be assigned a unique one-to-one position in B from words alone.\n\nThe map preserves the early fragments and the later counterparts instead of deduplicating them. It does **not** establish replay, looping, a deliberate edit, two different calls, a master-file omission or what produced the displayed structure. Similar statements may be repeated in an actual conversation; playback/session handling, source coverage and transcription are additional untested possibilities. The first **Flight12** attributed to FA ONG in B11 is distinct in the printed sequence from the later AA/OP Flight12 exchange in B12. Matching that number alone would create an unsupported alignment.\n\n## Agreement and the strongest competing reading\n\nThe seat/**3R**, name/number-three/**Flight11**, Boston–LosAngeles, later flight-number correction and medical-contact ending supply substantial ordered parallels. Both later access passages use **into the cockpit**, and both terminal medical-contact lines end at **get**. These agreements constrain a claim that the printed differences demonstrate wholly different calls. They still do not prove identical native recordings, authenticated voices or calibrated clocks.\n\nAn ordinary source-generation/transcription account could produce differences of wording, speaker labels and displayed coverage. That account is plausible, **not demonstrated**. Conversely, the paper differences alone do not establish fabricated or deliberately altered audio, attack participation, concealment or motive. Related transcriptions and their handling descriptions cannot be counted as independent authentication of the underlying call.\n\n## Next discriminating records and remaining scope\n\nThe useful targets are the actual A interview/playback recording with its full session/seek history, the B-source CD and analog rerecording with duplication/transcription logs, and the native call/master plus segment/channel mappings. Compare authenticated samples at the injury, cockpit-question and Somebody/nobody passages; retain unaffected seat/route and terminal passages as controls. Then determine whether the two written accounts represent identical source samples, different coverage or transcription choices. These tests remain **unperformed**.\n\nThe prior engineering inquiry, effective recorder configuration, faxed statements and receipt, original notes, carrier/operator/transfer/recipient links and clock definitions remain TODOs. The [prior report](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/17aef02c7d79169234dc04c4a67f38425900ea30/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-transcript-generation-chain-2026-11-02/README.md) and all original conflicting values remain unchanged. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9e8479a5a254fc143d31) carries all five tracks/eighteen original requirements forward. This comparison completes only the declared printed-passage review, not any native-input acceptance criterion.\n\n[CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3d2ebec104868603487e), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-af7b7fae138f2d0869eb) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5a7de96e158079fea7f4) distinguish actual reading, preservation checks and remaining tests. No raw scan, full transcript, audio, signature/contact field, redacted identity or private case material is included in this derivative. Publication does not establish historical accuracy or main-branch adoption.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 727382fccfadc02547a133926dabf8e83b4d49e6f53dcbfe66f43c1d2ae008c4 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-42745b526bfd4006\"></a>\n### Telephone originals: a recipient interview and an answering-machine lead\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-recipient-message-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b0e8714f90a0431acbb7).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 42745b526bfd40068f49a5d5c89628743ca0f02a9b3335029197c775fa3118d1 -->\n# Telephone originals: a recipient interview and an answering-machine lead\n\nOctober 31, 2026 Eastern / November 1 UTC. The [official FBI September interviews, part 05 of 08](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-05-of-08/view) supplies two source-specific retrieval leads. These are released interview/form representations, not acquired native carrier tables or audio. They do not complete any of the eighteen original five-track requirements.\n\n## 1. Recipient report CE40: separate recollection, belief and caller statements\n\n**Viewer pages 25–26**, internal pages 1–2, are an FD-302-style report with **Lead Control Number CE40**, transcription date **09/12/2001**, and **REQ. #35-13** footers **000000151–000000152**. The caller is identified in the visible text as Sandra Bradshaw. The recipient's masked identity remains masked.\n\n| Source location | What the report actually says | What has not been established here |\n|---|---|---|\n| Page 25, incoming-call paragraph | A call was received between **9:30 a.m. and 10:00 a.m.** on September 11. | A measured switch timestamp or a time zone. No zone is supplied in that passage. |\n| Page 26, second paragraph | The recipient **believes** the call used a **GTE telephone mounted on the back of an airplane seat**. | Verified device, carrier/service routing or a match to a native billing/switch row. |\n| Same paragraph | The call was **estimated** to last **five to ten minutes**. | An independently measured duration or actual start/end pair. The thirty-minute receipt window and duration estimate describe different quantities. |\n| Same paragraph | The connection was described as poor; the wording includes inability to hear background conversations or noise, followed by mostly hearing **air noise**. | A recording-based acoustic result or an inference that other passengers were silent or absent. Preserve both descriptions without choosing or rewriting one. |\n| Pages 25–26, relayed narrative | Caller statements include hijackers, passenger movement and an asserted flight location. The page-25 account also describes crew location as an **assumption** and says the first-class curtain obstructed the caller's view. | Direct observation by the recipient, independently measured aircraft position or direct sight of the cockpit. |\n| Page 26, notification paragraph | The recipient reportedly called **United Airlines in Newark immediately afterward** and spoke to an **FBI Chicago agent later**. | Original outgoing call records, airline intake/incident log, agent-contact record, independently established sequence or a calibrated time. |\n\nPage 25 also reports **27 passengers at the back** with the caller. This remains a relayed, phase-specific account, not a manifest census or an independently verified count. It must not be combined with other calls' headcounts as though every account describes the same moment and population. No row-level accounting was performed from this narrative.\n\nThe most discriminating next records are the original recipient interview notes, any source recording