/README.md), which expressly reports a cassette and transcription remaining in FBI custody then. **No same-recording, same-caller or custody join between these reports has been established.** A description of a message does not inherit the other report's custody assertion.\n\n## Scope, preservation and outstanding tests\n\nThe official item advertises **1,097,079 PDF bytes** and its viewer exposes **26 pages**. Six distinct source pages were inspected: **1, 16, 17, 18, 25 and 26**. Page 1's photographic-identification interview is outside the adopted telephone findings. Only the relevant header of the personal/background form on 16 was adopted; personal/contact fields and unrelated narrative were excluded. Larger and fitted views of 25–26 support the selected paragraph/footer readings. Pages **2–15 and 19–24** were not read; neither thumbnails nor loading frames establish their content or absence of attachments.\n\nSeven unmodified viewer images were retained locally. [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-87e38d068d557f4f434c) records the official URL, selected page/paragraph/footer locators, SHA-256 values and preservation timestamps. These hashes identify **captured browser views**, not an original FBI PDF, audio, answering-machine device or authentic historical event. No PDF was requested or obtained, and no audio was acquired, played, decoded, transcribed or forensically tested. No new OCR, hidden-identity recovery, failed-download retry or access workaround occurred.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e5e75018d9049d481ff6) carries the original-message and recipient-record dependencies alongside all existing FAA/telephone/recorder/materials/steel requirements. No witness/agency contact, new request, fee, experiment, mailbox access or private case-material use occurred. Raw images, contact details, signatures, masked identities and private correspondence are excluded from the public payload. Earlier records and published assessments remain unchanged; no conspiracy, fabricated-call, suppression or current-retention finding follows from these source limitations.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 42745b526bfd40068f49a5d5c89628743ca0f02a9b3335029197c775fa3118d1 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-45cc8d533013c3d1\"></a>\n### Initial call recipient: statement, observation limits and reported restrictions\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-recipient-statement-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f269396eebd43a540880).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 45cc8d533013c3d1e142cfd19edc89546dd68e6d8a58b321574320e2a4f5f9af -->\n# Initial call recipient: statement, observation limits and reported restrictions\n\nA complete four-page interview in an already-held public packet provides a concrete lead to a separate statement reportedly written after the call. It also reports an instruction to **“block it”** concerning unspecified system information. The same account expressly limits what the recipient heard and what she merely assumed. These are attributed reports in a reproduced interview, not the native statement, telephone events or proof an instruction was implemented.\n\n## Source and reading scope\n\nThe [public mirror](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf) has 73 pages and 2,997,662 bytes; SHA-256: `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`. It was acquired October 27, 2026 and remains unchanged. This November 2 examination is a scoped reading of held material, **not a new acquisition or independently authenticated native agency production**.\n\nThe recipient interview occupies physical **38–41**, internal **1–4**, footers **000000447–450**, lead controls **DL267/CE66**, case **265D-NY-280350-CE**. Its transcription/investigation/dictation fields read **09/12/2001**. All four page faces were read through the end for the business, call and source passages adopted below. Biography, family/contact details, obscured identities and unverified marginal annotations are excluded.\n\nThe distinct two-page booking report at 42–43 was viewed to establish its complete boundary and check a tentative year reading. Page 44 is a different phone-analysis record, used only for its header/boundary; its financial/identity/call fields are not newly adopted or reproduced. Seven full-page images were displayed, with three detail rechecks on 38, 41 and 42. Those rechecks are not additional records. [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-bf4fdc51a49223f14adf) records the source URL, original access date, hashes and exact page/footer scopes. No whole-packet reading, hidden-text recovery, OCR, audio listening, ASR or native clock/system test is claimed.\n\n## A separate statement to locate\n\n[Physical 41, first body paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=41) says a supervisor directed the recipient to write a statement and be available for debriefing. It reports that she wrote the statement in a conference room. That airline statement is a different object from this FBI-form interview. The reproduction does not supply its original bytes, content/version or receipt.\n\nEarlier work identified separately listed operator statements, notes, recordings and prospective 1A transfers. This is a closer creation-context pointer, **not proof that a listed enclosure is this exact statement or that a promised transfer occurred**. An actual content/date/version/custody match is needed; names or shared case/control labels alone do not join the objects.\n\n## Line setup and partial call coverage\n\n[Physical 38–39](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=38) reports an inability to find the emergency button, speed-dial contact with the international resolution desk, opening the line to three participants, a colleague activating his button and an operations participant indicated by a light. It describes an operations handoff. The account explains the button as triggering recording and alerting operations. These are reported actions/functions, not native switch, recorder configuration or authenticated call legs.\n\nReservation-side actions do not settle the separate later dispatch **patch/relay** accounts. The source's recalled first words also differ in source role from the opening of the [previously inspected printed recording transcription, part 04 physical 11/footer 458](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-04-of-08#page=11). No common first sample, actual trigger time or cause of the coverage difference has been established.\n\n[Physical 40, third body paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=40) says she **“did not hear the end”**. It describes a headset handoff and estimates more than 20 minutes before another listener took over. Her participation estimate is not total call duration, recorded duration or a calibrated crash/disconnect time. The account gives crash or lost communication as alternatives after the other listener removed the headset; neither is selected here.\n\nThe preceding paragraph reserves whether seat references were heard during the call or later operations discussion, and whether an exclamation was heard directly or learned afterward. Those qualifications prevent treating the reported details as direct last words or an independent seat identification. Reported repetition in conversation also does not explain or authenticate particular repeated passages in the earlier printed comparison.\n\n## Caller reports and recipient assumptions remain separate\n\n[Physical 39, second and third body paragraphs](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=39) reports an initial **Flight 12** reference, then **Flight 11, Boston to Los Angeles**. It expressly says the recipient **assumed** the references to **#5 and #1** meant other crew members. It says she **thought** the caller was relaying information provided by others and did not believe the caller could actually see events.\n\nThose are expressly marked interpretations in a witness account, not authenticated voice, crew identity, injury or direct-observation findings. They qualify how much weight this report can bear in assessing the earlier **“I’m number five” / “Our number 5”** printed conflict. Both printed versions remain preserved; this interview does not establish which words were spoken. Shared case controls and related source chains also prevent counting these pages as automatically independent corroboration.\n\n## Preserve reported times without joining clocks\n\n| Source and role | Account | Missing link |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Recipient interview, physical 38/footer 447, last body paragraph | **Approximately 7:59 a.m.** received a call | Native event/time source, timezone and clock calibration. |\n| Same interview, physical 41/footer 450, third body paragraph | Computer lookup reportedly said Flight 11 **took off from Boston at 8:04 a.m.** | Actual terminal/status record, field definition and timestamp basis. |\n| Previously read [official part 04, physical 2/footer 401](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-04-of-08#page=2), retrospective account | **Approximately 8:20**: an employee receives a call; emergency alert and coordinator listening are described | Which event, leg and clock each time denotes; a common source match. |\n\nThe **7:59** and **8:04** strings were checked in visible-page detail renders. They remain as printed, without selecting either as historical time. The **8:20** account is reused context, not a new measurement. Morning-time zones and native joins are unestablished. **No delay, common call-start time or call-before-takeoff finding is calculated from these unjoined descriptions.** Native agent/telephone events and the original terminal flight-status record would help test their relationship.\n\n## Information-control instructions: concrete lead, unknown execution\n\n[Physical 41, second body paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=41) reports overhearing discussion of information still accessible in a system, followed by an instruction to **“block it.”** The report adds **“apparently to keep it from being seen by others.”** That qualification remains the report's interpretation, not a verified purpose.\n\nThe precise information, system, object, scope, authority, recipient and actual execution are unestablished. Nearby manifest/ticket discussion does not identify **it**. This is not an audit log, deletion record or demonstrated change. Authorized incident privacy/security restriction, improper suppression, and a misunderstood or unimplemented instruction remain **untested alternatives**. None is selected to resolve or dismiss the report.\n\nDiscriminating inputs are the actual instruction and recipients, target data/system, effective incident/access policy, permissions/change/audit/retention logs and surviving relevant data or snapshots. None is recovered here.\n\nThe last paragraph of the same page says she tried not to discuss the call because she had been told not to. The issuer, exact words, time, scope and authority are unspecified. It is not identified as a legal gag order or joined to the block-it instruction. **The reported direction to write a statement and be available for debriefing remains alongside the reported discussion restriction.** That documentation account limits a simple claim that all documentation was stopped, while not establishing whether access/discussion restrictions were proper or improper.\n\n## Our rejected year reading\n\nAn initial low-resolution reading of the adjoining booking report suggested **2011**. A preserved detail recheck shows **2001 in both booking-date passages** on physical 42; its form date is **09/13/2001**. Our preliminary note and correction are retained locally. Source bytes did not change. This is **our reading error, not conflicting historical records**; no year-discrepancy lead, booking identity, payment or nationality inference is adopted.\n\n## Status and next inputs\n\nThe advance is a source-level map to a reportedly created airline statement, reported line/recorder actions, partial listener coverage, explicit assumptions and memory limits, and unverified access/discussion instructions. [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-440825a07f666e04dddc) contains nine related analyst observations, not nine witnesses or independent confirmations. Original statement/version/receipt, end-listener notes, native call/session media, switch/agent events, terminal data, effective policies and execution/custody records remain missing.\n\nNo covert role, fabricated call, deliberate alteration, executed deletion, conspiracy or motive is established. Prior sources, printed disagreements and the failed synthetic control remain unchanged. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-73e27ab0a45e7cc40fcf) retains all five tracks and 18 original requirements, including the priority FAA corrected answer/receipt, signed administrative decision and separate recommendation disposition. None is accepted by this reproduced interview.\n\n[CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-75d536cc50de83f21265), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-96613df0217a6029e58b) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-411cb9f91edea6b321cf) distinguish actual reading from byte/navigation checks. This derivative excludes raw scans/images/full interviews, private case material, biographies, personal/contact/payment data, signatures and reconstructed identities. Publication integrity is not historical validation, independent audit, substantive goal completion or main-branch adoption.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 45cc8d533013c3d1e142cfd19edc89546dd68e6d8a58b321574320e2a4f5f9af -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-84d9bf49ac5fefae\"></a>\n### A reported cassette handover and two different telephone relay accounts\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-recording-custody-relays-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-4b7b7aef9d8208ea7af0).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 84d9bf49ac5fefaeca9910ebced9258ad3b1c82f18a580e90f0c6077221ac4bc -->\n# A reported cassette handover and two different telephone relay accounts\n\nNovember 2, 2026, America/New_York; source-reading and verification receipts extend into November 3 UTC. TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. These are newly inspected pages in already-held public FBI records, not newly acquired tapes or independently authenticated calls.\n\n## 1. A concrete Boston cassette-custody target\n\n[Official part 01, physical page 11](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=11), production footer **000000002**, contains an FD-302 reporting collection of an answering-machine cassette associated with **Linda Gronlund**. The report describes these separate events on September 11, 2001:\n\n| Printed approximate time | Reported event | What is not established |\n|---|---|---|\n| **6:45 p.m.** | Writer telephonically contacted; told a message was on cassette and would be made available to the FBI. | This is the reported contact time, not the time the original message was recorded. |\n| **7:30 p.m.** | Writer interviewed the recipient and received the cassette recording from the answering machine. | No separately recovered evidence item, receipt, native recording identity or original-versus-copy determination. |\n| **9:20 p.m.** | Writer transported the tape directly to the FBI office in Boston and handed it to an assistant special agent in charge. | No separately recovered intake/transfer record, examination result, later disposition or present-custody proof. |\n\nAll three times remain as printed, with **no adopted time zone**. No elapsed interval, call time, aircraft time or calibrated clock is derived from them. The form prints transcription **09/12/2001**, investigation **09/11/2001**, dictated **09/12/2001**, file **265D-NY-280350**. Those are different field roles. The redacted recipient/author and personnel identifying fields are not reconstructed or reproduced.\n\nThis is a more specific retrieval target than a generic missing-recording allegation: the institution, receiving role, date and reported handover are identified. It is still an interview/collection report's account, **not the cassette itself or a complete evidence chain**. The actual receipt/item record, original/copy history, examination/transcription and retention/disposition records could corroborate, qualify or contradict the account.\n\nNo explicit item/control cross-reference joins this cassette to the earlier **BA264/IN3221 pickup, HQ1492, HQ366 or WF334** leads. Similar recording descriptions, caller associations or a common investigation are insufficient. Their earlier differing names, dates, AM/PM fields and assignments remain unchanged. [Preserved prior comparisons](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/56e7780d85b9947de12f36dfe614ac1794d3ff78/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-pickup-hq1492-disposition-2026-11-02/README.md).\n\n## 2. An attempted Beamer patch became a reported party-line relay\n\n[Physical page 43](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=43) and [continuation 44, internal page 2](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=44) contain a different FD-302, dated **09/11/2001**, file **265D-NY-280350**. The opening identifies a call from a **GTE Airfone office in Oak Brook**, relaying information from another employee reportedly speaking to **Todd Beamer**. It does not begin as a demonstrated direct FBI-to-passenger conversation.\n\nPreserve the following reported sequence without selecting a calibrated timeline:\n\n- **Approximately 8:45 AM:** contact to the special agent and a relayed passenger account.\n- The office was trying to patch Beamer's call to the agent; GTE employees could not accomplish that immediately. The report says **that office lacked the capability to record Beamer’s conversation**. It does not establish that no recording existed anywhere in the wider provider/recipient network.\n- **9:03 AM:** the intermediary said he believed the call had disconnected.\n- **9:11 AM:** the intermediary said the call had **not** disconnected and that the phone might be in a seat pocket.\n- **Approximately 9:15 AM:** a patch was described as ready, but the report says a **party-line call ensued instead**, introducing a New York State Police participant. The continuation describes a separate **Jeremy Glick-associated** telephone relay.\n- **9:36 AM:** the continuation says both intermediaries reported losing the calls. This is a reported endpoint, not an authenticated switch termination or aircraft event.\n\nNo time zone is printed in these adopted labels. The **believed disconnected / not disconnected** reports remain side by side as source statements at different stated moments; no cause or actual network state is chosen. Readiness of a patch is not proof that the intended passenger-to-agent patch was completed. Conversely, this report does not establish that no direct connection occurred at any other point. The masked identities and cross-call speaker/leg assignments remain unfilled.\n\nThe next discriminating records are the actual operator and FBI/NYSP call logs, bridge/transfer tickets, recordings if made, circuit/leg identifiers, field definitions and source-clock configuration. Those are needed before joining any printed carrier row to a passenger, operator, party line, silent interval or termination. The three-hijacker/weapon and passenger-count descriptions in the narrative are relayed statements, not independent physical or caller authentication; they are not newly used here to establish events aboard an aircraft.\n\n## 3. A separate recipient report asserts a recording and a later endpoint\n\n[Physical page 12](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=12), footer **000000003**, is a **different** FD-302 concerning a redacted recipient of a **Glick-associated** call. Its form prints transcription, investigation and dictated dates **09/12/2001**, while its narrative describes **09/11/2001**, sometime after **9:30 a.m.** Those roles and dates remain distinct.\n\nThe narrative reports hearing sounds, then silence, and an operator relaying information to police. It presents the recipient as sure there was a tape recording of the conversation and writes the provider-name variants **“Varizon, or Verizon.”** Neither the affiliation nor the recording's existence/content was independently verified here; the spelling is not silently standardized or used to reconstruct a masked person.\n\nIt reports the line remaining open until **approximately 10:45 a.m.** No printed time zone is adopted. Preserve that account beside the **9:36 AM** loss report on page 44 and the previously reviewed operator's speech/silence/provider-relay estimates. **Do not treat those as synchronized endpoints of an established common leg.** Clock basis, source identity, routing and which connection each witness meant are unverified. No preferred time, conversion, historical gap or causal explanation is selected.\n\nThe recipient's recording assertion and the GTE office's lack-of-recording-capability statement concern differently attributed accounts and potentially different offices/legs. They do not prove a single contradictory recording state. Nor does a possible different-leg explanation supply the missing record. Provider, recorder, police/office and custody records could strengthen or weaken either account. No new audio was acquired or listened to.\n\n## 4. Boundaries, index check and what was actually tested\n\nFive distinct page faces were visually inspected at **140 dpi**: **10, 11, 12, 43 and 44**. Page 10 is a different **CVR transcript page 10 of 10**, not a cover or continuation of the cassette-collection report. Its technical content was excluded from this telephone study; no recorder timing/translation work was duplicated. Page 12 is a separate report rather than a continuation of page 11. No complete 49-page visual reading or original-record authentication is claimed.\n\nThe held ordinary-text index had useful topic hits at pages 11 and 43. An exact check of the already-held public court prosecution index found **no literal Gronlund or Glick row match**. Its two generic cassette-title matches do not identify either requested recording, so neither was opened or adopted as related. This is a bounded check of a particular index representation, not an exhaustive no-record finding. No external query or new source download was needed for this unit. [Search/locator scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b1b865ba1239e54f462f).\n\nThe original PDF remains **4,468,234 bytes, 49 pages**, SHA-256 **4760de107bef3c75f4d7629f90f7a70d2c861cb3b53dcbe37a3bf0fb768f93cb**. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-16d4d7ab6d9b24589f4c) pins its original access time, relevant paragraph/field locators and the reused court-index entity. Source bytes and selected render hashes were verified. The automated checks reproduce topic/index matching and bundle integrity; **manual image readings are not independently verified by that code**. No hidden text, mask recovery, new OCR, voice/caller authentication, native carrier decoding, synchronized clock fit or physical test was performed.\n\nThe source reports, potential tape, agency transfer account, court index, caller relays and later recollections are different evidence stages. They must not be counted as independent corroboration of wrongdoing. High confidence attaches to the selected visible readings; the historical message, recording/copy identity, actual leg/routing, source clocks and complete custody remain unverified. Nothing here establishes fabrication, concealment, explosives, motive or historical cause.\n\n## Next records and preservation\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-310f3e31d3ab6357736c) carries the actual Boston cassette receipt/item/examination/retention chain, GTE/NYSP/FBI bridge/operator records, and the alleged Glick-associated recording and recipient/provider source chain. All five original tracks and eighteen full requirements remain open or partial. Acquired Keyton/usage/court components and the technical owners' completed tests remain recognized; no narrower completion criterion is adopted.\n\nThis is an additive public derivative of the native research report. Earlier source files, source conflicts, reports and public history remain unchanged. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d9f399c872ce647b6151), [METHOD.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-98f6534e515018636e96), [verification code/results](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1ed27f3115a6dbbec3c1) and the [actual preceding-text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b4ada6f83bd03ed22598) record the work and its limits. Raw scans, full extracts, cassette/audio, personnel/contact/signature information, masked identities, private case/correspondence and coordination records are excluded. No outreach, new request, fee, mailbox access, private push, merge, deletion or history rewrite was performed. Publication verifies disclosure of reviewed research, not substantive completion of the investigation.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 84d9bf49ac5fefaeca9910ebced9258ad3b1c82f18a580e90f0c6077221ac4bc -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-0b37db336b1a5c98\"></a>\n### A public transcript reproduction supplies a recording item ID and conflicting accounts\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-recording-index-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3c0505d4285b5ea8d52f).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 0b37db336b1a5c981176ca0f702cd2334636f7898dd85da2245cc9d19fd58381 -->\n# A public transcript reproduction supplies a recording item ID and conflicting accounts\n\nOctober 31, 2026, America/New_York; captures extend into November 1 UTC. **TEL01-TEL04 / existing AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** The ordinary public catalogue returned a 21-page reproduction matching the cited title. Its indexed/OCR representation supplies **item 1A-1A64148**, **SOURCE_ACCN 2496**, and Bates range **M-NKA-00012169–00012189**. These are more precise retrieval keys for the underlying media and records. The actual original audio, envelope, native transcript and receipt remain unacquired.\n\n## Source form and actual reading\n\n[Public record 18886478](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886478/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-Todd-Beamer-Fdr-9-15-01-FBI-302-Transcript-UAL-SAC-Nick-Leonard-Re-Jefferson-Beamer-Call-419) is a third-party mirror under a 9/11 Document Archive upload attribution. Its title is a catalogue pointer, not proof of official custodianship. Its actual pages display indexed fields, an OCR section, transcript text and privacy markings. We did not obtain an authenticated original FD340 facsimile, a master PDF or audio. No native PDF/audio hash is claimed.\n\nNormal public search/page/zoom controls exposed the text without sign-in or export. One catalogue query and one matching-result open were used; the second planned query was unnecessary. After an initial four-page check, the reading scope was prospectively extended to the same complete 21-page representation to understand its nested records. All 21 reported Bates labels and the end-of-tape text were read/captured through the ordinary reader. Twelve selected viewport JPEGs across ten viewer pages support the important fields; these are not 21 complete facsimile images. Contact-pattern lines were omitted from the printed reading aid, and no incidental family details are adopted here.\n\nThe preserved browser-decoded UTF-8 source capture is **65,271 bytes**, SHA-256 **f97c92e565db27da6a7445a4e2114163ddb8320c5c4f52a73b4712ab43e0eeeb**. This fingerprints that capture, not an original PDF, recording or FBI master. Raw privacy-marked images, reader text and full speech remain outside this public payload. [Source/capture fingerprints](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a1a0fc746daae47a6653), [actual scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-04c6481222fc1d4f9cd7), [page/Bates/paragraph and capture-line pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-80c2cdd469a091c17af1). Use the reader's Jump to Page control for the viewer-page locators below; captured DOM line numbers are separate from archival pagination.\n\n## 1. The evidence index is more specific than the earlier promise\n\nViewer page 1/Bates 12169 displays **FBIITEMNO 1A-1A64148**, **EVIDENCETYPE 1A**, **P_SEIZDATE 09/15/2001** and **P_DESCR “RECORDING OF CONVERSATION”**. The item repeats in later footers. This is displayed index/OCR content, not independent proof of a seizure or physical receipt on that date. Handwritten/garbled received-date text and masked agent fields were not accepted or reconstructed.\n\nThe previously read [official September 22 FD302, physical 47-48](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=47) describes a September 15 follow-up being taped, a synopsis copy in 1A, and a recording copy to be provided later. Preserve that future-copy wording beside the new index date. No original envelope/receipt or media hash currently proves whether these concern the same copy, what the date field means operationally, or when material entered FBI custody. Do not convert either source into a controlling receipt date.\n\nThe mirror header on viewer page 3/Bates 12171 reads **285A-NY-280350-NK**. The official September 22 form reads **265A-NY-280350-NK**. Both source readings remain. The mirror's indexed/OCR form makes the original facsimile and case/item/Bates crosswalk especially important. An OCR/index/transcription issue, a different record assignment or another explanation remains untested. This is a provenance/retrieval difference, not established historical misfiling or tampering. No redacted identities are filled from this or another release.\n\n## 2. Two conversations and a letter require separate source roles\n\nViewer pages 4-6/Bates 12172-12174 begin with a United Airlines representative reading a letter. The opening uses transcript terminology; the cover being read calls its content a **“text recollection.”** The described three-page letter contains a cover, contact information and an account; the reader skips the contact page. A letter dated September 14 is being read, which does not independently date the recording of that reading. S-A-C is the representative's stated UAL designation; its expansion and any claimed FBI authority are not established here.\n\nViewer page 7/Bates 12175 then notes a pause, introduces another conversation, mentions a received summary and asks to record the conversation. The document's recording label cannot collapse these into an original in-flight recording, one continuous call, or an authenticated single cassette. A transcript of a later reading is not the original written enclosure. Original audio, typed transcript, letter/fax and source-version/copy records remain separate targets.\n\nViewer page 18/Bates 12186 contains a negative response to a question about a tape and an explanation that local recording would have required leaving the floor/going to an office. Preserve the scope: this is a reported local-recording account, not a demonstrated absence of every possible carrier, facility or FBI relay capture. It provides contrary context to an assumption that the original in-flight call must have been recorded and then withheld. The facility policy/configuration and surviving media are still unverified.\n\n## 3. Preserve the numerical and wording differences\n\n| Question | Letter-reading segment | Later dialogue / other source | What remains untested |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Front/back count | Viewer 5/Bates 12173: **27 front / 10 back** | Viewer 10/Bates 12178: **10 front / 27 back** | Original letter and audio/transcription, source of counts and actual manifest/locations. Both sums are 37 only as arithmetic of reported values. Neither value is selected. |\n| Conversation length | No independently measured duration obtained | Viewer 14/Bates 12182: initial **about 40 minutes**, then a **10-minute** reference attributed to others, then **15 minutes** | These are separate statements, not an adopted 10–15 range or calibrated duration. Who supplied the later figure and what each measured remain unknown. |\n| End/held-line descriptions | Viewer 6/Bates 12174 describes silence while connected, followed by an ending at **nine a.m.** | Viewer 19-20/Bates 12187-12188 describe **about 10 more minutes** holding and later radio news **about 10 minutes later**. The [earlier official operator account](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/29ee78c52ae09a2cadeb33b0856c654c51982a3c/investigation/broader-evidence/fbi-vault-operator-record-2026-10-31/README.md) records a **20-minute** silent-open phase and a separate **approximately 5-minute** later-contact estimate. | Event/leg boundaries, recording and clock alignment are missing. No arithmetic timeline or controlling duration is imposed. |\n| Phrase attribution | Viewer 6/Bates 12174 leaves a phrase to an unspecified speaker | Viewer 15/Bates 12183 contains a question/answer attributing a later wording to Todd | Original audio, notes and synopsis versions are needed. Do not silently make different reported wording a single verbatim last statement. |\n\nThe later dialogue also reports a call time of **about 8:45 central standard time** at viewer 8/Bates 12176. The letter-reading has an 8:45 a.m. label. Neither establishes a calibrated timebase, EST/EDT conversion or a match to a particular native row. Retellings and billing fields cannot be joined by a desired time alone. [All retained values and discriminating tests](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3123b149fc093cd06105).\n\n## 4. Later knowledge, service claims and contrary evidence\n\nViewer pages 13-14/Bates 12181-12182 distinguish prior service use/corporate-program information, facts learned later and an inference about passengers discussing action together. Those distinctions matter for independence: a later detail is not automatically something independently heard during the original call. The actual provider/account records, initial notes, synopsis and recording versions should test that chain.\n\nViewer 19/Bates 12187 reports information told to the speaker about handling **over 200 simultaneous calls** in ordinary winter-storm conditions, **360** that day, and a lock-up described as short of a total crash. This is an anecdotal/reported technical account. Over 200 is not a hard 200 maximum, and 360 is not an authenticated incident metric. Native fault/recovery/session/clock logs are needed before using the passage to explain any particular billed or held duration.\n\nThe dialogue's calmness discussion, expressed uncertainty, later-learning disclosures and local-recording explanation are contrary evidence to treating every difference as an admission of fakery or concealed reconstruction. The ending discusses prospective press contact and information sharing; it does not itself establish a false account, foreknowledge or attack coordination. Different recollections, source copying, transcription/OCR problems and other causes remain untested. No preferred cause is adopted.\n\n## 5. Processing dates are not one historical event\n\nViewer 21/Bates 12189 displays **INPUTBATCH: 1st Batch of 1A1B1C's delivered in August**, **RPTTEXT01: 1**, **EDIT_DATE: 10/30/2003**, **CREATE_DATE: 08/19/2003**, and **SOURCE_ACCN: 2496**. The 1 belongs to RPTTEXT01; the field does not say delivery on August 1. August has no supplied year/day. The footer elsewhere displays May 10, 2004 11:57 a.m.. Preserve those processing/footer labels separately from P_SEIZDATE 09/15/2001, the September 14 letter date and September 22 interview/copy promise.\n\nNo label alone authenticates a delivery recipient/date, physical custody, a particular Commission request, an edit to the historical account, or the completeness of a production. The original schema, batch manifest and actual receipt/version records remain missing. The 21-page container and inclusive 12169–12189 Bates range agree arithmetically; the transcript header/final page separately display internal PAGE 1 / PAGE 19. Different pagination is not proof of missing pages, and matching totals do not authenticate content or audio.\n\n## Next originals and the full work plan\n\nHighest retrieval value: item **1A-1A64148**, **SOURCE_ACCN 2496**, the exact Bates range, original released FD340/transcript facsimiles, actual media/copy/receipt/disposition and the original letter/synopsis. Then compare recorded words and source versions with the conflicting counts, duration/phase descriptions and attribution. Native carrier/operator/recipient/clock/usage/exhibit joins and the GTE paper/Excel 97 diskette remain required. No native audio, original letter, master PDF, confirmed custody or independent clock/vendor test is claimed here.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9e5e7caba71280f37277) preserves all five tracks and original 18 requirements. FAA drafting/knowledge/corrected QFR/receipt/signed-action and separate recommendation-outcome originals remain open. Recorder/materials native-input and empirical tests remain with their technical owner. Steel preservation/transfer/native inventory/attribution and contractor-originals remain open. This source acquisition and reading advances TEL provenance and retrieval; it closes none of the original 18 criteria.\n\nHigh confidence attaches to the displayed fields and the retained captures within their stated scope. Fidelity to original documents/media, complete custody and historical event truth remain unverified. The next originals could weaken or strengthen particular interpretations; source count, arithmetic or publication is not proof of conspiracy. Earlier contradictory observations, sources, reports, shared registers/workplan and public history remain unchanged.\n\n[Reading/checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-66fe20eca7a70a0dc9f7), [verification limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d64aad0c94df9f5257fa) and [actual addition diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0ec681425cd0f1ab384d) accompany the notes. Only appropriate original research, selected safe values and source links form this redundant public derivative. Raw privacy-marked source captures/full speech, incidental personal/contact/financial/access/signature data, private case material and credentials are excluded. No account/gate bypass, outreach, fees, new request/filing, mailbox access, experiment, source overwrite, deletion, private push or history rewrite occurred. Publication is established separately by the actual AveLyra account/commit/ref/all-file receipts; no independent audit acceptance is implied.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 0b37db336b1a5c981176ca0f702cd2334636f7898dd85da2245cc9d19fd58381 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-a26cf2f0058df413\"></a>\n### Charlotte's SERO evidence inventory identifies original media, statements and copy routes\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-sero-evidence-inventory-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-4ffef5d5b99c9a830162).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY a26cf2f0058df413e10f1c858aff910cf688cb61c636a2861372dfb6578dd961 -->\n# Charlotte's SERO evidence inventory identifies original media, statements and copy routes\n\nOctober 31, 2026, America/New_York; reading November 1 UTC. **TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** The Woodward original-note search did not recover his signed notes. It instead led to previously uninspected pages in an already held compilation: a September 13, 2001 Charlotte FBI communication describing a separate **AA11/Ong/SERO** evidence chain. It names original-format media, original statements, system/configuration backup and particular copy/transfer routes. The underlying media, statements, receipts and native logs remain unacquired; this is a more precise retrieval map, not an authenticated call reconstruction.\n\n## Source and exact reading boundary\n\nThe [public PDF mirror](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=30) is a third-party reproduction of FBI records, acquired October 27 UTC: **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 **e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa**. That hash identifies the preserved mirror body, not native agency custody or original media. All **eight EC pages**, physical **30–37**, a header page followed by printed internal pages **2–8**, footers **000000429–000000436**, were visually read at **140 dpi**. The other 65 compilation pages were not comprehensively read. Existing ordinary text served only as a locator; no new OCR, hidden/redacted-text recovery or fresh PDF download.\n\nThe initial plan mistakenly assumed the first five identified pages completed the communication. Page 34 visibly continued. Before further image reading, an existing-index boundary check located its end and the scope was prospectively extended to eight images. The initial plan, five-page qualification and later extension remain preserved locally. No unread page is claimed read, and completing this EC is not a complete-production or native-authentication finding. [Source/image fingerprints](CITATIONS.md#nov04-052f27c065872a7b0eef), [page/item pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-634fada0afa011e2381d), [actual scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e35e8fb8f37c78050e6e).\n\n## Precise case and holder references\n\n**Physical 30/header page** prints **09/13/2001**, From **Charlotte / Raleigh Resident Agency**, case **265D-NY-280350-CE (Pending)**. It references **265D-NY-280350 Serial 187**, **DL267**, **CE66** and **CE233**. Serial 187 is a referenced lead/record, not proved to be this EC's own serial. Pending is a historical label, not present case status. The administrative paragraph says Charlotte retained the original evidence it obtained. It addresses the Director's Office/SIOC and several field offices; address-list inclusion is not demonstrated receipt. P01.\n\n## Original media and statements, with their labels intact\n\nThe inventory on **physical 30–32/header and printed 2–3** identifies:\n\n- **Item 1(A):** an original CD-ROM recording of the Ong call in **WAV** format. **Item 1(B):** an original CD-ROM recording in both a **Rockwell Industries format** and **WAV Format**. These are the inventory's labels, not inspected files, known codecs or two independently captured calls. Both sit under a holding labelled **1B**; item 1(A) is not itself a classification of 1A evidence. P02.\n- **Item 3(A–H):** eight statement entries with handwritten, typed and otherwise unspecified forms. The list expressly distinguishes an **unsigned** typed version and a **signed** typed version for one named participant, and original/typed versions for other participants. Eight entries do not mean eight independent witnesses or eight separate corroborations. No actual statement or signature was inspected. P03.\n- **Item 4:** one original **4 mm DDS 90 tape** described as snapshots of the automated call distribution system **as of 0130EST, 9/13/01**, containing **ACD Operation System** and **ACD configuration settings**. Preserve the September 13 date and EST label. This is not demonstrated September 11 effective configuration, calibrated time, call audio, a complete event archive or a validated forensic system image. P04.\n\nThese are separate media, statement and configuration targets. A digital carrier/storage description does not authenticate the contents, and the word original in an inventory does not prove a bit-level native acquisition or full custody chain.\n\n## Copies, interview notes, activity reports and future dispatch\n\n**Physical 32–34/internal 3–5** lists copies of interview/transcription reports as enclosures. It also says original FD-302s and specified **1A** materials would be sent separately **at a future date**: work-copy CD-ROMs, original FBI interview notes and **AA Activity Reports for Minter and Sadler** described as showing exact call times. The word exact is a source characterization, not verified calibration. Original operator statements, FBI interview notes, report copies, work-copy audio and original-format media remain distinct. A promise of future dispatch is not actual dispatch, delivery, receipt or present custody. P05.\n\n**Physical 36/internal 7, first paragraph** reports copies of documentation passing through AA's Dallas Security Headquarters to the FBI Dallas Division, while original versions and a system copy on hard media were placed with Charlotte. This gives additional reported copy-holder routes. It does not establish identical bytes, an intact receipt trail, delivery of the promised 1A package or a complete forensic image. P06.\n\nThe last paragraph on **physical 37/internal 8** says the particular Serial-187 Cary/Charlotte leads should be considered covered. That is not a global FBI closure, completed recipient delivery, complete records search, destruction authorization or proof every laboratory/technical question was answered. P07.\n\n## Time sources, recording limit and routing uncertainty\n\n**Physical 34/internal 5** explicitly says a witness's remembered call time differed from AA telephone-system records and that times in the EC were estimated using the records custodian's knowledge rather than the interviewed witnesses. The same page uses **approximately 8:20 A.M.** earlier, then **precisely 8:20 A.M., EST** for recording start and **approximately 8:44 A.M., EST** for call end. Preserve the source's changing precision, without choosing a controlling timestamp, converting EST/EDT or aligning it to a desired event. P08.\n\n**Physical 32, enclosure 10** describes a four-minute transcription of an approximate twenty-five (25) call; that particular phrase omits an explicit duration unit. **Physical 35/internal 6** explicitly describes a **25-minute** call. Both readings remain; no unit is silently inserted into the earlier line and no exact duration is calculated from approximate clock claims. P09.\n\nThe EC attributes the **four-minute recording stop** to a pre-programmed default timer, while describing a longer call. **Physical 36** reports a negative check for an additional automatic quality-control recording and describes the same four-minute limit for a separate unrelated call. These are reported technical/search accounts from one communication, not independent configuration tests. The original audio, native settings, audit/change history, extraction method and alternate-recording search logs were not inspected. No deliberate truncation or complete absence of other recordings is established. P10.\n\n**Physical 35–36/internal 6–7** records a manager's initial assumption about a direct shortcut route, a reported AT&T Digital no-record response for such a call, and proposed routing through the general reservations number using either a cellular or flight phone. Preserve all accounts. This is a provider response relayed through another person; the actual carrier query, scope, raw result and call-leg join are missing. It does not establish that no call occurred, select cellular versus onboard service, or transfer SERO/Rockwell receiving-system semantics to GTE ACIS or another flight. The exact shortcut/destination numbers are not reproduced here. P11.\n\n## Next records and evidentiary strength\n\nThe discriminating originals are: the two described media items and their format/export histories; the DDS backup and associated extraction/version/change records; individual original statements versus FBI interview notes; the two operators' activity reports and native time definitions; the promised 1A-package dispatch/receipt; Charlotte/Dallas/SIOC copy manifests; and the actual AT&T route-query and alternate-recording search records. Reproduced inventory, narrative and transmittal passages from this single chain are not independent corroboration of the call or its timing.\n\nThe [Woodward signed-note target](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/e357f0778da4001ee9ea41d56ce77bae974e862f/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-signed-notes-continuations-2026-10-31/README.md), the separate Jefferson Post-it notes and original letter/media, and all native caller/operator/recipient/clock/exhibit joins remain open. The EC's unrelated customer/reservation allegations and personal information are excluded from this public review; no ethnicity-based or identity inference is adopted. None of these records establishes fabrication, concealment, foreknowledge, coordination or attack participation. The listed originals could support, qualify or contradict the reports.\n\nAll original five tracks and 18 requirements remain open or partial. New progress is source-level identification of native media/configuration, note, copy-holder and timing-method targets; source counts, hashes and publication are not historical proof or completion. [Comparison](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b16138300da50ae3533f), [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ac8942dbac56f005b1d6), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5940743f0ee54f76080c), [verification limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f988244debc23548d4d8) and [addition diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-de1bafd95cee2a37d3cb) accompany the safe redundant notes. Raw marked PDFs/images/text, signatures, personal/contact/financial data, private case/correspondence/strategy and credentials are excluded. No outreach, fees, new request/filing, experiment, mailbox, deletion, overwrite, private push or history rewrite.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY a26cf2f0058df413e10f1c858aff910cf688cb61c636a2861372dfb6578dd961 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-e0ce31674748d495\"></a>\n### An FBI interview continuation identifies signed and dated call notes\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-signed-notes-continuations-2026-10-31` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-21e523d5a1bc7162d775).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY e0ce31674748d495f3463b458d970bc9268d9815464dee3bcdee33f576aea8e4 -->\n# An FBI interview continuation identifies signed and dated call notes\n\nOctober 31, 2026, America/New_York; reading November 1 UTC. **TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** Three previously unread continuation-page images in the held official FBI releases were inspected. One supplies a specific original-record target: notes Woodward reportedly made during the Sweeney conversation, signed and dated, and gave to the interviewing agent. The notes themselves, their item number and present retention remain unverified.\n\n## The handoff statement is a record lead, not the recovered notes\n\n[Part02 physical page 25](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=25), internal page **2**, dated **09/11/01**, names **Michael Woodward** and displays case **265A-NY-280350-302**. Its third body paragraph says he made notes while speaking with Sweeney, signed and dated them, and gave them to the interviewing agent. The footer shows **REQ. #35-13** and **000000391**. This is an interview report's handoff statement, not an attached original note, inspected signature, intake receipt or proof of present FBI custody. P01.\n\n[Part02 physical page 57](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=57) reproduces the selected same body claims, named witness, printed date, case and internal-page label, with footer **000000586** and the same request tag. Preserve both footer labels and separate page-image hashes. They are two reproduced versions of the account, not two independent witnesses, two handoffs or proof of two note sets. No whole-document/byte equivalence or cross-redaction reconstruction was performed. P02.\n\nThe next discriminator is the actual signed/dated note set and its attachment, intake, copying, transfer and retention records. A declared handoff is more specific than a generic reference to missing telephone evidence, but it does not authenticate the original notes' content or establish whether they agree with the interview summary. The original notes could corroborate, qualify or conflict with the later account. No preferred result is assumed.\n\n## Keep the caller, artifact and service distinctions\n\nThe preceding paragraph on the same two pages reports Sweeney describing **Ong** speaking to someone on an air phone. That is a reported observation concerning a different caller. It does not itself identify the device or service Sweeney used, classify every AA11 call, validate a carrier row, or supply an authenticated recording. Do not transfer a device description from one caller to another. P03.\n\nThese Woodward/Sweeney notes are a separate record target from Jefferson's brief Post-it notes described in the [newly inspected May 11, 2004 memorandum](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886438/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-Todd-Beamer-Fdr-5-11-04-MFR-Lisa-Jefferson-416). The [preceding review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b6923d4d9c874ab71fe88112f401d5279caaeb95/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-operator-notes-mfr-2026-10-31/README.md) retains that reported FBI holding, its limited-value qualification and missing custody join. Neither note set is the typed synopsis, September 14 letter, carrier spreadsheet, recorded follow-up conversation or original in-flight audio. A specific original-note crosswalk is needed; a common agency or similar label is insufficient. P04.\n\n## The Jefferson continuation preserves the relay and timing limits\n\n[Part01 physical page 21](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-01-of-08/at_download/file#page=21), internal page **2**, names **Lisa Jefferson**, prints **09/11/2001**, and displays case **265D-NY-280350**. Its footer shows **REQ. #35-13** and **000000128**. The first paragraph records a last exchange at **9:00 a.m. Central time**, then another **twenty minutes** of silent/open connection before disconnection. It also reports tracking equipment indicating service through a Pittsburgh transceiver. The transceiver claim is not independently checked aircraft position or a calibrated event clock. P05.\n\nThe second paragraph describes a separate Verizon relay call **approximately five minutes later**, estimated at **9:30 a.m. Central time**, continuing until **approximately 9:43 a.m.** It expressly says Jefferson could not hear the other passenger directly and received information second hand through the Verizon employee. Preserve this scope beside the later MFR's tentative account about another operator possibly listening to that other call. Different participants and legs have not been joined, and no contradiction or reconciliation is imposed. P06.\n\nThe **15-minute** silent/open estimate in the May 2004 MFR, the earlier **20-minute** account and the follow-up reproduction's **about 10 more minutes** remain separate source readings. These are not synchronized or summed into a timeline here. The newly read copy is not a new independent witness or a new measurement of an already documented estimate. The printed **265D** case is retained for this form; it is not silently substituted for the **265A** label on the different Woodward form or the later follow-up record. P07.\n\n## Actual scope and remaining work\n\nThe three newly viewed images are **part01 physical 21** and **part02 physical 25/57**, rendered at **140 dpi** from the two already held official-hosted PDFs. No new download, OCR, whole-release rereading, hidden/redacted text recovery or detail crop was performed. Context first pages **20/24/56** were previously read; they are not counted again. The continuation headers provide printed internal-page, name/date and case context; adjacency alone is not used to authenticate a complete record or production. No native carrier, note, media, manifest or office log was acquired. [Source fingerprints](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1446b3eb0063141f3886), [pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-17f51b7b2582f537c84d), [scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5436b0492cc9fca400d7).\n\nHigh confidence attaches to the selected visible fields and handoff paragraph in these preserved copies. The reported historical handoff, exact note identity, completeness and present custody have not been independently authenticated. Reproductions, interview summaries and later recollections are not independent corroboration. No missing-record, false-call, concealment, motive, coordination or attack-participation conclusion follows from the note reference, clock estimates or different footer labels.\n\nAll original five tracks and 18 requirements remain open or partial. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-68f62563f4751903d67c) retain the individual note sets, originals/receipts, complete production, letter/media and carrier/operator/clock/exhibit joins. [Comparison](CITATIONS.md#nov04-46663da5d242cee9158e), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-24a1400e2fd8192475c9), [verification limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2fc719676e37e34c4269) and [additive diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f36f6f0a753aac348a1f) preserve this supplement without altering prior evidence or public history. Only selected appropriate original research and source links are published; raw PDFs/images/extractions, personal/contact/financial/signature information, private correspondence/case material, litigation strategy and credentials remain excluded.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY e0ce31674748d495f3463b458d970bc9268d9815464dee3bcdee33f576aea8e4 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-8e36df708b91ae3e\"></a>\n### Sweeney telephone reports: preserve service descriptions, separate clocks and missing recording custody\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-sweeney-source-conflicts-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-612e337c43c42aaf5bd9).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 8e36df708b91ae3e8be152d221a5a6208c01602685ac52474127c62529979296 -->\n# Sweeney telephone reports: preserve service descriptions, separate clocks and missing recording custody\n\nNovember 2, 2026, America/New_York; reading continued November 3 UTC. **TEL01–TEL04 / AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110.** Two newly read bodies in the held official FBI release describe Brian Sweeney contacts differently from the already held May 13, 2004 Commission briefing. This review source-pins those accounts and their limits. It acquires no new carrier export or original recording and does not authenticate caller identity, aircraft, service, clock or historical cause.\n\n## What the records actually say\n\nThe [official FBI part02, physical 61/footer 000000603](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=61) reports a live conversation with Sweeney's mother. The next [physical 62/footer 000000604](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=62) concerns a message on his wife's answering machine. These are different reported contacts, not duplicate descriptions of one established call. Recipient names appear unmasked in these public records, but personal biographies, addresses, telephone numbers and message content are unnecessary here and excluded from this derivative.\n\n| Source / exact locator | Service description | Time and its stated basis | Qualification |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FBI physical 61/footer603, first substantive event paragraph | Phone aboard a plane, **“possibly from his cell phone”** | **8:58 a.m.**, read on the recipient's **kitchen-stove clock** at the call | The report also says he **may have been** on United Flight175. It is not a carrier record or clock-calibration certificate. |\n| FBI physical 62/footer604, final substantive paragraph | Message described as **“made from his cell phone aboard the plane”** | Message left at **approximately 8:58 a.m.**, as recorded by the **answering machine** | This is the interview report's device/service description; no underlying handset, carrier return or original message was examined here. |\n| [Official May13 briefing, physical 3, GTE Airfone table, third data row](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/legislative/rg-148/2524787/t-0148-911MFR-00216.pdf#page=3) | **GTE Airfone Calls**, seat-bank **31 AB**, Brian Sweeney, wife recipient | **8:58:45**, length **27 sec**, under **all Times Eastern AM** | A Commission memorandum of the DOJ briefing and reconstruction, not a native event-to-recipient join. |\n| Same briefing, physical 3, fourth data row | **GTE Airfone Calls**, **31 AB**, Brian Sweeney, parents recipient | **9:00:02**, length **60 sec**, same Eastern label | The row is attributed to the parents, but the worksheet linking that row to the particular earlier interview is not held. |\n\nThe [briefing's first page](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/legislative/rg-148/2524787/t-0148-911MFR-00216.pdf#page=1) says all Flight175 calls were made through Airfone. It attributes the reconstruction to GTE records and engineers, passenger cellular-record examination, and recipient/family interviews. Its second page says DOJ added caller names to other spreadsheet versions using recipient interviews. Those statements provide a reported methodology and a competing service classification. They do not make the event-to-person assignments independent of the interviews or verify the underlying implementation.\n\n**Preserve the discrepancy:** the early reports use qualified or affirmative cell-phone language; the later briefing assigns these contacts to Airfone. The live-call report's kitchen-clock8:58 remains beside the later parents-row9:00:02; the answering-machine approximately8:58 remains beside the wife-row8:58:45. Do not silently correct either interview with the later chart, join contacts on a surname alone, treat the two early8:58 strings as one calibrated instant, or adopt a preferred service or time. These are source-described contacts and candidate associations, not verified common-event identities. No numerical clock offset or impossible-overlap result is calculated.\n\nThe live-call report also attributes to the caller a belief that the plane was somewhere over Ohio and says the recipient saw the second impact on television after their call. Those are reported statements, not independently timed aircraft-position or live-broadcast evidence. They are retained as contextual qualifications, not converted into a different flight identity, foreknowledge or an authenticated clock. The source's uncertain Flight175 association stays uncertain.\n\n## The recording lead is specific; the custody evidence is still missing\n\nPhysical62 describes an answering-machine message. It does **not** supply an actual audio file, tape, evidence-item identifier, FBI receipt, copy/examination log or retention disposition in the paragraph inspected. Seek those records, including a copy with its source device/settings and any time-check documentation. A recorded-message assertion is not proof of FBI acquisition or present survival. The separate photograph handoff described on physical61 is **not** an audio handoff; its private image and biography are excluded.\n\nThe pages display case **265A-NY-280350**, **REQ. #35-13**, footers **000000603 / 000000604**, and distinct upper date strings **9/28/01 / 10/2/01**, each above lower **9/11/01**. The date roles are not labeled on the inspected faces; this review does not declare them transcription/interview dates or a historical date contradiction. Bottom handwritten302-like controls were inspected in two detail crops but are not adopted as reliable exact identifiers or assigned an evidence/serial role. Use the official PDF, footer and visible case/request references rather than a guessed handwritten locator.\n\n## Additional recording references: useful provenance, repeated substance\n\nThe same bounded reading covered [physical38–40/footer444–446](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=38), a September12 Gonzalez report, and [41–43/footer447–449](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=41), a September12 Minter report. The Gonzalez report prints **DL267; CE66; AND CE233**; the Minter report prints **DL267 AND CE66**. Shared printed references are retrieval leads, not proof that two reports refer to an identical tape or independently corroborate its contents.\n\nGonzalez's physical39/internal2 describes the emergency-button **Rockwell telephone recording device**, a recording capacity of **up to four minutes**, overall contact of **approximately23–25 minutes**, provision of the recorded portion to the FBI, and a separate unrecorded portion. This is a report of provision, not an actual intake receipt, original recording or completed examination. Minter's physical43/internal3 qualifies whether some details were heard directly or learned later; she did not hear the end and estimates being on the call over20minutes. Preserve those limits when attributing words or using an interview to validate a transcript.\n\nThese repeat previously reviewed Ong recording/interview substance and **are not new independent corroboration**. The approximately7:59 initial-recipient and approximately8:20 supervisor descriptions also overlap the already published interview comparison. They are not newly measured start times. Physical27/footer401 overlaps the already read retrospective playback account. No new playback, audio comparison, flight-clock reconstruction or native-media authentication was performed. Different callers sharing the surname Sweeney, including the separately reviewed AA11 attendant account, are not merged with the Brian Sweeney reports here.\n\n## What could distinguish the explanations\n\nAn interview/device-label error, a later compilation/recipient-row error, approximate or differently set clocks, a different event/leg association, or an additional contact are **untested possibilities**, not adopted explanations. Repeated names, matching minute labels and an official summary do not decide among them. The strongest present limitation is that these records are recollections and a later investigative reconstruction; the needed underlying joins and time bases are missing. A genuine contrary carrier return, authenticated receipt or corrected source could change the assessment.\n\nKeep these as TODOs without stopping other available work:\n\n1. Agency-held originals and attachments corresponding to footers603/604; interview notes, source-date fields, amendments and document-control crosswalk.\n2. Answering-machine recording, source/copy/extraction details, FBI intake/evidence/custody/analysis records, and retained derivatives or disposition.\n3. Native Airfone/cellular returns and the exact worksheets matching the two Sweeney-attributed rows to the contacts; retain failed, negative and unassigned records too. Request the basis for the cell-phone descriptions and the later Airfone classification, without presuming either true.\n4. Device settings and contemporaneous checks of the kitchen clock, answering-machine time and carrier timestamps. An uncalibrated household clock is not an aircraft clock.\n5. DL267/CE66/CE233 report-to-media crosswalk, Rockwell export/configuration and actual receipt/copy/examination/retention records. Do not transfer a code from one report to another because some codes overlap.\n\nNo new request, contact, fee or filing occurred. The court's selected UA93 asset comparison is complete and was not rerun; denied routes and the failed automated-transcription method were not retried. FAA signed disposition/correction, telephone native joins, steel decisions/attribution, and the recorder/materials work assigned to the technical owner remain open under all five tracks/eighteen substantive criteria. Publication does not complete those criteria or establish wrongdoing.\n\n## Scope and preservation\n\nThe official FBI PDF remains **5,561,167 bytes /78 pages**, SHA-256 **055a7ed1294c42b976cc98a65dd0a8a80d677723fa4300f0fea38fb41590bb51**, acquired October31,2026 UTC. The May13 UA175 PDF remains **515,215 bytes /3 pages**, SHA-256 **e581efca33a84473d2f08f577f328123759b176d2513c47adc1ba958bd9c980c**, acquired October29 UTC. Official delivery establishes the provenance of these released entities, not the historical truth of every assertion. Exact access times, URLs, page/paragraph/table locators and source forms are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-42574d849f2b15b75fbd) and [LOCATORS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f0c2c27cd211f6c3931e).\n\n**Ten unique FBI faces** were inspected:27,38–43,61–63; two additional crops show only the controls on61/62. This is not full78-page reading. The independent allegation following the Gonzalez continuation on physical40 and the unrelated biography/report beginning on63 are excluded. No concealed/redacted text or masked identity was reconstructed. The already read May13 memorandum was reused; only its page3 table was re-inspected in this unit. All originals, earlier candidate readings and prior reports remain unchanged.\n\nOne local procedure error is preserved separately: the initial renderer was launched before the two media-path checks had returned terminal status. Both checks subsequently returned verified Intel paths and the producer completed before image adoption; source and image hashes were checked. This is an execution-order defect in this review, not a historical evidence anomaly. The later context render was awaited before reading. No claim of flawless preflight ordering is made.\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2154fc83a34eb0ed5a35), [READING-SCOPE.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-53e52e286e47f76e6ebf), [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3a070af3535939445b89), [OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d19e2c4dc78f84431f81) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e90c04776f37f30e8060) distinguish accepted source readings, unaccepted handwriting, reused evidence, preservation checks and missing native inputs. The exact additive [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0cac18d5a9f1a3e6f7f2) is against the immediately preceding preserved combined review, identified by its hash. Text comparison, PDF/source reading, input-hash checks and remote Git verification are separate operations. No historical call test or physical/independent replication is claimed.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 8e36df708b91ae3e8be152d221a5a6208c01602685ac52474127c62529979296 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-40ff313e5bda5b1c\"></a>\n### Ong-labelled records: a documented CD-to-tape conversion and unresolved transcript differences\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-transcript-generation-chain-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-85eb7973037c6f45b2db).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 40ff313e5bda5b1c495e4c51219859dc939eef82c924a05d015c63a484e25b26 -->\n# Ong-labelled records: a documented CD-to-tape conversion and unresolved transcript differences\n\nNovember 2, 2026. TEL02/TEL04; AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. The previously unexamined continuations identify recording-generation and engineering-record targets. They do not establish altered audio, an impossible call or a completed source-authentication test.\n\n## What was acquired and read\n\nThe [official FBI September release, part 04](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-04-of-08) was retrieved as an 18-page PDF: **601,286 bytes**, SHA-256 **854bf3408241640a4b5549fba79b7a1f8a9a2639267488b9db3132bd08ac3caf**. The [previous study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/abefdac15a5474b2cba2407dc7d0e6bcd58ead59/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-playback-custody-2026-10-31/README.md) had viewed selected browser images, without acquiring this binary or reading pages 3–16.\n\nThis unit visually read pages **1–17**: fourteen previously unread pages, plus three context pages. Page 18's separate playback record was not reread. This is a released reproduction, not native audio or a complete FBI production. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f3dcdc3c4fdeabd28cfe) records the actual acquisition and reading scope; [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1da28d74a35bec1c2e41) supplies physical/internal-page, footer and passage locators.\n\n## Two source chains must stay distinct\n\n**First record, physical 1–9, DL-336:** its cover has transcription date **09/12/2001**, but investigation/dictation fields **09/11/2001**. Page 2 opens a retrospective session at **12:28 p.m. Central Time**, asks about the morning and requests playback. Page 3 introduces the playback. After a recording-concluded marker on page 7, questions and recollection continue through page 8. These are different source roles and dates, not a reason to classify the whole report as contemporaneous airborne dialogue. Page 9 has a continuation header/footer with a visually empty body; no cause or missing-content finding follows.\n\n**Second record, physical 10–14, lead controls DL267/CE66:** page 10 explicitly describes material obtained from American Airlines on September 11 and copied **from CD-ROM onto analog audio tape for transcription**. Its transcription/investigation/dictation fields show **09/12/2001**. This supplies a concrete conversion and custody target. It does not supply that CD or tape, file identity, conversion settings, duplication log or fidelity test. The different date fields are retained in their respective roles; neither date authenticates the call clock.\n\n## What the first continuation adds\n\nAt physical **7 / internal 7 / footer 000000406**, after playback ends, a question describes another **five or ten minutes** of conversation and receives an affirmative reply. A speaker then reports that communications staff were checking why recording stopped despite the emergency button remaining on. This is an attributed account of an inquiry, not a completed technical explanation or independently measured duration.\n\nThe earlier [Charlotte EC review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/d5b279a04f2fe18b78548222aea75451bfa7f60a/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-sero-evidence-inventory-2026-10-31/README.md) preserves a later default-timer explanation, four-minute capture and approximately 25-minute call. Keep those accounts alongside the new passage. They could describe a developing inquiry, but that relationship has not been verified. Do not add the durations, select a controlling total or infer deliberate truncation. The actual engineering findings, effective configuration, audit history and source recordings remain missing.\n\nAt physical **8 / footer 000000407**, an interviewer assumes a cellular phone; the reply says the speaker did not know and had not determined it. The question is not evidence of service type. The final exchange also requests **two statements by fax** and receives a promise. The statements, fax transmission and recipient receipt remain concrete original-record targets; a promise is not delivery.\n\n## Selected conflicting transcript readings\n\n| Potentially corresponding passage | DL-336 record | DL267/CE66 transcription |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Injury description after the number-one reference | Physical 5 / footer 000000404: **our passenger is stabbed** | Physical 12 / footer 000000459: **our purser has been stabbed** |\n\nThese are the printed words, not independently heard speech. The reviewed records contain other dialogue and attribution differences; this is **not an exhaustive textual collation** or a sample-aligned audio comparison. Neither wording is selected or silently corrected. Copy generation, source coverage and transcription choices are untested alternatives to an underlying content change. Source media and segment mappings would distinguish them.\n\nThe second transcript also prints **Flight 12** near its opening and later **Flight 11** responses (physical 11–13). Keep the surrounding dialogue; an initial statement or speaker label is not independent aircraft identification. Physical 15–17 begin a separate report and are not an extension of this transcript.\n\n## Evidentiary limits and next work\n\nThe useful advance is an item-level map to the **CD, analog rerecording, recorded interview/playback session, engineering check and promised statements**. It narrows TEL02's retrieval chain. The strongest competing interpretation is ordinary copying/transcription and an evolving technical inquiry. Neither that account nor fabrication is established by these paper records. Related transcripts and an inventory must not be counted as independent authentication of the call.\n\nNo listening, voice identification, native waveform comparison, carrier join, calibrated clock test or full cross-version collation was performed. The previously tested court audio representations remain preserved with their own limits; no master-to-court join is newly demonstrated. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-842a21b2154234d4b648) retain those originals and all five tracks/eighteen substantive requirements. None is newly accepted by acquiring and reading a scan.\n\nPrior reports and conflicting records remain unchanged. [Checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3ef442a616e1911e6b43), [source checks](CITATIONS.md#nov04-01ab95c73c58aa7216f1) and [addition diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f040ecd4b389b00250d4) accompany this redundant public note. Raw scans/images/text/audio, contacts, signatures, masked identities, private case material and correspondence are excluded. No outreach, new request, fee, filing, mailbox access, deletion, overwrite, private push or history rewrite occurred.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 40ff313e5bda5b1c495e4c51219859dc939eef82c924a05d015c63a484e25b26 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-ed579d9453f9a597\"></a>\n### Transfer, relay and declared audio editing: source records kept separate\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-transfer-relay-records-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9cdeef2b6c442e36bba9).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY ed579d9453f9a59771014d8ab102db0ae131fe55747f3153d57a43f2edd14ad9 -->\n# Transfer, relay and declared audio editing: source records kept separate\n\nNovember 2, 2026. TEL02/TEL04; AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. Two source descriptions differ on how Ong's information reached airline operations. The hearing also explicitly announces recording edits and excerpt selection. These are documentary leads; the actual telephone routing and master-to-exhibit chain remain unverified.\n\n## Transfer versus relay\n\nThe reproduced **Craig Marquis FD-302**, physical **4 / internal 1 / footer 000000134**, describes the call as **transferred to central dispatch**. Its transcription/dictation fields show **09/16/2001**, while the investigation field shows **09/11/2001**. These fields have different roles. [Released-file mirror](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=4).\n\nIn the **January 27, 2004 hearing**, printed/physical **106–107**, **Chair Thomas Kean's introduction** instead describes an inability to transfer the call or patch operations personnel into it, with Gonzalez relaying information on another line. That passage is the chair's introductory account, **not Gonzalez's own firsthand testimony**. Her remarks begin later on 107. [Archived Commission transcript](https://govinfo.library.unt.edu/911/archive/hearing7/9-11Commission_Hearing_2004-01-27.pdf#page=106).\n\nBoth descriptions remain unchanged. They do not establish the same telephone leg, phase or use of transfer terminology. Shorthand reporting, different phases, a misunderstanding or an actual routing/account difference are untested possibilities. No source is selected as controlling. The switch/bridge/conference logs, operator records, handset setup, original interview notes and matched recordings would distinguish the alternatives. Neither paper account alone establishes that Marquis directly heard Ong's voice.\n\n## The hearing discloses editing and selection\n\n**Kean's remarks on page 109**, before the calls are played, say:\n\n| Recording described by the chair | Announced scope |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ong to Gonzalez | Entire **four and a half minutes** recorded, as described by the chair. |\n| Gonzalez to operations | Approximately **20 minutes** in duration; **four minutes selected** for the hearing because of time constraints. |\n\nIn a separate paragraph, the chair announces a possible momentary blank and a small edit to protect a family member. That paragraph does not supply a specific file, call-leg or edited-interval mapping. This is affirmative evidence that editing/selection was disclosed. It is a source-reported purpose and scope, not a recovered edit decision list, proof of what was removed, authorization record, original-file comparison or complete audit. It does not establish that the same edits occur in the later court Flash files or explain their previously measured unmatched tail. No audio was listened to or compared here. [Page 109](https://govinfo.library.unt.edu/911/archive/hearing7/9-11Commission_Hearing_2004-01-27.pdf#page=109).\n\nKeep **four and a half** beside the earlier FBI four-minute descriptions; keep **20** beside Gonzalez's own **approximately 23-minute** conversation account on page 108 and the separate earlier approximately 25-minute account. They concern differently described calls, recordings or estimates. Do not combine them into missing minutes or adopt one duration. A disclosed edit could explain a specific feature only after the actual source/export/segment relationship is established.\n\nThe hearing's page 110 also uses **purser** in the injury passage. That is another documentary representation alongside the [earlier passenger/purser comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/17aef02c7d79169234dc04c4a67f38425900ea30/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-transcript-generation-chain-2026-11-02/README.md). It does not authenticate the acoustic word or independently corroborate a shared source.\n\n## Specific originals remain to retrieve\n\nMarquis's report, **mirror 5 / internal 2 / footer 000000135**, says he was unsure but thought his conversation recorded and would check and notify the FBI. That is a proposed verification, not a recovered recording or completed notification. **Mirror 6 / internal 3 / footer 000000136** says he supplied a **copy of his notes and an annotated crew manifest**, referring to an **FD-340 envelope**. The passage does not identify its envelope number. Those actual items and their custody/receipt remain missing.\n\nThe report's approximate **7:25–7:49 a.m.** labels and first-page **Central Standard Time** remain as printed. Its inference that impact was near 7:49 is based on another reported call, not a calibrated event measurement. No zone correction, clock fit or independently measured duration is adopted.\n\n## Handwriting is not enough to authenticate contemporaneous notes\n\nThe compilation's first three handwritten pages refer to other reports, ask retrieval questions and give editing/addition instructions. They have no author/date authenticated in this review. Page 1 points to original typed Cary statements in a **1A file**, with **265D NY 280350 CE / Serial 594**; that is a reference, not the statements themselves. Page 3 points to a report explaining the four-minute limit. These pages are consistent with research/retrieval notes. They are **not established as the contemporaneous call notes** described by Marquis, Woodward or Hanson. Adjacency does not make that join. Unrelated personal assertions are excluded.\n\n## Actual scope, contrary evidence and limits\n\nThe held 73-page mirror was not downloaded again. Five new full pages **1–5** were read; previously read page **6** was reexamined as context. One new archived hearing PDF was acquired, **338,805 bytes / 144 pages**, SHA-256 **705c92312057c1efcfcc272f7480ead285b1dfdb055b37a1cfd937f5b2f84e10**. Only its **106–110** images were read. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8108ed1458ab9213b13a) and [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-70de23a18646fae214cb) separate source layers, page roles and observed claims.\n\nOrdinary copying, imperfect recollection/terminology and expressly announced presentation editing remain competing possibilities. These records establish no fabrication, concealment, unlawful editing, calibrated delay or historical cause. Conversely, the stated editing purpose does not authenticate every derivative or erase differences. The originals could strengthen or weaken those interpretations.\n\nNo native call media, original notes, carrier/office bridge records, editing project, independent voice or clock test was acquired/performed. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ecd52d7e941334afe1b2) retain those inputs and every original five-track/eighteen requirement. Prior records and conflicting values remain unchanged. [Checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-64596e684d4b464300cd), [source verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-075f57d642f971251824) and [addition diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8f3e90b312ddda782026) distinguish acquisition, reading, inference and publication. Raw scans/images/text/audio, signatures, contacts, masked identities, private case material and correspondence are excluded. No outreach, request, fee, filing, mailbox, deletion, overwrite, private push or history rewrite occurred.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY ed579d9453f9a59771014d8ab102db0ae131fe55747f3153d57a43f2edd14ad9 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-c3a55b65083d40b9\"></a>\n### Two UA93 court assets: equal decoded text, different source bytes\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-ua93-court-variants-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3ebbc9cc17670e7a62b9).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY c3a55b65083d40b90aec07506d3fd4a96671c25c04db1f89d2e8b86d42ad6b35 -->\n# Two UA93 court assets: equal decoded text, different source bytes\n\nNovember 2, 2026, America/New_York; execution receipts extend into November 3 UTC. TEL02/TEL04, AUD016-A1, TC05-B105 and TC06-B110. This is a source-version and recording-locator test using an already-held public court archive. It does not recover or authenticate a native telephone recording.\n\n## Why this pair was inspected\n\nThe [preceding FBI review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5c2a489db46eb230900d41b05f1710497e636965/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-recording-custody-relays-2026-11-02/README.md) identifies a reported Gronlund-associated cassette receipt and September 11 handover at the Boston FBI office. Its actual tape/item/receipt/examination/retention chain remains missing. The already-held court prosecution index supplied no literal Gronlund row match; that does not establish what is in the separately distributed presentation archive.\n\nThe [court ZIP](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/flights.zip), linked from the [P200054 exhibit page](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html), contains fourteen members. None is Gronlund-named. It contains the following **two different UA93 members**. They occur in the same held archive; no earlier/later chronology is inferred from their names or order.\n\n| Archive member | Original bytes | SHA-256 | Decoded text definitions |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n| UA93.swf | 3,464,811 | f104ab54492e05550c9e776894e0dbb0d9238039a8f2e9c40be41b1a122d7675 | 420 |\n| UA 93 Calls.swf | 3,464,520 | 9b6703c286cc4e5be8de36728c10bc0fc60dc54e4b732898ba4d4fbfda2fec5e | 420 |\n\n## Actual test result\n\nThe two sources differ in bytes and by **291 bytes of file length**. The existing passive reader recovered **420 text definitions / 379 distinct decoded strings** from each. The **exact multiset of decoded codepoint strings matches**, including every repeated occurrence, NUL and other codepoint. No whitespace, case or source-value normalization was used to obtain that result. The shared multiset digest is `9a4da7dc704250b0cb7d2649a8b47586653bdbe16bfce3ce3a50eb9c1419dede`.\n\nThis establishes equality only in that decoded representation. It does **not** establish equal font shapes, geometry, color, layering, buttons, actions, visited screens, execution order, actual trial display or historical accuracy. The definition IDs and offsets differ. A field location valid in one member cannot be applied blindly to the other. The exact source bytes remain separate and unchanged; no preferred version or cause of the difference is selected.\n\nBoth have SWF-version-5 headers, a declared 12 frames per second, 176 declared root frames and the same stage rectangle. Those are authoring metadata, not call duration, a carrier clock or proof of runtime behavior. Their complete numeric tag-count dictionaries differ: tag code **28** occurs **1,216** times in UA93.swf and **1,190** times in UA 93 Calls.swf. This test does not interpret those instructions or simulate their effect. Equal counts for other tag types would not establish equal tag bodies.\n\n### Gronlund is a stored term, not an authenticated tape\n\nThe decoded definitions contain Gronlund, Glick and Beamer terms in both members. For example, a Gronlund-matching definition appears at **UA93.swf: character ID 679, uncompressed tag offset 282713**, and its raw decoded-string hash matches **UA 93 Calls.swf: ID 1754, offset 3415889**. Other Gronlund-associated definitions occupy different IDs/offsets too. [RESULTS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b5c98e1f569c5a3a15eb) preserves selected safe term coordinates and source hashes; it excludes the full text table, recipient/contact/phone fields and compound text contents.\n\nAn exact term hit is not independent voice/caller identification, proof that a particular text was displayed, or a unique join between the court data and the Boston cassette. These objects may contain a court summary of information derived from several sources; the source-to-exhibit construction/attribution records remain unacquired. Multiple definitions, duplicate labels or two source variants are not multiple calls or independent corroboration.\n\n### No standard SWF sound tags in these two members\n\nThe complete recursive tag traversal found **zero** occurrences of the selected sound-definition/playback/stream tag codes **14, 15, 17, 18, 19, 45 and 89** in either member. Neither inspected object therefore supplies an identified Gronlund recording through those standard sound structures. No sound payload was extracted, decoded or listened to.\n\nThis is not a claim that the full archive, other court holdings or the FBI lack the recording. Other members were inventoried but not decoded in this unit. External media, unused/opaque data, script references and runtime behavior were not evaluated. The objects contain actions, which were counted but neither interpreted nor executed. The cassette's historical existence or fate cannot be inferred from this bounded result.\n\n## What actually ran\n\nThe unchanged court ZIP was verified at **28,304,524 bytes**, SHA-256 `3a1e08b2276dcf0f1bdf5a7071113314776aca4660d73d0cf42fd91f92296801`. Only **UA93.swf** and **UA 93 Calls.swf** were read and preserved as separately named local derivatives; no executable launcher or Flash/ActionScript ran. Both full passive extractions and tag inventories remain local on the verified Intel store. No new download, external query, OCR, ASR, audio/voice/caller/clock inference or native carrier decoding occurred.\n\nThe initial source lookup used a guessed flights.zip filename and failed; the preserved acquisition script identifies the actual court-flights.zip path, which passed the media guard and byte checks. That was our path error, not missing historical evidence. A prior protocol had expressly left the Calls variant uninspected; the bounded reading-history check found no completed comparison of this pair. Completed Lyles/Ong/AA77 tests were not repeated as new findings.\n\nThe equality calculation treats raw decoded strings as a multiset, not a set. Fixed comparator controls require a reordered identical input to match and reject changed multiplicity, case changes and removal of a NUL. These controls test the comparison rule; they are not an independent SWF implementation or historical authentication. The same existing font/tag parser underlies both extraction and reproduction, so parser dependence remains a limitation. The court's original authoring project and a verified actual runtime/display are not available in this test.\n\n## Next records, preservation and scope\n\nThe most useful inputs remain the actual Boston cassette/evidence receipt and source-to-court-recording construction/copy records. For presentation versions, obtain the authoring projects, exact build/delivery/version manifest, source-to-field mapping and any external media references with their source/custody. The present equality result cannot decide why the bytes, IDs or tag counts differ or whether those differences affect a particular visited screen.\n\nAll earlier FBI handling times, source-specific 9:03/9:11 status reports, 9:36/10:45 endpoint accounts, provider/recording assertions and earlier telephone conflicts remain unchanged. No historical discrepancy is resolved, no clock/leg/caller is selected and no inference of fabrication, concealment, motive or attack mechanism follows. A different build/export or assembly is a possible untested explanation, not an adopted one.\n\nAll five original work-plan tracks and eighteen full requirements remain open or partial. Existing Keyton/usage/court sources and completed technical-owner work remain recognized. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-09526c73e87ca9f44faa), [source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-85f020bead4bdd8ca6b5), [method](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5a8f7153227c76070674), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-169ef0f6d15dfa802358), [verification](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d78066c33f56117bfbfd) and the [actual additive diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-424b20a1568cddf47da5) distinguish the performed source test from missing originals and unperformed empirical tests. Raw media, full text, contacts, recipient/personnel/signature information, masked identities, private case/correspondence and internal coordination are excluded from the public derivative. No outreach/request/fee/mailbox, deletion, overwrite, private push, merge or history rewrite occurred.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY c3a55b65083d40b90aec07506d3fd4a96671c25c04db1f89d2e8b86d42ad6b35 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-8f2176657a63cef6\"></a>\n### WF1899: a voicemail-access lead with unlocated collection and message identities\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-wf1899-voicemail-access-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7d94138a78f25839c985).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 8f2176657a63cef6b70b692883cbe88d94419db3ccf59601ae177ecf887c43c3 -->\n# WF1899: a voicemail-access lead with unlocated collection and message identities\n\nA newly read FBI-form record, **WF1899**, reports that **Ted Olson had new voicemail at his former law firm** and that his former secretary would provide access to the FBI. Its follow-up instructs contact with the firm's office administrator **“FOR ACCESS TO MAIL OF OLSON.”** This supplies a concrete office-message/access/disposition target for the telephone investigation.\n\n**The record does not identify who left the messages or say they were Barbara Olson's calls from Flight 77. It does not document completed access, collected audio or a final result.** The difference between **VOICE MAIL** in the intake and **MAIL** in the instruction remains preserved. No message medium, sender, caller, flight or carrier-row identity is selected from context alone.\n\n## Exact source and reading\n\n[Public reproduction, physical 63–65](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=63), production footers **000000761–763**. All three full-size page faces were newly read on **November 2, 2026**, after a bounded reuse check. The earlier contact-sheet view was navigation, not a full-page reading.\n\nThe unchanged source has **73 pages**, **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`, acquired **2026-10-27T13:40:38.310907+00:00**. It is a **third-party public reproduction of FBI-form records**, not an independently authenticated FBI master/native intake database or complete production. No new source download or public search occurred. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b51bc4e656291758be75) pins the page-image identities and actual scope; raw scans/images and private-office contact details are excluded from publication.\n\n## What the intake and lead establish\n\n[Physical 63, Event, footer 000000761](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=63), reports a September11 interview of Ted Olson, identifies Barbara Olson as his wife and a Flight 77 passenger, then says that on **09/13/01** he advised of **“NEW MESSAGES ON HIS VOICE MAIL AT HIS OLD LAW FIRM”** and that his former secretary **“WOULD PROVIDE ACCESS TO THESE CALLS TO THE FBI.”**\n\nThe paragraph's wife/flight context does not identify the senders or contents of those new messages. “New” is not a message timestamp or proof of when a call occurred. The future access statement is not actual delivery, an evidence receipt, a recording/transcript, speaker authentication or a completed investigative finding. The underlying source conversation and message records remain necessary.\n\n[Physical 64, footer 000000762](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=64), marks **Lead Required? YES**. [Physical 65, Set Lead 1, footer 000000763](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=65), records **WF1899**, **WFO / Washington, DC**, and a direction to contact the **office administrator at Gibson Dunn & Crutcher** **“FOR ACCESS TO MAIL OF OLSON.”** The private contact name and masked assignee are not reproduced or reconstructed.\n\nThe instruction says **MAIL**; the intake says **VOICE MAIL**. It does not explicitly say to copy audio, export a voicemail database, collect email or seize physical mail. Possible shorthand, different requested material and an incomplete source description remain untested possibilities; none is chosen. The original task context, attachments and actual response would clarify the intended medium. The source's former-secretary and office-administrator roles are also not silently equated to one person.\n\nThis is a **contact/access directive**, distinct from [HQ1492's explicit request to obtain a recording](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2f363700f6b7010a7927a4794ba9972f09385dbe/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-hq1492-recording-request-2026-11-02/README.md). That comparison concerns wording and work stages. It does not join these records to one message, person, recipient or carrier event. Neither an offered access route nor two lead controls constitute independent confirmation of a call or evidence of failed follow-up.\n\n## Preserve dates, clocks and identifiers\n\n| Location / field | Literal value or qualified reading | Limit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Physical 63, header Date | **10/16/2001** | Document-header role; creation/export history unverified. |\n| Physical 63, Information Received | **09/13/2001, 10:30 AM** | Intake field, not authenticated message-left time. |\n| Physical 63, Event Date / Time | **09/13/2001 / 10:30 AM** | Source event field; specific clock/field semantics unverified. |\n| Physical 65, Assignment | **09/13/2001 at 2:15 AM** | Printed assignment label, not proof of completed contact. |\n| Physical 63/65, typed control | **WF1899** | Identifier, not authentication of contents/outcome. |\n| Physical 63, handwritten bottom notation | Read as **WF3089** | Author/date/function and any alias relationship unknown. |\n| Physical 63, case | **265A-NY-280350-WF (PENDING)** | Source text; not verified present status. |\n\nThe **2:15 AM** assignment label is earlier on the printed date than the **10:30 AM** receipt/event labels. Preserve them without changing AM to PM, assuming a common clock, calculating a delay or selecting an explanation. Date/time differences could involve distinct field meanings, source entry/import history or other causes; those remain untested. None establishes when the reported messages were actually left. Native creation/edit/routing/assignment history, field/clock definitions and original submissions are the discriminating records.\n\nPhysical 63 also labels **Source: OLSON, TED**, **Method of Contact: Telephone/Radio**, **To: WFO**, **From: WFO**. These identify record context; they are not the original interview, a carrier record or an executed access receipt. Typed and handwritten identifiers are preserved without treating them as aliases, replacement controls, separate investigations or separate calls.\n\n## What remains to be tested\n\nPriority targets are the original source/contact report, native WF1899 and cross-reference/routing history; the actual office-contact interview/lead response and completion/disposition; any consent, access or collection documentation; original messages and metadata, export/copy/receipt/inventory/custody records; transcripts/examinations and final findings, including negative and inconclusive results. Relevance to a particular flight call requires independently supported message/caller/carrier/session/canvass joins.\n\nThese could show relevant passenger-related messages, unrelated messages, an inaccurate or incomplete intake, unavailable material, or a successful or unsuccessful collection. They are untested alternatives. This unit cannot establish a recovered Barbara Olson recording, a new confirmed flight call, fabricated calls, deliberate noncollection, missing evidence throughout the FBI file or wrongdoing. A recorded access opportunity and no outcome on these three pages are not a case-wide absence finding.\n\n## Work completed and verification limits\n\nThree full source faces were read; no whole 73-page audit, new OCR, audio/ASR, technical-owner experiment, profile search, private-case/mailbox access, outreach, request or fee occurred. [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a7006ab57c3379a03c79) has four related analyst entries from one unit, not four independent confirmations. Private personnel/contact identifiers, raw/full source text and images remain outside the derivative.\n\n[verify.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1a7093ca8759b5f78a1e) checks declared source/image/derivative bytes, manually entered page/field/value consistency, all 18 TODOs and exact predecessor preservation. It does not independently transcribe pixels, authenticate audio, identify callers/messages, calibrate clocks or prove access/collection/disposition. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0f892c51875915c42ac4) records actual runs. The original PDF and preceding review remain unchanged; [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e6dfe197c61f2ee65b6e) is the actual additive text diff. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c800b528aec580249d4d) records the request-by-request disposition.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ca1f73f84bb486a3fd57) carries forward the new WF1899 originals and all five tracks/18 original requirements, including previous HQ1492/WF334/serial3255/print/engineering targets. No original-record criterion or whole investigation is completed by this reading or publication. Missing inputs remain TODOs; publication is separate from native authentication and independent audit.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 8f2176657a63cef6b70b692883cbe88d94419db3ccf59601ae177ecf887c43c3 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-6d58b01ca5b5c1a0\"></a>\n### WF334 name check: a court-presentation candidate, not a verified message\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-wf334-court-name-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-834312042eb24b493de3).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 6d58b01ca5b5c1a01e7507c3f66f3805d46bc167f42b2e6af62ddc4e9ba38c81 -->\n# WF334 name check: a court-presentation candidate, not a verified message\n\nThe held court presentation contains **“Reuben, Todd”** and separate **“Reuben” / “Todd”** text definitions. The previously reviewed FBI-form tip **WF334** reports **“TODD RUBEN,”** described there as a passenger on **Flight #77**. Preserve both spellings. This is a specific identity-check lead; **the records have not been joined to the same person, message or call**. It is not yet a demonstrated contradiction about one established individual.\n\n## Exact source trail\n\nThe [official court page for prosecution exhibit P200054](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) describes a Flight 77 summary of crew identities, passenger seat assignments and telephone calls, and expressly also includes information about the other three hijacked flights. The complete held HTML is **2,117 bytes**, SHA-256 `866887c38f78c1f5b68ab73a695ae5345812eaf53a3e34da240f5345a1cd96c5`. Exact saved-file lines: **25** (prosecution exhibits), **45** (P200054), **51** (description), **73** (ZIP link). These are local HTML line numbers, not transcript pages. The separate HTML receipt lacks an access timestamp; none is invented.\n\nThe [court archive](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/flights.zip) was acquired **October 27, 2026, 13:40:38.310051 UTC**, as a 200 response. The preserved ZIP is **28,304,524 bytes**, SHA-256 `3a1e08b2276dcf0f1bdf5a7071113314776aca4660d73d0cf42fd91f92296801`. Its exact **AA77.swf** member is **5,162,821 bytes**, SHA-256 `844dfb545c8414f9e7da1edc89ffe090a09d00d721a2c65c820e15f5fe201a06`. This unit verifies the held bytes and re-decodes the member without executing Flash. No new download or repeated source query occurred. The HTML's HTTP download link and acquired HTTPS URL are recorded separately, without assuming response equivalence.\n\n[The prior WF334 review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6e9ce8fa287fa4410241bc8fba303cefd6476467/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf334-recording-lead-2026-11-02/README.md) pins the other record to [physical 68–70](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=68), production footers **000000766–768**, in a 73-page third-party public reproduction of FBI-form records. The literal name is on **physical 68, Event paragraph, footer 000000766**. PDF SHA-256: `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`. This unit reuses that full-page reading; it does not newly authenticate an FBI master or reread all 73 pages.\n\n## Exact decoded locators\n\nOffsets start at zero at the beginning of the **uncompressed AA77.swf**, including its file header. The member is **FWS**, already uncompressed. IDs are dictionary-character identifiers, not frames, people, calls or page numbers. Body lengths exclude the tag header. Text comes from glyph indices and embedded font mappings, not assumed literal ASCII substrings in the binary.\n\n| Text | Character ID | Tag offset, bytes | Body length, bytes | Font ID |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `Reuben, Todd` | 331 | 61,801 | 49 | 158 |\n| `Reuben, Todd` | 930 | 192,906 | 49 | 126 |\n| `Reuben` | 1786 | 3,576,769 | 41 | 1012 |\n| `Todd` | 1787 | 3,576,816 | 37 | 1014 |\n| `American Airlines Flight #77` | 433 | 113,604 | 81 | 126 |\n\nAll five are root-level **DefineText**, tag **11**. [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-c5c24608daa2ade6bc8d) also preserves four navigation definitions: IDs **422** (Flight 93), **427** (Flight 11), **429** (Flight 77), **431** (Flight 175), with exact glyph, offset, bounds and font locators. Their presence fits the court page's stated multi-flight scope and cautions against inferring a specific flight/call relationship from the filename alone.\n\nThe four name definitions belong to **one presentation**. They are not four independent confirmations or four calls. Independent origin of the court summary and investigative accounts is not established.\n\n## What this can test\n\nThe name similarity supplies a candidate for checking WF334's spelling and identification basis. It does **not** establish that the names identify the same person, that this person left the alleged message, that it came from Flight 77, or that it falls within the previously reviewed family-canvass scope. No court seat, native manifest row, recipient, device, carrier event or session is assigned here.\n\nThe title and names coexist in the asset; their display-list/action relationship and actual runtime display were **not** tested. Nearby unrelated personal/profile fields were not interpreted. A prosecution summary is not a native airline manifest or a judicial finding authenticating every assertion.\n\nAn inaccurate tip, clerical spelling variation, a different person, an earlier or misattributed message, and a genuine relevant message remain untested possibilities. None is selected. The original tip identification basis, contact/disposition, recording/custody, independent passenger/flight record and carrier/canvass join would discriminate between them.\n\nNothing here adds a verified canvass recipient or refutes the prior four-unknown-call attribution account. It does not establish fabricated calls, concealed evidence or coordinated wrongdoing. The prior header/receipt/event/assignment values, typed **WF334** and handwritten **WF8406** remain preserved in their original record roles.\n\n## Reproduction and limits\n\nThe earlier decoder was reused unchanged: SHA-256 `62f254468e5bbc265d3a04a44c735a09da65339c3a13e1f79046b6e503410617`. It passively re-decoded **548 text definitions**, producing exactly the same JSON-serialized result as the preserved extraction. This unit examines and publishes **nine selected definitions**, including four name definitions; it does not substantively review every name, call or screen.\n\nRun `python3 verify.py --court-zip /path/to/court-flights.zip` to verify archive/member bytes and reproduce the selected font/text records. `python3 verify.py` alone checks the published bundle. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0e6674e44ebb30da35b5) records actual runs. Reproduction using the same decoder is not independent method validation, identity authentication, audio analysis, carrier reconciliation or runtime-display verification.\n\nTwo initial local comparisons failed: numeric keys in raw Python font/tag dictionaries differ from JSON string keys; the first correction overlooked the tag dictionary. Complete JSON-serialized equality was subsequently tested. These are our comparison errors, preserved locally, **not historical source anomalies**.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3db7b4726453b89f4f74) carries forward all five tracks and 18 original requirements plus the identity/message/court-source targets. Earlier records, assessments and conflicts remain unchanged. [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5fd85ea78d777c1d187e) is the actual additive text diff against the preceding combined review. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-864996f85230cd74627f) separates completed source work from unperformed authentication. Neither this bounded check nor publication completes an original-record criterion.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 6d58b01ca5b5c1a01e7507c3f66f3805d46bc167f42b2e6af62ddc4e9ba38c81 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-25a529fdf45379b8\"></a>\n### WF334: a reported saved-message lead and an unlocated follow-up outcome\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-wf334-recording-lead-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-e2989122ba4bde8ba51a).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 25a529fdf45379b845e0d5326db14c56b546ffed321150d6696e5d271664c742 -->\n# WF334: a reported saved-message lead and an unlocated follow-up outcome\n\nA newly read intake/lead record says a masked recipient had saved an in-flight message attributed in the text to **“TODD RUBEN,”** described as a passenger on **Flight #77**. It assigns contact about the message’s contents under **WF334**. This is a concrete recording/disposition target, **not a recovered or authenticated message**.\n\nThe three pages supply no recording, completed contact report, carrier match or disposition. They do not establish another genuine Flight 77 call or a fabricated call. The reported name is preserved literally; no spelling correction, passenger-list match, recipient relationship or masked identity is supplied.\n\n## Source and actual reading\n\nThe [public mirror, physical 68–70](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=68), is an already-held reproduction of FBI-form records. The PDF has **73 pages**, **2,997,662 bytes**, SHA-256 **`e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`**; it was acquired October 27, 2026. This unit newly examined all three selected page faces on November 2. Production footers are **000000766–768**. Analyst ordinals do not purport to be printed internal page numbers.\n\nThis is a third-party public representation, not an independently authenticated agency master, complete FBI production or evidence-custody chain. [SOURCES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-45897a56e995791f8dfb) records exact access/hash/page scopes. Raw scans, images, full tip text, personal/contact/profile/signature fields and masked identities are excluded from the derivative.\n\nA source-reuse check caught an old suggestion to examine official part 01 pages 47–49: those pages were already reviewed, so that work was not repeated or counted as new. Initial thumbnail control/name associations were also wrong; the full-page reading supplies the adopted values. Our tentative readings are preserved locally as rejected processing notes, **not as alternative historical evidence**.\n\n## What the record reports and requests\n\n[Physical 68, Event paragraph](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=68), alleges an in-flight message and ends with **“SHE HAS MESSAGE SAVED.”** That records the allegation; it does not supply the device, media, content, recording time, caller identity or validation. The recipient/source fields are masked, and no relationship to the named person is inferred.\n\n[Physical 69](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=69) marks **Lead Required? YES**. [Physical 70, Set Lead 1](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=70), records **WF334**, **WFO / Washington, DC**, assignment **09/12/2001 at 7:20 AM**, and a request to contact a masked person **regarding contents of the message on an answering machine**.\n\nThat wording does not explicitly order acquisition of the recording. An assignment is distinct from actual contact, collection, authentication and a completed result. No outcome appears within these three pages; this limited scope does not establish that the FBI never followed up or that the record is absent elsewhere.\n\nThe immediate underlying targets are the original ICF and source/contact record, lead-response/interview and disposition, any original message/device or preserved copy, evidence inventory/receipt, and any transcription or analytical finding—including negative and inconclusive results. No contact or new request was made here.\n\n## Preserve the date and control fields\n\n| Source field | Printed value | Scope limit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Header, physical 68 | **12/15/2001** | Role in the create/edit/export history is unverified. |\n| Information Received, physical 68 | **09/11/2001, 7:49 PM** | An intake-receipt field; not an authenticated time the reported message was left. |\n| Event Date/Time, physical 69 | **09/11/2001 / time blank** | No message time or calibrated event clock supplied. |\n| Assignment, physical 70 | **09/12/2001, 7:20 AM** | Records an assignment label, not a verified completed action. |\n| Typed control, physical 68 and 70 | **WF334** | A source identifier, not proof of the lead’s contents or outcome. |\n| Handwritten bottom notation, physical 68 | Read as **WF8406** | Writer, date, function and any alias/cross-reference relationship remain unknown. |\n\nKeep these values side by side. No timezone, processing-delay calculation, date correction or conclusion about a post-crash call is derived. The label **PENDING** in the printed case **265A-NY-280350-WF (PENDING)** is not a verified current case status. Native ICF history and routing/assignment/receipt records would distinguish the field roles.\n\nWF334 and the handwritten notation are not counted as two independent leads. The annotation does not authenticate an alias or replacement number. Any retrieval should preserve both appearances and seek their original inventory/cross-reference relationship.\n\n## Why this matters to the call-attribution review\n\nThe previously examined [final-report note 57, printed page 455](https://www.9-11commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.pdf#page=7), reports FBI/DOJ belief that four unknown connected records concerned the Olson office. Its stated context includes family canvassing that identified May’s parents and Ted Olson as recipients. The [earlier telephone review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/639bd09f9f8116707df2be5fb04d87472afd58cb/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-originals-2026-10-27/README.md) already preserves the uncertain row-to-conversation mapping.\n\nWF334 gives a specific alleged saved-message lead whose verification and disposition can be checked against that account. **It does not by itself refute the canvass or establish an additional call.** It cannot be assigned to one of the unknown rows, to a device or to a caller/session merely from a name and flight label.\n\nIf an authenticated message and carrier/session evidence established another relevant Flight 77 recipient, the scope and attribution inference would need reassessment. An inaccurate or unrelated tip, a misattributed or earlier message, an inconclusive follow-up, and a genuine additional message remain untested possibilities. No one is selected as the explanation. The actual message, contact/disposition and full canvass scope/inclusion rules are the discriminating records.\n\nNo association to the separately reviewed operator calls is made from a similar first name or message terminology. This record’s literal name and flight description remain its own unverified allegation.\n\n## Work completed and limits\n\nThree full source faces were read; no whole 73-page census, new OCR, hidden extraction, audio/ASR, voice identification or native clock test occurred. Two exact official-domain queries returned no usable result; three held official text indexes also produced no exact locator. These bounded misses do not establish nonexistence, withholding or destruction. No recording, original lead response or disposition was acquired.\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b2b120624ec7f6422c9b) contains five related analyst entries from one intake/lead unit, not five independent confirmations. The strongest limitation is that a recorded allegation and assignment can remain inaccurate or unverified; copies and handling stages do not independently corroborate the claimed call. No fabrication, concealment, intelligence affiliation, motive or historical cause is established.\n\nAll five tracks and 18 original requirements remain open or partial. [OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-81616da7261eabc5e597) preserves them and the new WF334/message/disposition targets; earlier actual analyses remain performed. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d8327929ef8ca38afffd), [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f083af6618c766ee6a27) and [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-735d61ee86753a1c34c6) separate manual source reading and byte/navigation checks from unperformed authentication. Prior sources, reports, conflicts and history remain unchanged. Publication is not main-branch adoption, independent audit or goal completion.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 25a529fdf45379b845e0d5326db14c56b546ffed321150d6696e5d271664c742 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-ab23e621a3d48fbe\"></a>\n### WF334: static court-animation links clarify the name's presentation context\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-wf334-static-context-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-38ad439c85222d44f2dc).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY ab23e621a3d48fbeace27b2dbbca98f5f0835837fbf100798656582adbfc28d5 -->\n# WF334: static court-animation links clarify the name's presentation context\n\nThe court asset's **“Reuben, Todd”** text is explicitly referenced by a sprite instantiated as **“Names.”** That container is placed in the same authored root frame as the **American Airlines Flight #77** title. A separate **“Reuben” / “Todd”** text pair has a traceable route through a container instantiated as **“Photos,”** with a matching **Reuben** frame label.\n\nThis advances the [previous dictionary-only name check](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/926139fc0a26c869387a85030352613b8f0674d7/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf334-court-name-2026-11-02/README.md): there are actual static placement links. **It still does not authenticate WF334's reported message, establish that its “TODD RUBEN” is the same person, or prove a call or recipient.** Both spellings and all earlier uncertainties are retained. The source-to-caller join remains a TODO.\n\n## Exact structural source locators\n\nSource: [court flights ZIP](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/flights.zip), acquired **2026-10-27T13:40:38.310051+00:00**; **28,304,524 bytes**, SHA-256 `3a1e08b2276dcf0f1bdf5a7071113314776aca4660d73d0cf42fd91f92296801`. Exact member **AA77.swf**, **5,162,821 bytes**, SHA-256 `844dfb545c8414f9e7da1edc89ffe090a09d00d721a2c65c820e15f5fe201a06`. The member declares **SWF version 5**; that is a format version, not a creation date. No court archive was downloaded again.\n\nOffsets below are zero-based **tag-header bytes** in this uncompressed member, including the file header. **Local frame ordinals belong to different timelines**: they are not seconds, call times, execution order or proof of joint visibility.\n\n| Link or definition | Byte offset | Local authored frame / role |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Text ID930, `Reuben, Todd` | 192,906 | Dictionary definition |\n| Sprite985 definition, 66 frames | 198,740 | Container dictionary definition |\n| `Reuben` frame label inside sprite985 | 201,070 | Sprite985 frame46 |\n| Place text930 at depth2, flags3 | 201,090 | Sprite985 frame46; replaces the character at that depth |\n| Place sprite985, instance name `Names` | 202,128 | Root frame37 |\n| Place Flight77 title433 | 113,691 | Root frame37 |\n| Text1786 `Reuben`, text1787 `Todd` | 3,576,769 / 3,576,816 | Dictionary definitions |\n| Place text1786 and text1787 | 3,577,511 / 3,577,528 | Both sprite1788 frame29 |\n| Sprite1788 definition, 35 frames | 3,576,859 | Container dictionary definition |\n| Sprite2011 definition, 69 frames | 5,106,155 | Container dictionary definition |\n| `Reuben` frame label inside sprite2011 | 5,108,358 | Sprite2011 frame54 |\n| Place sprite1788 inside sprite2011 | 5,108,371 | Sprite2011 frame54 |\n| Place sprite2011, instance name `Photos` | 5,109,018 | Root frame37 |\n\n[OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-09bc281d8b995ebd1489) preserves **18 selected explicit placements**, relevant sprite definitions, exact flags/depths/local frames, selected instance names, prefix bytes/body hashes and the two labels. It also retains the separate name ID331 route through sprite778, instantiated as **Pointers**. Repeated references, name variants, labels and containers in this **one** asset are not independent confirmations or extra people/calls.\n\nThe [court P200054 index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) calls it a Flight77 summary and explicitly includes the other three flights. Prior saved-HTML lines **45/51/73** identify the exhibit, description and ZIP link; its SHA-256 is `866887c38f78c1f5b68ab73a695ae5345812eaf53a3e34da240f5345a1cd96c5`. The prior HTML review is reused, not counted as newly acquired evidence. Its absent access timestamp remains absent.\n\n## The conflicting records remain separate\n\nThe [public FBI-form reproduction, physical68, Event paragraph, footer000000766](https://www.les-crises.fr/wp-content/uploads/2016/06/Team7-Box13-Flight-Call-Notes-and-302s.pdf#page=68), reports literal **TODD RUBEN**, **Flight #77**, and a saved message. The prior three-page review preserves typed **WF334**, handwritten **WF8406**, header/receipt/event/assignment fields and the assigned follow-up. No spelling correction, alias selection or date reconciliation has occurred. Mirror SHA-256 remains `e3cf374351cb753d1297433f86bb5807c56cb42a6dc69837a9df02dd0d54f4aa`; this third-party reproduction is not an authenticated FBI master.\n\nThe new structural evidence supports treating the court name as a **specific Flight77-presentation candidate**, rather than relying only on a filename or global-menu text. It does **not** prove that a human actually viewed these frames, that the local child timelines were selected together, that the two source names identify one person, or that an airline manifest or caller was authenticated. The instance name **Photos** does not identify or authenticate an actual photograph; none was examined here.\n\nNo native passenger/seat/flight record, original tip identification basis, lead-response outcome, recording/custody chain, carrier event or canvass join was acquired. This cannot be counted as a verified additional message or a refutation of the prior call-attribution account. Inaccurate tips, clerical spelling differences, different people, earlier/misattributed messages and genuine relevant messages remain untested alternatives. Original identification/contact/disposition and independent carrier/media records are the discriminators. No fabrication, concealment, motive or coordinated wrongdoing is established.\n\n## Method and reproducible limits\n\nThe original passive tag/font parser is reused unchanged, SHA-256 `62f254468e5bbc265d3a04a44c735a09da65339c3a13e1f79046b6e503410617`. The added [structural reader](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0511240dd19da625a3d4) reads sprite IDs/frame counts, placement prefixes and selected frame labels. It records explicit-character references; it does not simulate actions, button behavior, clipping, transforms or move-only state. Root-frame placement is an authored structural relationship, not runtime visibility.\n\nThe field layout was checked against **Adobe's SWF v9 specification**, [printed/physical50–51](https://me3tweaks.com/guides/files/gui_editing_2/swf_file_format_spec_v9.pdf#page=50) and [243](https://me3tweaks.com/guides/files/gui_editing_2/swf_file_format_spec_v9.pdf#page=243). This later edition describes earlier placement/sprite structures. It is a **third-party mirror**; publisher-master identity was not independently authenticated. Local PDF text was read. Two web screenshot attempts failed and were not repeated; no successful visual specification check is claimed. Raw specification PDF stays outside the public payload. Access **2026-11-02T22:06:04.221958+00:00**, **2,061,625 bytes**, SHA-256 `78555c7f7cea97923445e08ddbccf36a166c0e130c2e4b2f17d68e2b953d58cb`.\n\nActual structural scope: **98 sprites**, **18,330 PlaceObject2 tags**, **3,643 explicit-character placements**, **4,282 ShowFrame tags**, **402 DoAction tags**, **253 DefineButton2 definitions**. All98 declared sprite frame counts and the root's **159** match their local ShowFrame counts. These are file-structure counts, not call counts, persons or proof percentages. Only the selected name/title/container relationships were substantively examined; this is not a complete call/roster census. Actions and buttons remain unexecuted and semantically untraced.\n\nSix fixed byte-vector controls and one truncated-input control test the new prefix reader, including ID-absent updates and replacement flags. They passed; those controls check parsing, not historical identity. [verify.py](CITATIONS.md#nov04-92d0f4b6a8aa22ec0639) reproduces the selected result from the exact held ZIP and checks published bytes, prior-review preservation and all18 TODOs. Run `python3 verify.py --court-zip /path/to/court-flights.zip`; without that argument it checks the bundle and parser controls only. [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b8e435c6c42218884b66) states the actual runs. Same-reader reproduction and internal frame consistency do not substitute for an independent runtime implementation or the original records.\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ba2af2ad524b0efcdc8f) keeps every original five-track requirement and prior WF334/serial3255/print/engineering target open. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1a3f6edb5e91a3f8c73b) and the actual additive [Git text diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-21d16c8cdab2da48e6e3) record exactly what changed; the preceding report, conflicting values and source bytes remain untouched. No original-record acceptance criterion or the whole investigation is completed by this step or publication.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY ab23e621a3d48fbeace27b2dbbca98f5f0835837fbf100798656582adbfc28d5 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-fa03c3f3f844096a\"></a>\n### Flight77 court exhibit: the zero entry's actual structural context\n\n**Source unit:** `telephone-zero-entry-context-2026-11-02` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2ed8c5691d608eb2d9a6).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY fa03c3f3f844096ab22e58272d5d8601518578029e485a57526d49525ef43cfc -->\n# Flight77 court exhibit: the zero entry's actual structural context\n\n2026-11-02. TEL01–TEL04; AUD016-A1 / TC05-B105 / TC06-B110. **New work in an already-held primary exhibit; no new source download, witness, carrier record or historical call verification.**\n\nThe original court-distributed file puts **09:18:58, “0 SECONDS ” and “DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICEUNCONNECTED CALL” in an authored structure that also contains Barbara Olson's name**. A separate structure labelled **Unknown** contains **09:14:57, “ON BUTTONPRESSED” and “UNCONNECTED CALL.”** This goes beyond the October27 text-dictionary check: the associations now have actual encoded character references, rather than just adjacent definitions. It does not prove that either event occurred as labelled, that a particular screen was displayed at trial, or that no other call reached the office.\n\n## Original and scope actually tested\n\nThe [court's P200054 exhibit page](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) describes summaries and links a [ZIP](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/flights.zip) containing all four flights. The ZIP was acquired October27,2026 at13:40:38.310051UTC, not newly downloaded here: **28,304,524bytes**, SHA-256 `3a1e08b2276dcf0f1bdf5a7071113314776aca4660d73d0cf42fd91f92296801`. Its `AA77.swf` member has **5,162,821bytes**, SHA-256 `844dfb545c8414f9e7da1edc89ffe090a09d00d721a2c65c820e15f5fe201a06`. The filename does not make every stored object Flight77-specific; the file also holds navigation and other-flight material.\n\nWe reused the static text and placement readers from the [earlier Reuben-name structural check](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2f78618d88ebcbd3e91811e9ba17f6457a6027ef/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-wf334-static-context-2026-11-02/README.md). That earlier selection did not test this zero entry. This unit selected22text IDs, their incoming explicit placement/button references and ancestor sprites. All548previously extracted text definitions reproduce unchanged. We parsed98sprite declarations and253button definitions for structure; only the selected references were substantively assessed. We did not review every stored text, execute Flash/ActionScript, simulate display state or inspect a trial recording. [Source entities and access dates](CITATIONS.md#nov04-cdf5a6b38356714ada9a) · [Selected encoded results](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f06f368e84b869f0f71a) · [Prospective scope and follow-on](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2224985b0eddc37e862a).\n\n## 1. The zero entry has an encoded association with the Olson structure\n\nAll offsets below are **zero-based bytes in the uncompressed AA77.swf**. Frame numbers are **local authored ShowFrame ordinals**, not seconds, synchronized playback or evidence of actual joint visibility.\n\n| Item | Text ID / definition offset | Actual encoded placement |\n|---|---|---|\n| Olson / Barbara |1684/3182196;1685/3182241 |sprite1704 local frame1, offsets3186267/3186303; further name definitions1689/1690 placed in that sprite at frame12, offsets3187111/3187128 |\n|09:18:58 |1691/3183776 |sprite1704 frame20, offset3193352, depth396 |\n|0 SECONDS (source has trailing space) |1692/3183822 |same sprite/frame, offset3193375, depth397 |\n|masked destination already in source |1693/3183887 |same sprite/frame, offset3193398, depth398; no masked digits reconstructed |\n|DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICEUNCONNECTED CALL |1694/3183950 |same sprite/frame, offset3193421, depth399 |\n\nSprite1704 is defined at3186221 and is placed inside sprite2011 (`Photos`) at local frame48, offset5108120. The parent has an **Olson** label at frame47, offset5108067; that preceding frame places sprite1686, not1704. Preserve that one-frame distinction: no runtime jump, sequencing, persistence or screen appearance was simulated. The shared named structure is a firmer exhibit association than dictionary proximity, but it is not carrier evidence or an authenticated human-to-network-event join.\n\n## 2. The button-pressed entry belongs to a different authored structure\n\nThe09:14:57 / ON BUTTONPRESSED / UNCONNECTED CALL text definitions are2001/5075936,2002/5075982 and2003/5076055. Their explicit placements are in sprite2010 at local frame19, offsets5105096/5105119/5105165. A button definition2009, offset5077604, also refers to all three; its over/down state flags and later placement at sprite2010 frame23 are encoded, not executed.\n\nSprite2010 is placed inside `Photos`2011 at frame69, offset5109000, alongside its **Unknown** label at5108986. That association supports retaining this as the exhibit's separate unknown/button-pressed entry. It does not identify a person, establish an additional conversation or explain why the May2004 briefing table has seven rows while its text says eight calls. The earlier eight-minute-label crosswalk already existed; it is not a new independent finding here.\n\nThe other selected unknown entry,09:25:48 /159 SECONDS, has IDs1997/1998, definition offsets5075706/5075752, and placements in sprite2010 frame10 at5103551/5103574. This source association does not settle **159 versus154seconds**.\n\n## 3. Summary counts are paired with names in actual button records\n\n| Stored pair |Text IDs |Button IDs / definition offsets |Root placement frames / offsets |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|2CALLS / RENEEMAY |2129/2130 |2134/5160536 and2139/5161492 |144/5160748 and151/5161702 |\n|1CALL / BARBARAOLSON |2136/2137 |2138/5161103 and2143/5162253 |148/5161315 and155/5162465 |\n|5CALLS / UNKNOWNCALLER |2140/2141 |2142/5161861 and2144/5162550 |152/5162087 and159/5162777 |\n\nEach name/count pair is referenced together within a button definition, including up and over/down state records. Two button definitions reuse each pair. **These repeated presentation objects are not additional call records or independent corroboration.** The3pairs also do not independently validate a census of eight attempts, completed conversations, network legs or persons. Their action bodies remain opaque and unexecuted; this test did not prove a button's interactive destination or the screen a trial viewer saw.\n\n## Conflicting records remain side by side\n\n- **Connection:** the September20,2001 *American Airlines Airphone Usage* reader pages43–44/internal1–2 reports an unnamed operator-routed caller “was subsequently connected” to the Solicitor General's Office. The May20,2004 briefing page2 and the court label classify09:18:58 as unconnected. The early report supplies no unique switch/leg join; the named caller and event cannot simply be equated. [Early report rendering](https://www.scribd.com/document/24392516/T7-B19-Key-302s-Fdr-Entire-Contents-FBI-302s) · [May briefing](https://www.scribd.com/document/18886083/T7-B12-Flight-93-Calls-General-Fdr-52004-DOJ-Briefing-on-Cell-and-Phone-Calls-From-AA-77-408).\n- **Duration/counts:**159seconds in the briefing/court versus154seconds in the [Commission final-report note57, printed455](https://www.9-11commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.pdf#page=7); eight calls in the briefing text versus seven displayed rows. Neither is resolved by tracing this exhibit. These are reused observations, not newly discovered discrepancies.\n- **Recipient accounts:**Keyton says the later call was direct, not collect; Voss believed both were collect. The official-hosted Keyton counterpart is already held at FBI September part02 physical69; Voss's previously reviewed mirror is physical51. [Official counterpart and source comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/fb0d56eeaa07cfc9348306d1cedbcbea059fc5c8/investigation/broader-evidence/fbi-keyton-acis-originals-2026-10-31/README.md). Their reports do not uniquely identify the unknown connected rows.\n- **May time descriptions:**6:05a.m.Pacific in the Dallas relay versus6:13a.m.with no printed zone in the already-held LasVegas family response remain unreconciled. [Preserved relay/response qualification](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/e451c84f5494eef39539807b9b984bdb2bcd8eec/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-may-response-qualification-2026-11-02/README.md). This unit performed no new time comparison or conversion.\n\nDifferent event/leg definitions, source versions, clerical error or mistaken reconstruction are untested possibilities; intentional manipulation is also untested. None is selected as the explanation. A zero-duration named entry cannot by itself establish that no other conversation occurred. Conversely, a named exhibit label does not authenticate that person's attempted call. The [official staff report, physical94 note265](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=94), expressly leaves which unknown records represent the two reported conversations uncertain. That qualification is material contrary evidence to an assumption of claimed complete identification.\n\n## Holdings, TODOs and test limits\n\n[HOLDINGS.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2192ac0fc151840d3d89) distinguishes held released records from missing native inputs. The zero label, Keyton released form, September20 reader rendering and May-family released response are **held components**, not wholly missing categories. The complete Request14 submission/response/release chain, native operator/carrier events, installed definitions/clocks, office routing, actual underlying recordings/notes, and unique source-to-call joins remain open. A statement that a lead was covered is not a global investigation closure. [Open dependencies](CITATIONS.md#nov04-26f6918b79f8c57a9fc0).\n\nThe mechanical checks reproduce the frozen548-definition extraction, verify ZIP/member hashes, check all98sprite frame counts, recheck43selected explicit placement prefixes directly from encoded tag fields, and validate the limited button layout controls. They do not constitute an independent historical decoder or experimental replication. Parsing all253buttons does not mean their actions or every semantic label were reviewed.\n\nThe legacy format interpretation uses Adobe-authored documentation hosted by a mirror, not an authenticated publisher master: [SWF v9 specification, printed50–51,234–237,243](https://me3tweaks.com/guides/files/gui_editing_2/swf_file_format_spec_v9.pdf). The later edition documents legacy tags; this does not certify SWF5 playback. An initial portable-check failure resulted from sorting Python numeric keys before JSON string normalization; the source and frozen expected digest were unchanged, and the corrected check passed. A failed local SOURCES.json path lookup was also our error, not missing historical evidence.\n\nRun `python3 -B verify.py --zip /path/to/court-flights.zip` to check bundle integrity and reproduce the source trace; without `--zip`, only the public bundle hashes are checked. [Actual execution result](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b1b56ad244b1ae86498d). Earlier source/research files and public history remain unchanged; [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5ef4c7d8c5c4fbaa3430) is the real additive text diff against the immediately preceding preserved combined review. No historical discrepancy was adjudicated and none of the18full goal criteria is accepted complete by this publication. Raw scans/SWF, contact/card data and private records are excluded.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY fa03c3f3f844096ab22e58272d5d8601518578029e485a57526d49525ef43cfc -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-2067d4599e340e25\"></a>\n### FAA and NMCC communications records: unresolved bridge and connection joins\n\n**Source unit:** `faa-nmcc-bridge-scope-2026-11-04` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8412481129165980c2bd).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 2067d4599e340e2585eee61f8b873b78feb6fb365f1a1e2f8978b032f785bfdf -->\n# FAA and NMCC communications records: unresolved bridge and connection joins\n\nNovember 4, 2026. **The released NMCC-related chronology supplies specific FAA references, but does not identify them as the FAA headquarters bridge or verify that a requested connection occurred.** Reading it beside the reproduced May 2003 answer exposes the precise joins still needed. It does not resolve the earlier disagreement or supply a later correction or personnel decision.\n\n## The actual records compared\n\nThe [official DOT/OIG report](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf) is **3,632,256 bytes**, SHA-256 **`8dde0e97d6e6adac23afea241cfff77c9a0fb4095087959f54874fc6640dc616`**. Appendix5 is physical page30. It reproduces FAA’s answer; it is not the native authoring file, original transmittal or receipt.\n\nThe [official NARA release, ISCAP2012-156 document21](https://www.archives.gov/files/declassification/iscap/pdf/2012-156-doc-21.pdf) is **23 pages / 1,669,674 bytes**, SHA-256 **`bf6ca550673b48850b6e863bda7f846c67aaf75091553b4b8b9a28cd4a6c0fc2`**. Its text title reads **“CHRONOLOG FOR AMERICAN BOMBINGS.”** This source was acquired by the existing NR149 study and reused here; it is one record, not a second independent corroboration. Its January21,2021 declassification notice does not authenticate its creator, creation date, underlying recording or clock.\n\nBoth complete saved entities were hash-verified before and after the selected reading. [Source/version scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-528e8cd4b5841e5ba74a) and [exact page/line pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-254fd86436f099b4299b).\n\n## Preserve the event, actor and conference fields\n\n| Source and exact text-layer locator | What it records | What remains unproved |\n|---|---|---|\n| DOTphysical30 lines12–21 | FAA’s answer describes several bridges; the Air Force liaison immediately joining the **FAA headquarters** bridge and contacting **NORAD on a separate line**. | Actual membership, connection logs and calibrated times; the reproduced claim is not independently validated here. |\n| DOTphysical30 lines23–25 | The answer attributes **9:24a.m.** formal Flight77 notification to NORAD logs, beside a claim of earlier continuous sharing. | Identity/version of those logs and the actual event/recipient join. |\n| NARAphysical2 lines25–27 | Label **111535Z SEP01**; Navy CDRGardner says FAA reported **“Fl757”** missing from **Dulles to LA**. | Direct FAA audio, a bridge identifier, an accepted flight-number identification or a link to the claimed9:24notification. Do not silently rewrite Fl757. |\n| NARAphysical15 lines11–17 | Winfield is still on an air-threat conference; **“l l 1917Z SEP01”** precedes an instruction to get FAA on a **second line**. Gardner **initiates** a call to get FAA on with the President and STRATCOM. | A completed connection, first FAA contact, Air Force liaison membership, or identity with the FAA headquarters bridge. Preserve letter-like glyphs and inaudible text. |\n| NARAphysical1 lines8–10,30–34 | Opening labels **111115EDT / l l1515Z SEP01**, plus a partial FAA reference ending **inaudible**. | Earlier coverage, recovered missing words, uninterrupted recording, a complete roster or an independently calibrated clock. |\n\nThe source records therefore contain **different reported actions and communication contexts**. A later request for a particular second line cannot establish that FAA had been absent from all earlier communications. Equally, a report attributed to FAA does not authenticate the reproduced claim that the liaison immediately joined a particular bridge and separately contacted NORAD. The required identity and source-generation joins are unknown. No preferred historical account or clock value is selected. [Typed assertion crosswalk](CITATIONS.md#nov04-34f04e468ac22a2a5ac1).\n\n## Keep the OIG findings and outcomes separate\n\n[DOTphysical9 lines17–36](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=9) distinguishes reliance on an inaccurate notification timeline from its finding that executives later learned the liaison/bridge answer was inaccurate and failed to correct it. [Physical10 lines6–31](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=10) retains differing knowledge dates, expected correction and the liaison’s contrary account. Those findings remain visible; the NMCC chronology neither validates nor erases them.\n\nRecommendations **1–2 on page12** address correcting the answer and **considering** administrative action. Recommendations **3–4 on page13** address recording preservation and response procedures. The report also retains the mitigating context of more than6,000materials supplied. A corrected answer’s delivery, signed action/no-action determination, recommendation implementation and investigation closure remain separate outcomes. None was recovered in this comparison.\n\n## Reading, tests and remaining work\n\nThis unit read **eight selected embedded-text pages**: NARA1,2,15 and DOT9,10,12,13,30. Other DOTpages were keyword-located only. No native page image, audio, new OCR, timestamp parser, clock alignment, source redownload or physical test was performed. MuPDF emitted **“No default Layer config”** while locating/reading the DOTfile; the warning is retained and no visual/layout equivalence is claimed. Exact pin and source-hash checks establish this text representation, not historical truth.\n\nThe next discriminating records are the actual bridge/line IDs and participant/connection logs, source recordings and chronology generation/custody records, independently anchored clocks, and the distinct correction/decision/follow-up records. A completed connection record could strengthen a particular join; a different channel, failed attempt or contrary source could weaken it. Neither is presumed. [Open inputs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8a83969d903766923978).\n\nAll **18 original requirements across five tracks remain open or partial**. Source reuse and this completed field comparison do not close them. Earlier sources, conflicting labels/counters and failed checks are unchanged. [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-0dec9250e20eaaaec159) appends this comparison to the immediately preceding preserved record without removing historical text. [Checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-771bbf6844907501662d) and [verification limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a201352b25401e3f135f). Only original research notes, selected released-government text, source links and hashes are published; raw PDFs/media, private correspondence, personal/contact fields, strategy, credentials and chat-coordination material are excluded.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 2067d4599e340e2585eee61f8b873b78feb6fb365f1a1e2f8978b032f785bfdf -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-a2fcc622bf233984\"></a>\n### A released NMCC account identifies concrete configuration and circulation records to pursue\n\n**Source unit:** `faa-ot2-config-scope-2026-11-04` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d3670627b05ea7dd383c).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY a2fcc622bf233984d527d2b1f1bc94fca1d3e779b3f4e7ab46cf42cf9c0569bd -->\n# A released NMCC account identifies concrete configuration and circulation records to pursue\n\nNovember 4, 2026. **The OT-2 account attributes conference problems to preset configuration, a missing FAA directory number and secure-terminal baud-rate incompatibility.** It also describes FAA requests reaching a national-level conference. Both accounts must remain visible. Neither proves a common session, an absence of all FAA communications, deliberate exclusion, or who later knew about the problems.\n\n## Actual source and scope\n\nThe [official NARA release, ISCAP2012-156 document26](https://www.archives.gov/files/declassification/iscap/pdf/2012-156-doc-26.pdf) is **1,156,759 bytes**, SHA-256 **`fa723f99b4b8bf580034d986ddf746f6c04aabb717e2aa2c58dbe3329cfdc025`**. The existing NR150 study acquired this record; this unit reuses that same entity, rather than claiming a new download or independent corroboration. The whole saved PDF hash was verified. This unit read **physical pages1,2,3,4,6 as embedded text**; no native page images, roster/contact fields, audio or hardware were examined.\n\nThe cover’s date extracts as **“4-Oct-0 l”**; its final letter-like glyph has not been visually confirmed. The companion study describes it as an October4,2001 cover; that interpretation and the literal extraction remain separate. The cover identifies NMCC/Joint Staff/OT-2 context, a Deputy Director of Operations line and two attachments. It does not establish native creation time, a physical signature, a verified addressee or receipt by any FAA executive. Do not date the entire20-page packet from this cover. [Exact source text/page/line pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-61e55e754a639492a328).\n\n## Preserve the specific, potentially different contexts\n\n| Released account / physical page and extraction lines | What it supplies | What remains unverified |\n|---|---|---|\n| **3:5–9** | “No FAA in Preset Conf”; direction to add FAA; no Red Switch FAA number available. | Which preset/version/endpoint, actual connection state and whether it describes the FAA headquarters bridge. |\n| **3:23–32** | Transition from SEC to Air Threat Conference; services dropped due to preset configuration; inability to keep FAA in a secure conference attributed to **STU-Ill baud rates**. | The service-drop and FAA-compatibility clauses are separate statements. No configuration, handshake, repair or session records were tested here. |\n| **4:51–53** | FAA passed flight-authorization requests into the national-level conference. | Source channel, session, participant and calibrated time, or how this participation relates to the preset/secure-connection account. |\n| **3:67–74** | A need to capture taskings/assignments/responses; insufficient phone/work space and phone management. | Actual subsequent equipment, recording, policy, procurement, acceptance or implementation. |\n| **6:3–15** | Integrated chronology calls itself a compilation; ATCcomments can be paraphrased and its times are described as accurate within a matter of minutes. | No numerical ±error bound, independently calibrated clock or visually verified row-colour/source assignment. This warning cannot automatically be applied to separate document21. |\n\nThese are **attributed source accounts**, not independently reproduced equipment failures. A technical configuration problem is a concrete alternative to an intentional-exclusion hypothesis, but it does not resolve every conflicting account. Conversely, later reported FAA participation does not establish that an earlier requested connection succeeded. The original source strings and unproven joins remain in [OBSERVATIONS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b49d5e03b7fd38d05cb5).\n\n## Five specific retrieval chains\n\n1. **Presets and connection events:** actual SEC/ATC rosters/configuration versions, Red Switch directory entries, and add/drop/initiation/establishment/termination records with conference and line identifiers.\n2. **Secure-terminal compatibility:** corresponding FAA/NMCC endpoint models, settings/versions, interoperability tests, handshake/fault/repair/incident records and associated call segments.\n3. **Report circulation and knowledge:** original cover/attachments and their version, approval, distribution, transmission and receipt trail. A sender/date does not prove that named FAA executives possessed this account when preparing or learning about the May2003answer.\n4. **Source generation and channel mapping:** original ATC/SEC/NOIWON recordings/logs/notes, keeper/custody/clock records and row-to-source mapping. Literal text and source roles must survive the join.\n5. **Actual implementation:** issued procedures and equipment configuration/installation/test/acceptance/follow-up records, distinguished from a stated need or recommendation.\n\n[RECORD-TARGETS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-960852dc87c089f5e379) gives each target’s exact passage, candidate office route, discriminating test and custody uncertainty. These are research targets, not submitted requests or assertions that every record existed or survives. A failed attempt, contrary configuration or documented correction could weaken a proposed link; no outcome is presumed.\n\n## The later correction question remains separate\n\nThe [reproduced May2003answer and DOT/OIG findings](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/597fb92d0d4da93fba6938452db95500ab74e76f/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-nmcc-bridge-scope-2026-11-04/README.md) remain unchanged. The QFR describes several bridges, the liaison on the FAA headquarters bridge and a separate NORAD line. DOT later distinguishes inaccurate notification information from its finding that executives learned of a liaison/bridge error and did not correct it. The military configuration account neither establishes their knowledge nor erases that noncorrection finding.\n\nDOT’s page12 recommendations to correct the answer and consider administrative action remain distinct from page13 recording/procedure recommendations. No actual corrected-answer delivery, signed consideration/action/no-action decision or recommendation disposition was obtained here. [Unchanged exact DOTpins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-7f49d90d24df1aca1537).\n\nAll **18 original requirements across five tracks remain open or partial**. This source-backed record-target refinement does not complete them. No peer timestamp/UA175/engagement analysis, new media operation, clock calibration, source signature/custody authentication or configuration experiment was performed. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-5d1b52e275f7ab24d339), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-988d16e09d4d279ee456), [verification scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-6512d93efa922a865d01), and [actual additions-only predecessor diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-2d82ba7b0c4b55e3b121). Earlier sources, conflicting values and failed checks remain preserved. Only original research notes, selected released-government text, links and hashes are published; raw PDFs/media, personal/contact fields, private correspondence, strategy, credentials and chat coordination are excluded.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY a2fcc622bf233984d527d2b1f1bc94fca1d3e779b3f4e7ab46cf42cf9c0569bd -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-681f71d3bb083652\"></a>\n### FAA contact-role and conference entries: service and timing joins remain unresolved\n\n**Source unit:** `faa-role-service-log-2026-11-04` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-aab2e7f0a1064a892562).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 681f71d3bb083652ebb9fff692d720a4e520bae3038740d802a2ebcd4c1c8ad1 -->\n# FAA contact-role and conference entries: service and timing joins remain unresolved\n\nNovember4,2026. **A released event-log copy contains an FAA point-of-contact role with a DSN-labeled field. A separate pass-down fragment records FAA initiating a hijack conference.** These are specific original-record leads. Neither establishes the availability of a RedSwitch endpoint, successful membership on a particular bridge, or knowledge of the later inaccurate answer.\n\n## Exactly what was found\n\nThe [official NARA document3](https://www.archives.gov/files/declassification/iscap/2012-156-doc-3.pdf#page=2), physical2/extractionline14, contains the literal prefix **“FAA POC”** and service label **“DSN.”** The public derivative retains those institutional labels and omits the person’s name and contact value. It is **not a verbatim quotation of the entire line**. The role label does not establish the person’s employer or assignment, or identity with an unnamed/redacted liaison in another record. [Minimized observation](CITATIONS.md#nov04-b74ca9aac8d52598c03d).\n\nThe complete released DOC3entity is **604,018bytes**, SHA-256 **`7246f587794b3fa57f5f582f65ae968610acd54e7fb674758897ebb7dbd9c4ff`**. This is a released copy containing note/chat-style material, not an authenticated native electronic export or source creation/clock history. Its field cannot simply be dated from adjacent messages or assumed available when a conference first opened.\n\nThe [official NARA document1](https://www.archives.gov/files/declassification/iscap/2012-156-doc-1.pdf#page=1), physical1/extractionlines47–54, says **“FAA INITIATES A HIJACK CONFERNCE”** and describes an air-threat conference convened at NORAD’s request. The original **CONFERNCE** spelling and extracted time glyphs **1.UOZ / 1.1:451.** remain uncorrected. No reliable clock value is assigned from them. The complete DOC1entity is **603,753bytes**, SHA-256 **`5add378cc48144943ba4293dbc1f4fc682d07d166cf70320ea4c54b7bd268560`**. It is a two-page released fragment, not proof of a complete originating log. [Exact noncontact text and source pins](CITATIONS.md#nov04-1f36de47ac309cd69819).\n\nThe existing NR151study acquired these two source entities; this unit reuses them. Two files are not automatically two independent observations. Whole-file hashes were verified without a new download, image/clock test or source alteration.\n\n## Preserve the unresolved comparison\n\nThe [OT2account](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/6d148a319c76e579b59dece22395501d66b64463/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-ot2-config-scope-2026-11-04/README.md) reports no FAA in an initial preset, no RedSwitchFAA number available, and secure-conference compatibility problems. The new role/service field remains beside those statements. **No common service, endpoint, conference, writing time or availability has been established.** The records have not been adjudicated as contradictory or reconciled.\n\nA directory/contact-role entry does not establish a completed call; conference initiation does not establish the full roster or a common FAAheadquarters/NMCC/NORADbridge. The same sources can support more than one explanation, including different sessions, timing, source generations or recording errors. Those possibilities remain untested. The contact’s identity is not used to reconstruct redactions or attribute wrongdoing. [Claim/source comparison](CITATIONS.md#nov04-067df4af4f9bf7ba0fb5).\n\nFour next chains are now specific: the entry’s original creation/version/shift/custody; duty-role and functional directory/service records; actual call/bridge/participant/configuration events; and report/QFRdistribution, correction and decision receipts. A documented later entry, inapplicable service or failed connection could weaken a proposed join. An authenticated endpoint/session/receipt could strengthen it. [Targets and tests](CITATIONS.md#nov04-3ee97fe3c16ebe3ae165). Nothing was requested or sent.\n\n## Scope, handling and remaining requirements\n\nFour operational text pages received literal FAA/F.A.A.locator searches; relevant event/role windows were inspected. A previously unread contact-only third page received **institutional/service-label presence testing only**. That limited text query does not establish a complete directory, absence of FAA, or the meanings of uninspected fields.\n\nA prototype context screen missed DSN-format contact details in a local preview. The raw preview/context file and its erroneous no-contact status flags are excluded from publication; an additive handling correction preserves the failure locally. The final public candidate was manually reviewed and tested as a fixed role/service-only derivative. **No personal name or contact value appears in this package.** No person was contacted and no identity join was attempted. [Verification scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-8f193b3997a93ab75210).\n\nThe OIG’s distinct notification and known-liaison-error/noncorrection findings remain preserved. Actual corrected-QFRdelivery, signed consideration/action/no-action and recommendation disposition remain unacquired. All **18 original requirements across five tracks remain open or partial**. Existing source values, uncertain clocks, metadata/counters and failed checks are unchanged. [TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-510de7265d61bbf4d7a4), [checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-badfb7653758f2d9801a) and [additions-only predecessor diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-de278733f159cf61aa77). Raw PDFs/media, personal/contact values, private case material/correspondence, strategy, credentials and chat coordination are not published.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 681f71d3bb083652ebb9fff692d720a4e520bae3038740d802a2ebcd4c1c8ad1 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-691486a847e5aa4e\"></a>\n### A separate FBI steel artifact and a conservation-record trail\n\n**Source unit:** `steel-fbi-conservation-2026-11-04` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-58d519731803f43ebecc).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY 691486a847e5aa4e38088c4ca7df3322291fab56f145259a43927e8d8d90c867 -->\n# A separate FBI steel artifact and a conservation-record trail\n\n**November 4, 2026.** Two institutional sources add useful original-record targets: an FBI-held commemorative steel artifact reportedly transferred in **2010**, and the museum’s described conservation documentation. Neither supplies an authenticated original recovery chain or identifies a WTC 7 scientific specimen. A large difference between two published debris totals is preserved separately.\n\nScope: **STL01–STL03, AUD011/AUD016, B188/H005**. All eighteen original five-track requirements remain open or partial. Earlier steel/telephone findings, conflicting records and missing originals remain unchanged.\n\n## What the sources establish\n\nThe FBI’s [artifact page](https://www.fbi.gov/history/artifacts/911-world-trade-center-steel-beam), web-reader lines **48 and 54**, describes a steel piece reportedly received from the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey in **2010**. Its original function is tentative: **“an elevator system or a subway rail.”** The page also describes it as coming from **“one of the eight buildings.”** These are the agency’s public descriptions, not independently authenticated origin, receipt or examination findings. No artifact identifier, accession number, original recovery marking, evidence-item number or building-specific source is supplied in the read paragraphs.\n\nThe page therefore supplies a **separate holder/transfer lead**: the FBI artifact accession/property record and Port Authority release/selection/dispatch record could identify the piece and its previous handling. A 2010 commemorative transfer is not a documented 2001 investigative seizure. Proximity on a history page to general investigation totals does not join this artifact to an original evidence item, a forensic test or a particular building. The tentative elevator/rail description must not become a confirmed structural-column or WTC 7 attribution.\n\nThe museum’s [conservation page](https://www.911memorial.org/visit/museum/collection/conservation), saved parser-text lines **82, 85 and 88**, describes outside conservators helping preserve Hangar 17 artifacts in 2002, and later work involving condition documentation and analysis. That identifies another potential records chain: object-level condition reports, treatment histories, material analyses and their associated photographs. These are **possible retrieval targets, not acquired reports**. This general page does not establish which artifacts were treated, whether a given report survives, whether a test concerned explosives, or whether the FBI piece passed through the museum. No common accession or object identity was established.\n\nThe same page, lines **90 and 92**, describes care to preserve historically significant damage and to limit treatment changes. This is relevant contrary evidence to an assumption that conservation necessarily erased damage or suppressed evidence. It is a statement of practice, not independent proof of every treatment’s compliance. Actual before/after records and dates are needed to separate recovery damage, later handling, stabilization and subsequent deterioration. No physical, chemical, fracture or temperature test was performed here.\n\n## Conflicting numerical accounts — unresolved\n\n| Source actually read | Original published value | Locator and scope |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| FBI artifact description | **“180 million tons”** | Web-reader line 54; describes debris recovered from Ground Zero. |\n| Museum [FAQ](https://911memorial.org/911-faqs) | **“1.8 million tons”** | Saved parser-text line 494; recovery-duration paragraph describes debris cleared from the site. |\n\nThe published numeric values differ by a factor of **100** if compared in the same unit. Their measurement definitions, source worksheets and intended scope have not been established. Neither value is selected or silently corrected; no cause for the difference is adjudicated. Editorial error, different source definitions and other explanations remain untested. The underlying statistics and publication/edit histories would discriminate between them.\n\nThis is a **public-description discrepancy**, not an independent debris measurement and not evidence that steel was fabricated, removed unlawfully or concealed. Its importance is lower than an authenticated specimen/transfer/testing record. It does not establish a defect in NIST’s calculations or a collapse mechanism. A total-debris figure must not be substituted for the mass of structural steel or the number of samples.\n\n## Provenance and actual reading\n\nThe FBI article was read successfully through the web reader before an ordinary anonymous downloader returned **403**. That later route was stopped. A selected-line transcription from the earlier reader result is retained locally with its own hash; **no FBI HTTP-entity hash or historical native-document authentication is claimed**. The preserved web-reader labels are representation-specific lines, not original pagination. No image or high-resolution link was followed.\n\nTwo museum HTML entities were acquired with HTTP **200**, preserved separately, and parsed to text. Relevant conservation sections and the FAQ recovery paragraph were inspected. The hashes below identify the captured representations, not native 2002/2010 documents, original wire bytes or physical objects.\n\n| Captured representation | SHA-256 |\n| --- | --- |\n| FBI selected-line transcription of the web-reader result | `6003dc5065f5ebbbb7ec34143ac82df91faac306d172c008ce66903e43b5a2c2` |\n| Museum conservation HTTP HTML entity, 80,873 bytes | `f642240183905a1a6db663daa581c364596adf64c6e4694c69b7e46afbe1566b` |\n| Museum FAQ HTTP HTML entity, 236,662 bytes | `f1b24e8dcf5ba7d7fe62a4b089f453a8aa7d860842dd75ff9747f052d5588bbe` |\n\nExact URLs, access/request dates, representations, separate parsed-text hashes and reading scopes are in [SOURCE-PINS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-79cd00fbb12997bf09f1). No linked collections policy, contract, accession file, native inventory, condition report, analysis result, image, audio or video was acquired/read. Earlier source failure and handling limits remain in the native research record. The 2012 historic-resources report was inadvertently reopened before its earlier review was recognized; it contributes no new claim here and was not downloaded again. The scoped duplication search is not a universal novelty census.\n\n## Missing records stay TODOs\n\n[OPEN-TODOS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-00eb14775ca272425b59) retains four precise next chains:\n\n1. **FBI and Port Authority:** the 2010 artifact accession/property/transfer record, original artifact ID, selection and dispatch/receipt records, recovery/marking photographs and any earlier inventory aliases. Inspect actual identifiers before proposing a specimen match.\n2. **Museum Collections/Conservation and Port Authority:** object-specific condition/treatment/analysis reports, source-image associations, original and later label versions, conservator project files and corresponding object/loan/intake records. Applicability to any selected steel piece must be demonstrated; no laboratory result is presumed.\n3. **Each relevant holder:** dated recovery, cutting, handling, cleaning, treatment, storage and transfer events with the actual item key, preserving uncertain matches and contrary records. Keep memorial preservation and forensic sampling separate.\n4. **FBI/museum publication records and original statistical source:** source worksheets, definitions and edit/version records for the two debris totals. Do not equate a corrected webpage with a changed historical specimen or laboratory result.\n\nNothing was sent, requested from a person, tested physically, deleted or overwritten. Existing FAA, telephone, recorder, materials, steel, Beverly Hills certification/attachment and native-data TODOs remain open. Publication of this review does not complete them.\n\nThe research original and redundant public derivative remain separately named. [CHECKLIST.md](CITATIONS.md#nov04-ec5646dd9f38d4f7ea96), [CLAIMS.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-d5e229bd647a1f425c1e), [VERIFICATION.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-933debb5f5cdc4569d58), [BUNDLE-HASHES.json](CITATIONS.md#nov04-924be235c666a4cb3aaa) and [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-39a9eb11e2590412b4d5) retain scope, uncertainties and an exact additions-only diff against the immediately preceding preserved combined review. No PDF/layout verification is claimed. Remote publication verification is a separate step from historical authentication.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY 691486a847e5aa4e38088c4ca7df3322291fab56f145259a43927e8d8d90c867 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<a id=\"supplement-f6b3d6eecf727938\"></a>\n### A specific photograph lead for the filmed N10-C3B marking\n\n**Source unit:** `steel-n10-c3b-catalog-2026-11-04` · [unchanged original body](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f91e206d172727501076).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Full owning report, including limits, failed checks and TODOs</summary>\n\n<!-- BEGIN REPORT BODY f6b3d6eecf727938eb856d7154f919653d46d95c5addb83fc62dedc777c62508 -->\n# A specific photograph lead for the filmed N10-C3B marking\n\nNovember 4, 2026. **A previously acquired NIST-linked archive listing names a specific photograph, [SPANDRELS N10-C3B_1.jpg](CITATIONS.md#nov04-85ffbec898dfcdeaa20a), whose filename contains the marking previously read in the steel movie.** A fresh read-only metadata response confirms the same file record. This narrows a retrieval target; no image-to-movie, building-origin or custody match has been authenticated.\n\n## What is established\n\nRow **files[805]**, zero based, of the preserved 1,000-item listing gives file ID **1BN8cuz5mbLP_zHp9EvOjBILdwIYPMsQe**, JPEG MIME type, reported size **748,330 bytes**, and object creation/modification **2019-11-26T06:03:27.620Z**. The new metadata response agrees on all seven compared fields: ID, title, type, size, URL and both dates. [Selected row](CITATIONS.md#nov04-288620abb8feda4284e5) and [current metadata](CITATIONS.md#nov04-a106176b7ae82317ca95).\n\nThe complete listing serialization is **353,962 bytes**, SHA-256 **`e1c4a3399ddb73df2022b64b14db371d0865264dd24ddb9b808516fbadb3df33`**. That hash identifies the saved listing, **not the photograph**. The image itself was neither downloaded nor viewed in this unit; its SHA-256 remains unknown. Connector metadata explicitly reports **access_not_verified**. An anonymous web-tool open did not retrieve the image-view page, and no HTTP status or access denial is invented from that tool limitation. The archive linkage is the already-documented [NIST archive page](https://www.nist.gov/world-trade-center-investigation/photos-videos-and-simulations) and its collected-steel repository; current anonymous image access remains unverified.\n\nThe [preceding movie study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/da9fd9dfb7d1af87c88143b0148914439420c4cd/investigation/broader-evidence/steel-tape2-3-source-2026-11-03/README.md) recorded **N10-C3B** at decoder-input index **8440**, reported presentation **563.229897 seconds**. Its lower **B-1/8-1** reading remains uncertain. Those are earlier qualified observations, not new image readings. The verified Intel-store guard now reports that the share is not mounted; no movie, frame, image or recovery copy was read, rerendered or repopulated.\n\n## A report locator, with its limits preserved\n\nAn exact-marking search returned a [GovInfo-hosted NCSTAR 1-3C appendices PDF](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-C13-41f9c1ed6889bdc5fd7ea98bfc31a05b/pdf/GOVPUB-C13-41f9c1ed6889bdc5fd7ea98bfc31a05b.pdf). Its **search-index excerpt**, not a newly read report face, labels an individual **“N10-C3B (WTC 1, Col.114, Fl 90)”** and supplies **Figure B-32 / printed page 392**. The parent caption separately describes **panel N-10 (A115; 89-92)**. These are separate object-scope fields; no disagreement or controlling value is inferred.\n\nThe web open reported a **38,602,567-byte** PDF beyond its retrieval limit and this unit's prospective 12 MiB acquisition cap. A proposed official text rendition was not accessible through the web tool. No report PDF, original face, photographic content or PDF hash was acquired. Therefore the WTC1/column/floor description remains an **unverified report locator**, not an accepted attribution of the filmed object. [Representation-specific pins and limits](CITATIONS.md#nov04-9a08c67f70d4fc58bb6e).\n\n## What follows, and what does not\n\nThe next discriminating work is specific: acquire the named photograph into the verified media store; read the actual Figure B-32 record; compare visible markings and geometry; then seek the underlying inventory/alias, filming, coupon, intake and transfer records. A shared string alone cannot join all three objects. Filenames, paint and published labels may descend from the same handling process, so they must not be counted as independent corroboration. A contrary image or source attribution must be retained.\n\nNo conclusion about WTC7 origin, deliberate alteration, loss, preservation adequacy, failure mechanism, suppression or intent follows. The movie's earlier **11,607 reported versus 11,606 read-packet/decoded-frame** observations remain unchanged; its planned **12-image** selection emitted **11**, and that failed acceptance check remains failed. The native MOV-table question was deferred when the store guard failed; no parser or alternate decoder test was performed.\n\nAll **18 original requirements across five tracks remain open or partial**. The FAA management-side search did not recover a corrected answer or signed disposition. Recorder/materials owner results and the independent method review were read without claiming their missing native inputs or empirical tests complete. This is progress in locating a particular source record, not completion of the original-record goal. [Open TODOs](CITATIONS.md#nov04-dfb097409167d4b4b31b).\n\nEarlier reports and conflicting values are preserved. [REVISION.diff](CITATIONS.md#nov04-f8b64d0d6a626a0bad1a) appends this record to the immediately preceding preserved combined version, removing no historical text. [Checklist](CITATIONS.md#nov04-34c6412ced6e6daa957b) and [verification scope](CITATIONS.md#nov04-508e2afdead845d46311). The public package contains original notes, links and minimized catalog metadata; no photographs, video/audio, raw source/report bodies, account details, private correspondence, litigation strategy or credentials are included.\n<!-- END REPORT BODY f6b3d6eecf727938eb856d7154f919653d46d95c5addb83fc62dedc777c62508 -->\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- END REPORT RECONCILIATION 2026-11-04 -->\n",
